PSI-10,Reports,PSI-10_Reports_TaskbookRpts.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Reports/PSI-10_Reports_TaskbookRpts.pdf,p30,2,"Task Progress: • The Requirements Definition Review (RDR) for this project was held in Cleveland during May 10 – 11, 2010. This review was successful and helped to advance synergies among the four ACME experiments. • The Science Requirements Document (SRD) for this project was extensively revised in preparation for the RDR. • The operational requirements, test matrix, and success criteria for this project were extensively revised in preparation for the RDR. These appear in the ACME science requirements document. • The presence of appreciable molecular oxygen at the location of maximum temperature has been observed and modeled in non-premixed oxygen-enhanced combustion processes. This work was published in one journal paper. This is significant for understanding soot formation in flames. • A paper considering kinetic and radiative extinction of spherical diffusion flames was prepared and submitted to a journal. This paper is important because an improved understanding of extinction can lead to improved combustor stability and efficiency. • Numerical simulations of sooting limits of spherical diffusion flames have been performed. This work has been published in one conference paper. • Two students completed their Ph.D. studies on this research. Bibliography Type: Description: (Last Updated: 02/16/2024) Articles in Peer-reviewed Journals Skeen SA, Yablonsky G, Axelbaum RL. ""Characteristics of non-premixed oxygen-enhanced combustion: II.",,False
