PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p73,1,"ACME-DEV-002 Engineering model will not be exposed to high oxygen concentrations during the course of testing and validation, so this requirement is not necessary for this build ACME-DEV-004 In order to avoid scrapping and remaking the S1101MFD2206 Zoom Lens Housing, a deviation is required to replace item C13, QTY 6, on S1101MFA2200, from NAS1101E00- 3 Screw, Machine-Flat Fillister Head .060-80 UNJF-3A x .188 Length to NAS1101E01-3 Machine-Flat Fillister Head .073-64 UNJF-3A x .188 Length on S/N 1001 and 1002. Also, Revision C of S1101MFD2206, per ACME-ECO-182, will not be incorporated on S/N 1001 and 1002. ACME-DEV-005 This deviation will enable us to use these parts for the GIU, without having to scrap and rework the Thermocouple rakes. ACME-DEV-006 This deviation enables the two brackets currently fabricated to be used for EM and flight with minimal rework. ACME-DEV-007 The NCR and Deviation allow for the use of the covers without having to refabricate parts, at a significant impact to schedule. ACME-DEV-008 To protect the expensive and delicate flow straightener from undue damage and stress from machining. ACME-DEV-009 Two assembly fasteners will not engage the locking features of their locking inserts. ACME-DEV-011 Two of the inserts on this assembly, as identified in ACME-NCR-055 and in the attached PDFs, are missing their locking features. This deviation allows for the use of item C19",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p74,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 74 Loctite on the two fasteners that no longer have their second locking feature (the first is torque) due to the faulty inserts on the subassembly parts. ACME-DEV-014 The positions of the two required thermocouples are at 5.72mm and 13.3mm, instead of the required 5 and 15mm. ACME-DEV-015 A formaldehyde = 440 nm x 100 nm (FWHM) filter will be used in place of the 450 nm bandpass filter described in the requirement. ACME-DEV-018 The required test matrix received by ZIN engineering from the ACME project scientist excluded gases required in the science requirements document. This disparity would require the engineering team to fill bottles that would not be utilized by science. ACME-DEV-020 For both S1101MFA1245 Rev.- (25mm BRE) and S1101MFA1230 Rev. A (50mm BRE_ the offset heat flux sensor position radius does not meet the requirement as stated. Actual offset heat flux sensor positions are as follows: S1101MFA1245 - 9.46mm instead of the required 10mm. S1101MFA1230 - 15.24mm instead of the required 15mm. ACME-DEV-025 The manufacturer for the Platinum wire (Goodfellow P/N PT005130) cannot meet the 5 micron requirement, and Zin does not have the capability to accurately measure the wire. The wire diameter for the 3 TFP Calibration Array Assemblies (S1101MFA1546, S1101MFA1557, S1101MFA1558) will instead be known to ±20 microns, the tolerance on the wire per the manufacturer.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p74,1,"ACME-DEV-026 For the purposes of consistency, the two TFP Arrays (Thermocouple Near Array Assembly S1101MFA1605 S/N 1002 and Thermocouple Far Array Assembly S1101MFA1609 S/N 1002) were designed identically, with two Type B thermocouples in the close positions (12 mm and 25mm for the Near, 45mm and 60mm for the Far) and two Type-K thermocouples in the other positions. Type B thermocouples have a high-tolerance range of 870-1700 C and Type K are 0-1250 C. Type B thermocouples do not work in the range of 0-100 C. The inner positions on the far rake (the 45 and 60mm positions) should have been Type K, instead of Type B. Since they are Type B, they do not meet the low end of the temperature range per the requirement. Additionally, at lower temperatures, the ±1 °C measurement also cannot be guaranteed due to the use of the Type B thermocouples. ACME-DEV-027 The 13mm and 25mm thermocouple locations on Thermocouple Near Array Assembly, S1101MFA1605, have Type B thermocouples installed, as noted by the project scientist in 3.4.4.6. Type B thermocouples do not meet the required tolerance range at the high end of the measurement range per 3.4.4.7. Standard Limit Type B thermocouples have a tolerance range of ±0.5% of measurement At the top end of the measurement range, 1700 C, that tolerance is ±8.5 C, well outside of the required ±3 C. The 45mm and 60mm positions also have Type B thermocouples installed.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p74,2,"Their disposition is discussed in ACME-DEV-026, and have the same tolerance range as the 13mm and 25mm positions. The 50mm, 100mm and 200mm positions have Type K thermocouples installed, manufactured by Marlin Mfg. The 50 and 100 mm positions have special limit tolerances, while the 200mm positions have standard limit tolerances. Per Marlin's data sheets, the tolerances on these measurements are based on the temperature measurement:",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p75,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 75 Special limits: 0 - 285 C : ± 1.1 C 285 - 1250 C: ± .4% (which at the upper range is ± 5 C) Standard limits: 0 - 285 C: : ± 2.2 C 285 - 1250 C: ± .75% (which at the upper range is ± 9.4 C) At all temperature ranges, neither the standard limit or special limit Type K thermocouple can meet the ± 1 C requirement. ACME-DEV-028 For the Static Mixer QD: The part number chosen by ACME is 941-08-2-T-04-V-D. This differs from the required part number in the -04- term, defining a 1/4"" ID hose connection, instead of 1/2"" and in the final D term, which specifies a cap. Additionally, no keying option was selected, so the YY field is blank. For the Manifold #4 (Fuel) QD: The part number chosen by ACME is 941-04-2-T-04-V-D. This differs from the requirement in the final D term, which specifies a cap. Additionally, no keying option was selected, so the YY field is blank. ACME-DEV-031 The outer diameter of the outer support tube is 28.8% of porous sphere diameter. ACME-DEV-032 The wire used on pin 57 of PPIL1-C (Assembly S1101EFA3501) is 22 not 20 AWG as the requirement states. The requirement detail was missed before the ACME harness was designed and built. The wire on PPIL-2 pin 26 (Assembly S1101DEF3500) is the correct 16 AWG size.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p75,1,"ACME-DEV-033 The Cube Assembly (13 of S1101MFA0100) and the Analog Camera Assembly ((item 52 of S1101MFA0100) are not directly bonded to the CIR structure but are bonded to chassis through their power returns to their respective single point ground locations. ACME-DEV-035 Review of the drawings shows the requirement is met in the S1101EFA0309 - CIA Signal Harness Assembly and the S1101EFA1413 - Analog Camera to Downstream Relay Harness Assembly - both of which reside in the Chamber Insert Assembly (CIA). However in the Avionics Package (AVP) for the S1101EFA3501 harness, for this short run for the CIA video (5”) and the S1101EFA3502/S1101EFA3501 harness for the Data Camera Video (14”) twisted 22 AWG - M22759/11-22 – was used. ACME-DEV-036 The E-Field Voltage Monitoring signal doesn't meet the .12% tolerance requirement referenced in the description of ISRD trace 1.7.1 below a magnitude of 3595 volts as calculations from ACME-ANA-013 illustrate In addition the signal does not meet the ""1% or 20 volt -whichever is larger"" tolerance referenced in the description of ISRD Trace 2.5.1, 2.5.4 between 80 and 20 volts. This is also illustrated in ACME-ANA-013. Using this same reasoning for the verification activity of the - Electric Potential – Accuracy requirement of section 2.51, 2.54 from the ISRD altering the above equations give: For the low side:",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p75,2,.99 * Vout < ((.999 * Vout) -.719 ) solving this gives Vout > 80 volts For the high side 1.01 * Vout > ((1.001 * Vout + .719) solving for Vout also gives Vout > 80 volts. ACME-DEV-038 The BRE Burner flux sensor position is out of the required tolerance. The tolerance is ± 0.05mm (.002 in).,,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p76,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 76 S1101MFA1230 50mm BRE Burner: Both positions are at -.012 in. S1101MFA1245 25mm BRE Burner: Center positions is at -.008 in, and the outer position is at -.014 in. ACME-DEV-039 ACME Does not use Nitrogen Bottles ACME-DEV-040 The TFP motor (S1101MFA1529 all current and subsequent serial numbers) cannot reach the minimum translation speed of 100mm/s. It also cannot achieve an uncertainty of .1mm/s from commanded to actual translation speed. ACME-DEV-041 Commercially sourced Silicon Carbide (SiC) fibers are 14 Micron diameter. There is no given tolerance band on the requirement so 14 microns is not within the requirement. ACME-DEV-046 A BG-7 Schott Glass Filter included on the ACME Data Camera Package meets all the specifications described in the requirement, except for the 1mm thickness. The BG-7 Filter that was purchased and installed has a thickness of 2mm. ACME-DEV-047 The long dimension of the FOV is not aligned with the CIR chamber axis. ACME-DEV-049 Igniter speed uncertainty was measured as being 2.54 mm/s not the required 0.1mm/s or less. ACME-DEV-050 ACME Igniter Motor testing met the first portion of the requirement but failed to retract the igniter from the ""free area"" of the ACME burner wiith in 0.5 seconds of turning off. Instead of 0.5 seconds, removal of the igniter from the free area was measured to have happened in 0.6 secs.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p76,1,ACME-WAI-012 The 9.5mm (3/8 inch) and 12.7mm (1/2 inch) burners were included in the requirements as contingencies for the 6.4mm (1/4 inch) burner. ACME-WAI-013 Only two of the originally required gas jet burner sizes are used in the required test matrix for ACME. (1.3mm and 2.1mm I.D.) ACME-WAI-016 One instance of the hall effect sensor boards (S1101EFA2216 s/n 1006) was excluded from workmanship vibration testing. ACME-WAI-019 ACME engineering will not be performing ignition reliability tests in 1g using gaseous fuels and therefore cannot meet this requirement. ACME-WAI-021 The science requirements document requires flow rates that are not being used in the flight required test matrix. ACME-WAI-022 The spherical burner positioned at 30mm upstream from the CIR window axis and the gas jet burner positioned at 30mm upstream of the CIR window axis is not needed for flight. ACME-WAI-023 The E-Field Supply Base and Downstream Relay Board Cover both impinge on the required exclusion zone.,,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p77,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 77 ACME-WAI-029 The parts were fabricated on a calibrated CNC machine, but the inspection prints were incompletely provided. ACME-WAI-030 Request a waiver of the thermal vacuum cycle test for ACME flight unit the following reasons: - The GRC testing facility was found to not be adequate due to lack of engineering best practices. - The engineering model (that is built to flight drawings) survived a mission sequence test in which it was exposed to a vacuum while operating several times, giving the engineering team high confidence that the flight unit will behave in the same manner. (ACME-RPT-008) - The flight unit has successfully passed thermal cycle testing with no adverse effects (ACME-TST-043-R1) - The thermally sensitive component (analog camera) that drove the need for vacuum thermal cycle testing is an orbital replaceable unit and can be swapped out in the unlikely event of a failure on orbit. (See ACME risk 034) ACME-WAI-034 The video circuitry utilizes a transmitter that is powered by the ACME secondary system and meets the balance signal requirement but has has a 1ohm impedance to supply ""ground"" (ie. to the system secondary single point ground) although this meets the requirement in point 2 (that it be referenced to the structure at a single point) it cannot at the same time meet the requirement to be isolated from structure (and thus single point ground) by > 6k.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p77,1,"ACME-WAI-037 A portion of the Cube Assembly case (13 of S1101MFA0100) is not directly bonded to the CIR structure but is bonded to through the primary power returns respective single point ground location at the EPCU. This bond path was tested for the < 0.1 ohm value which it did not meet, thus it does not meet the requirement of ACME-PVP-7.2.1a Part 1. ACME-WAI-042 The ACME DataCam Failed to meet the success criteria for FCF optics bench air flow testing as described in requirement 5.1.1.3.1 FCF-PLN-4149 Rev.- ACME Payload verification plan. Per ACME-ANA-005 section 3.2: The analytical required flow rate for the DataCam given it's known power draw was determined to be 1.85CFM. However, the minimum allowed flow rate to achieve a pressure drop of 0.4 inches of H2O was determined by test to be 6.08CFM. Therefore the DataCam does not meet the requirement as stated. ACME-WAI-043 The ACME AVP Failed to meet the success criteria for FCF optics bench air flow testing as described in requirement 5.1.3.1 FCF-PLN-4149 Rev.- ACME Payload verification plan. Per ACME-ANA-005 section 3.3: The analytical required flow rate for the AVP given it's known power draw was determined to be 10.78CFM. However the maximum allowed flow rate to achieve a pressure drop of 0.4 iches of H20 was determined by test to be 8.68CFM. Therefore the AVP does not meet the requirement as stated.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p77,2,"ACME-WAI-044 The Advanced Combustion Microgravity Experiment (ACME) does not meet the SSP 30237 requirements for radiated susceptibility (RS03), conducted susceptibility (CS01) and conducted emission CE(07) as documented in electromagnetic interference (EMI) test",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p78,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 78 report GRC-EMI-RPT-381. The radiated susceptibility (RS03) symptoms were higher than normal (< 10%) radiometer signal readings mostly in the horizontal polarity, between 1 and 14 GHz. The conducted susceptibility (CS01) symptoms were higher than normal deviating signal readings of the thermocouples photomultipliers and the pressure transducers, all less than +/-1% full scale. The transient of the CE07 test exceeded the limit by as much as 4V at .4ms and was within the envelope within 2ms. ACME-WAI-045 The Data Package uses external harnesses whose backshells to case or bulkhead mount resistances were required to be <2.5 milliohms. Not all the backshells get down to that value. The Results were as follows: 801-040-07M19-26SA-422B to PIPG3 Backshell 2.00 milliohms pass PCAM2 to J33 8.53 milliohms fail PCAM5 to J34 1.30 milliohms pass PCAM4 to J75 2.30 milliohms pass PCAM 1 to J36 4.60 milliohms fail PCAM3 to J76 3.24 milliohms fail ACME-WAI-048 An image was taken in order to check for reflections, using the ACME Flight Data Camera Package installed on the CIR GIU. The chamber was dark and only the ignitor, with a halogen bulb instead of the ignitor wire, was powered at a setting close to the expected max. The resulting image shows the spherical burner is in the center (it is dark but can be seen) and the bright ignitor is coming in from the left.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p78,1,"Between the 2 you can see the round reflection off the window directly opposite from the Data Camera. Note that the opposite window is the Intensified Camera view, looking at the flame from the other side. There are no other significant internal reflections from the hardware, leaving the only concern for reflections being the opposite window. Deviations and waivers which were identified by Stocker as affecting science in August 2016 are topically listed here. The degree to which the deviations and waivers were expected to positively or adversely affect the science at that time is indicated using stoplight indicators for good (G), neutral (N), cautionary (Y), or bad (R). The issue of back-reflection from opposed windows noted in regard to ACME-WAI-048 was subsequently addressed with the addition of internal window covers shown in the figures in section 3.C Optical Layout. Meanwhile, ignition concerns associated with ACME-WAI-019 were partially mitigated by the development of a second type of hot-wire igniter tip, specifically with a spring-like coil design.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p78,2,"Ambient environment (Y) ACME-WAI-023 – impingement of hardware by up to 8 mm into exclusion zone BRE burners (Y) ACME-DEV-014 – minor offset in thermocouple positions (Y) ACME-DEV-020 and ACME-DEV-038 – minor recessed position of the heat flux gages (i.e., where the gages aren’t flush with the outlet plate surface) DataCam diagnostics (Y) ACME-DEV-015 – formaldehyde instead of 450-nm bandpass filter (Y) ACME-DEV-025 – ±20 instead of ±5 micron uncertainty in platinum wire diameter (for absolute light calibration) (G) ACME-DEV-041 – SiC fibers have 14 instead of 15 micron diameters",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p79,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 79 (R) ACME-DEV-046 – blue-green BG7 filter is 2 instead of 1 mm thick adversely affecting the transmission and thus the quantitative determination of temperature, soot volume fraction, and CH* concentrations (R) ACME-DEV-047 – camera is not on its side with its long dimension along flame (chamber) axis (R) ACME-WAI-048 – back reflection from opposite window Electric field (Y) ACME-DEV-036 – voltage uncertainty greater than specified (Y) ACME-WAI-044 – high susceptibility of radiometer, thermocouple, and pressure measurements to EMI, and high conducted transient emissions (relative to FCF specifications) Gas-jet burners (E-FIELD Flames only) (N) ACME-WAI-013 – 2 instead of 7 burner sizes, i.e., matching ops plan Ignition (R) ACME-WAI-019 - no 1g testing (Y) ACME-DEV-040, ACME-DEV-049, and ACME-DEV-050 – motion is slower than specified (e.g., retracts in 0.6 instead of 0.5 s) and there is greater than specified uncertainty in the speed Operations (N) ACME-DEV-018 – exclusion of specified gas bottles not used in ops plan (N) ACME-WAI-021 – exclusion of flow ranges, i.e., mass flow controllers, not used in ops plan Spherical burners (N) ACME-WAI-012 – 1 instead of 3 burner sizes (i.e., just ¼” spheres) (N) ACME-WAI-022 – center sphere position only (i.e., no offset burner option for large flames) (Y) ACME-DEV-031 – tube O.D.",,False
PSI-10,Engineering Documents,PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Engineering Documents/PSI-10_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p79,1,"of 28.8% instead of ≤25% of the sphere diameter Thermocouple rake measurements (spherical flames only) (Y) ACME-DEV-026 – type B instead of K thermocouples for 45 and 60-mm positions (Y) ACME-DEV-027 – greater than specified measurement uncertainty 5. Drawings An extensive list of drawings associated with the ACME project is included in this section, where only a portion of these drawings is available through the Physical Sciences Informatics Systems (PSI) website, http://psi.nasa.gov/. They are organized by category as can be seen in the Table of Contents, where the most important for interpreting the experimental data are likely the burner drawings in section F. Note that drawings for the Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR), the facility in which ACME was implemented, are not listed here. Meanwhile, many photographs of the hardware are available at www.flickr.com/photos/space-flames. Additional photographs can be found at other websites, such as www.facebook.com/space.flames. While neither of those sites are specifically focused on ACME, they are both administered by Dennis Stocker, the ACME Project Scientist. A. Top Level Assembly S1101MFB0001 ACME Flight Drawing Tree S1101MFS0002 ACME Pneumatic Schematic S1101MFA0003 ACME Chamber Insert Assembly On-Orbit Configuration S1101MFS0004 ACME / CIR Integrated Pneumatic Schematic S1101MFA0100 ACME Chamber Insert Assembly Launch Configuration S1101MFT0101 Generic IMS Label",,False
