PSI-10,Raw Data,PSI-10_Raw Data_21301 test sheets.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Raw Data/PSI-10_Raw Data_21301 test sheets.pdf,p1,0,"ACME / Flame Design (normal-flame TFP calibration day) - Science Test Sheet Test date: Oct. 28, 2021 Local time: 10:54 GMT: 21 301 14:54 ACME test #: 21301A1 Test of day #: 1 Flame of day #: 1 Rack Officer (RO): [name omitted] DMO (CIR): [name omitted] PD (ACME): [name omitted] Researcher: [name omitted] TEST CONDITIONS Control?: fully automated Test type?: standard, other — TFP Oxygen conc.: 40 % (vol, nominal) Oxygen conc.: 39.41 % (vol, per calc) Chamber pressure: 13.7 psia (per FCU) Vent before?: yes, to 0.2 psia 'Air' added?: yes, to 13.7 psia Also just before?: not marked Fuel bottle (next row): C3H8 100% (printed, box pre-marked) Burner fuel conc.: ? % (volume) — note: * (see general comments) Fuel flow rate: 0.105 slpm (N2 basis) N2 flow rate: [label struck through] 0 > slpm — note: no N2 INSTRUMENTATION TFP?: fixed Gain: 0 DataCam, 21 ops camera DataCam: marked; filter? clear; ROI? full; fps: Intensified: marked; filter? CH*; ROI? full; 23 fps HiBMs: [struck through]; backlight filter? yes CIR backlight?: no fps?: [struck through] — note: no HiBMs FLAME BEHAVIOR Flame hot: marked Flame (hole/opening / partially detached): not marked Flame (oscillating / unsteady / ___): third box marked, written: quasi-steady Out: temp. limit Ignited?: yes Soot@ignition: lots Soot@middle: none Soot@end: none POST-TEST CONDITIONS Oxygen conc.: 39.00 % (vol, per calc) Valve safety timer: 351 sec Chamber pressure: 13.7 psia (per FCU) Oxidizer bottle pressure:",,True
PSI-10,Raw Data,PSI-10_Raw Data_21301 test sheets.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-10/Raw Data/PSI-10_Raw Data_21301 test sheets.pdf,p1,1,"1237 psia Fuel bottle pressure: 41 psia GENERAL COMMENTS - hot glowing burner thermocouple lead * While a 100% propane bottle was used on this test day, the fuel line [overwritten: had] had 30% propane (balance N2) before this and wasn't flushed with the pure propane because of the limited bottle pressure. Therefore the concentration reaching the burner increased over time and presumably test to test, at least initially. Form date: 24 March 2021",,True
