PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,p16,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration www.nasa.gov • Delivers 3 gases from CIR to the chamber or burner • fuel (2 slpm max in N2 basis) • oxygen/inert mix or diluent (e.g., He or CO2) • nitrogen (from ISS) • Mass flow controllers (crew swappable to vary flow ranges) Gas Flow System Background > Science > Hardware > Status",,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,p17,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration www.nasa.gov Burners & Igniter • Four types of burners are planned for the first 5 experiments: • gas-jet burners 0.4, 0.8, 1.3, 1.6, 2.1, 2.7 and 3.2 mm ID • spherical burners 0.25, 0.375, 0.5 inch diameter, porous sintered metal • coflow burner 2.1-mm ID inner tube, 25-mm ID outer tube • BRE burners 2.5, 5 cm diameter, porous (with heat flux transducers) • Thermocouple for surface temperature on most burners • Burners will be electrically isolated • Hot-wire igniter, retracting, similar to that in use for MDCA • Igniter tips are replaceable, e.g., to match the burner type/size gas-jet burner spherical burner Igniter, hot-wire, retracting Background > Science > Hardware > Status BRE burner coflow burner",,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,p18,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration www.nasa.gov Electric Field • ±10kV at copper mesh above (i.e., downstream of) isolated burner • Ion current through flame is determined from Ohm’s law (I=V/R) and a measurement of the voltage difference across a shunt resistor (in series with the flame) • copper mesh screen (removable) • high-voltage source (removable) • passive electronics (fixed) H.V. Chamber Nozzle Mesh electrode Shunt for current measurement, Rs Low voltage input, e.g., 0-24VDC Gas supply tubes Insulator Coflow burner with flame Electrode mesh Background > Science > Hardware > Status",,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,p19,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration www.nasa.gov 19 Basic Imaging • Color Imaging for Ops – Analog color camera (removable) with a 45-degree turning mirror – LEDs for optional illumination • Color Imaging for Data – Gig-E color camera, 1.4 megapixel, 12 bit, 30 fps with motorized control of both zoom & iris – 3 optional filters including a blue-green BG-7 filter (to balance light intensity for pyrometry), 430 and 450-nm for CH* (incl. soot subtraction) • Ultraviolet (UV) Imaging – Existing LLL-UV camera equipped with a 310-nm filter for imaging OH* – Field of view (FOV) options: 50-mm and 80-mm diameter Background > Science > Hardware > Status Color Camera Motorized Zoom Lens Electronics Enclosure 45° Fold Mirror Filters (swap via rotating barrel)",,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_ACME_ASGSR_20131107.pdf,p20,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration www.nasa.gov 20 Advanced Imaging • Pyrometry for Hot Sooty and Soot-Free Regions – Determine temperature distribution from broadband thermal radiation using an existing HiBMs camera with liquid- crystal tunable filter – Thin-Filament Pyrometry (TFP) to determine temperature profiles from the broadband thermal radiation, where the spectrum is indicative of the fiber temperature. Array of 15-micron oxidized SiC fibers stretched across the flame with motor to allow for scanning or removal of the fibers from the flame. – Field of view (FOV) options: 30-mm and 50-mm diameter • Soot Volume Fraction – Existing CIR illumination package (based on 653-nm laser diode) and a second HiBMs camera – Field of view (FOV) options: 30-mm, 50- mm, and 90-mm diameter TFP Soot vol. fraction HiBMs camera Soot pyrometry Background > Science > Hardware > Status",,False
