PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,p2,0,National Aeronautics and Space Administration Outline • Background – Why combustion? – ISS research • ACME – Science Science – Hardware – Status • SLICE SLICE • Questions www.nasa.gov 2,,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,p3,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration Why Study Combustion? yy • Energy – While we might associate fire with the Stone Age, we still make extensive use of combustion in our daily lives extensive use of combustion in our daily lives. • Electricity – about 70% in the U.S. from combustion • Heating of buildings, water, food, and in manufacturing processes • Transportation – Our reliance on imported fuel contributes to our national trade deficit and affects our national security. • Environment Combustion is a major source of greenhouse gases – Combustion is a major source of greenhouse gases. – Soot contributes to global warming and is a health problem. • Fire Safety Given its pervasive use with annual U.S. fuel costs on the order of a trillion dollars even small improvements in combustion technology can significantly reduce fuel needs and ll i d i ! www.nasa.gov pollution production! 3",,False
PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,p4,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration ISS Combustion Experiments p • Flame Extinguishment (FLEX) – Combustion of a single liquid droplet gq p • Idealized spherically symmetric combustion greatly facilitates computational and theoretical analysis – Initial tests on efficacy of fire suppressants in ypp microgravity, followed by fundamental science – Operating since early 2009 in the Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) g() • Smoke Point In Coflow Experiment (SPICE) – Laminar gas-jet diffusion flame in coflow of air St d i t ti t id ti d h t – Studying soot generation, soot oxidation, and heat transfer in microgravity flames – Conducted in spring 2009 in the Microgravity Science Gl b (MSG) www.nasa.gov 4 Glovebox (MSG)",,False
