PSI-23,Presentations,PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Presentations/PSI-23_Presentations_AIAA presentation - ACME on the ISS Jan2012.pdf,p20,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration Burners & Igniter g • Four types of burners are planned: • gas-jet burners 0.4, 0.8, 1.3, 1.6, 2.1, 2.7 and 3.2 mm ID • spherical burners 0.25, 0.375, 0.5 inch, porous • flat-plate burner 4-cm diameter, porous • coflow burner 2.1-mm ID inner tube, 25-mm ID outer tube • Thermocouple for surface temperature on most burners • Burners will be electrically isolated • Hot-wire igniter, retracting, similar to that already in use for MDCA • Igniter tips are replaceable, e.g., to match the burner type/size Honeycomb Igniter, hot-wire, retracting www.nasa.gov gas-jet burner coflow burner spherical burner",,False
