PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p1,0,"1 2017-FEB-17 ACME Non-Imaging Data Notes compiled by Dennis Stocker, 216-433-2166, dennis.p.stocker@nasa.gov The raw non-imaging data will be made available in a spreadsheet format, specifically in a csv format, i.e., with comma-separated values, which can be opened by software such as Microsoft Excel. The first row of the spreadsheet includes the experiment configuration … where this is an example from a ground test (presented here in 3 columns rather than 1 long row) 2016-12-19 354 19:17:01:028 Experiment: 1 Test Point: Req1.7.9.1_Neg MFCA1 Gas: 0 MFCA1 Full Scale: 20.000000 MFCA2 Gas: 0 MFCA2 Full Scale: 5.000000 MFCA3 Gas: 0 MFCA3 Full Scale: 2.000000 EField: 1 EFieldPol: 1 Igniter: 0 Burner: 4 Thermocouple: 0 Radiometer: 0 IPSU 1: 0 IPSU 2: 0 IPSU 3: 0 IPSU 4: 0 IPSU 5: 1 IPSU 6: 0 PMT 1 Gain: 0.000000 PMT 2 Gain: 0.000000 PMT 3 Gain: 0.000000 The second row has these column headings for the data (again shown here in 3 columns rather than a long row) … where this example shows standard headings (where there are variants, e.g., for BRE measurements) Time MFCA1StaticMixerFlow MFCA2BypassFlow MFCA3FuelFlow IonCurrent PTA1 PTA2 PTA3 EfieldVoltage PMT1 PMT2 PMT3 TCA TCB TCC TCD TC200A TC200B TCBurner Radiometer+60 Radiometer+60CJ Radiometer+30 Radiometer+30CJ RadiometerCenter RadiometerCenterCJ Radiometer-30 Radiometer-30CJ Radiometer-60 Radiometer-60CJ RadiometerOffset RadiometerOffsetCJ TCE Ch20 Ch21 TCCJ EfieldSetpointOut",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p2,0,"2 The data is generally explained through 2 excerpts from the Software IDD, i.e., Software Interface Design Description, ACME-DOC-010 Rev C (August 2016) 8. Output Files 4. Internal Interfaces (which includes Tables 15-17*) *where Table 17 describes channels A0-4 of the DNx-AO-333 analog output board as discussed in 8.1 below. 8.0 Output FILES 8.1 Data Output File Data output files are created using the SystemOpenTestPoint command which creates a file named and stored at /payload/sci/testpointName_x/testpointName_x_data.csv, where testpointName is the parameter received in the SystemOpenTestPoint command and _x is optional to avoid duplicate files, where x = 1,2,3, etc. The file contains a two-line header. The first line has the date and time, documentation of the setup received in a SystemDefineSetup command, and the PMT gains. The second line has the column headings for the subsequent rows of data. The text of the column headings is defined by the Diagnostics/Header registry entry or the Diagnostics/BreHeader entry depending on whether the SystemDefineSetup command experimentType parameter was BRE or not. The column headings should match the data which is the following: - A timestamp in the format HH:MM:SS:mmm, where mmm is milliseconds. - 11 channels of analog input from the cube DNx-AI-207 board in the order shown in Table 1. - 25 channels of analog input from the cube DNx-AI-225 board in the order shown in Table 2.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p2,1,"(The names of many of these values change depending on whether it is a BRE test or not, hence the two options for header.) - Channel AO-4 of the DNx-AO-333 analog output board. This is the E-Field control voltage. Rows of comma-separated data is added to the file between DataRecordingStart and DataRecordingStop commands at a rate defined by the Diagnostics/SampleTimeMsec registry entry, see Error! Reference source not found., defaulting to 8 msec for 125 Hz sampling.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p3,0,"3 8.2 Message Log File Software messages are logged to files named and stored at /payload/logs/YYYY-MM-DD_hh-mmACME.log, where YYYY is year, MM is month, DD is day of month, hh is hour, and mm is minutes. The date in the name is when the log file is created, soon after software startup. Each message line in the file begins with a timestamp and a logging category. The timestamp is of the format YYYY-MM- DD DDD hh:mm:ss:mmm, where DDD is day of the year, mmm is milliseconds, and the rest are self-explanatory. See section Error! Reference source not found. for information about the logging category and how to filter them out if desired. 8.3 Command Log File The message log file, section 8.2, includes messages showing commands received and their parameters. Command log files contain only the details of each command received. The files are named and stored at /payload/logs/YYYY-MM- DD_hh-mmACMECommands.log. The format is for each command received a timestamped line of text with the command name followed by timestamped lines of text showing each parameter name and parameter value, including header information.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p4,0,"4 4.0 INTERNAL INTERFACES 4.1 DNx-AI-207 Board This analog input layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 16 differential input channels with an input range of +/-10 Volts and 18-bit resolution. Several gains are available but ACME is using a gain of 1. Table 1 DNx-AI-207 Board Signals DNx-AI-207 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-0 MFCA1_FLOW MFCA1 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA1_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA1_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-1 MFCA2_FLOW MFCA2 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Nitrogen bypass/inert mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA2_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-2 MFCA3_FLOW MFCA3 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Fuel mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA2_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D- 302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-3 ION_CURRENT Ion Current -1.5 to 1.5V Measurement of ion current between E-Field grid and burner. Ion Current (A) = Voltage/(Rsense + RDA), where Rsense is resistance of shunt resistor and RDA is the data acquisition resistance. -25 to 25 µA..",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p5,0,"5 DNx-AI-207 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-4 PTA1_OUT PTA1 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Outer Coflow pressure. Converted in flight software to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B- /CM1/ATR. AIN-5 PTA2_OUT PTA2 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Inner Coflow/Burner pressure. Converted in flight software to to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33- 10B-/CM1/ATR. AIN-6 PTA3_OUT PTA3 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Chamber pressure. Converted in flight software to to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B- /CM1/ATR. AIN-7 HV_OUT E-Field Voltage -4 to 4 V Indirect measurement of E-Field high voltage supply. -10000 to +10000 V. E-Field (V) = Voltage * 2486.1795 + 141.9733. (Emperical equation). AIN-8 PMT1_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 1 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT1_GAIN, Table 3. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10- MOD2. Looks through a 310 nm bandpass interference filter AIN-9 PMT2_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 2 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT2_GAIN, Table 3. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10- MOD2. Looks through a UV neutral density filter Broadband with a UV-grade fused silica glass window and a neutral density coating. [Stocker clarification]",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p6,0,"6 DNx-AI-207 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-10 PMT3_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 3 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT3_GAIN, Table 3. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10- MOD2. Looks through a 430 nm bandpass interference filter. 4.2 DNx-AI-225 Board This analog input layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 25 differential input channels with an input range of +/-1.25 Volts and 24-bit resolution. ° Table 2 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-0 TC_A Rake Thermocouple A -6.45 to 55 mV Near or far array Rake A Type K thermocouple, -200 to 1250 C. BRE_CTR_180 BRE BRE Center 180 -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Center 180 (South) Type K thermocouple, 0 to 500 C. AIN-1 TC_B Rake Thermocouple B 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake B Type B thermocouple, 0 to 1700 C. BRE_OFF_180 BRE BRE Offset 180 -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Offset 180 (Far South) Type K thermocouple, 0 to 500 C. AIN-2 TC_C Rake Thermocouple C 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake C Type B thermocouple, 0 to 1700 C.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p7,0,"7 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion BRE_CTR BRE BRE Center -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Center Type K thermocouple on Medtherm 8-2.688- 10SB-0-0-36-21427KSA. AIN-3 TC_D Rake Thermocouple D 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake D Type K thermocouple, -200 to 1250 C. BRE_OFF BRE BRE Offset -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Offset Type K thermocouple on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB- 0-0-36-21427KSA. AIN-4 TC_200A 200mm Thermocouple A -6.45 to 55 mV Igniter side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. -200 to 1250 C. AIN-5 TC_200B 200mm Thermocouple B -6.45 to 55 mV Relay side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. -200 to 1250 C. AIN-6 TC_BNR Burner Thermocouple -6.45 to 55 mV Type K thermocouple on burner. -200 to 1250 C. Not valid when BRE burner is installed. AIN-7 RA+60 Radiometer +60 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is Dexter Research Center (DRC) XP-0055. BRE_OFF+60 BRE +60 BRE Offset 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP-0249. AIN-8 RA+60_CJ Radiometer +60 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF+60CJ BRE +60 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-9 RA+30 Radiometer +30 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP-0055.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p8,0,"8 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion BRE_OFF+30 BRE +30 BRE Offset 0 to 2.5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP-0249. AIN-10 RA+30_CJ Radiometer +30 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF+30CJ BRE +30 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-11 RA_CTR Radiometer Center 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 500. Device is DRC XP-0156. BRE_OFF-10 BRE -10 BRE Offset 0 to 2.5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP-0249. AIN-12 RA_CTR_CJ Radiometer Center Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF-10CJ BRE -10 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-13 RA-30 Radiometer -30 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP-0055. AIN-14 RA-30_CJ Radiometer -30 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. AIN-15 RA-60 Radiometer -60 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP-0055. AIN-16 RA-60_CJ Radiometer -60 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p9,0,"9 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-17 RA_OFF Radiometer Offset 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP-0869. This is located on the downstream relay board. AIN-18 RA_OFF_CJ Radiometer Offset Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is Texas Instruments LM20. AIN-19 TC_SPARE Spare Thermocouple N/A To use, an additional thermocouple would need to be hard wired to the Cold Junction Compensation Assembly. This is located on the downstream relay board. AIN-20 BRE_FLUX_CTR BRE BRE Heat Flux Sensor - Center 0 to 1.25 V Heat flux sensor output on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36- 21427KSA. Valid only with BRE burner installed. 1mV = 1 Btu/ft2 AIN-21 BRE_FLUX_OFF BRE BRE Heat Flux Sensor - Offset 0 to 1.25 V Heat flux sensor output on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36- 21427KSA. Valid only with BRE burner installed. 1mV = 1 Btu/ft2 AIN-22 N/A Not Used N/A N/A AIN-23 N/A Not Used N/A N/A AIN-24 TC_CJ Thermocouple Cold Junction 0.803 to 1.10 V Temperature on the Cold Junction Compensation Assembly. 0 to 100 C. Device is Analog Devices AD590. Temperature (Celcius) = (Voltage/0.00295) – 273.15. BRE Valid when the BRE burner is installed. 4.3 DNx-AO-333 Board This analog output layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 32 channels with an output range of +/-10 Volts and 16-bit resolution.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p10,0,"10 Table 3 DNx-AO-333 Board DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-0 MFCA1_CTRL MFCA1 Control 0 to 5 V Static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA1_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA1_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA1_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 4. AO-1 MFCA2_CTRL MFCA2 Control 0 to 5 V Nitrogen bypass/inert mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA2_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA2_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 4. AO-2 MFCA3_CTRL MFCA3 Control 0 to 5 V Fuel mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA3_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA3_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA3_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 4. AO-3 PMT_PWR PMT Power 0 or 5 V Power to three photomultipler tubes. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-4 HV_CTRL E-Field HV Control 0 to 10 V Sets E-field HV supply output between about -10000 and 10000 V. EField See EFieldSetVoltage command, section Error! Reference source not found., for equation.. AO-5 HV_EN E-Field HV Enable 0 or 5 V E-Field high voltage supply enable. 0 V = disabled, 5 V = enabled AO-6 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p11,0,"11 DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-7 IGN_EN Igniter Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disabled. 5 V enabled. Software sets IGN_CTRL then pulses IGN_EN. AO-8 IGN_CTRL Igniter Control -0.6 to +0.8V Sets voltage at the igniter between 0.46 to 12 V. AO-9 MFCA1_PWR MFCA1 Power 0 or 5 V Power to static mixer/oxygen MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered. AO-10 MFCA2_PWR MFCA2 Power 0 or 5 V Power to nitrogen bypass/inert MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered. AO-11 MFCA3_PWR MFCA3 Power 0 or 5 V Power to fuel MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered. AO-12 RB_UP_EN Relay Board Upstream Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disables signals. 5 V = state of signal output depends on signal value. Applicable signals: SV1, SV2, SV3, SV4, SV5, SV6, SV7, SV8, SV9, PMT_PWR, MFCA1_PWR, MFCA2_PWR, MFCA3_PWR AO-13 TFP_MOTOR_RST TFP Motor Reset 0 or 5 V 0 V to rest TFP stepper motor. 5 V to enable motor. AO-14 IGN_MOTOR_RST Igniter Motor Reset 0 or 5 V 0 V to reset igniter stepper motor. 5 V to enable motor. AO-15 SVA4 Solenoid Valve A4 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-16 SVA5 Solenoid Valve A5 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-17 SVA6 Solenoid Valve A6 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p12,0,"12 DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-18 SVA7 Solenoid Valve A7 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-19 SVA8 Solenoid Valve A8 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-20 SVA9 Solenoid Valve A9 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-21 SVA1 Solenoid Valve A1 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-22 SVA2 Solenoid Valve A2 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-23 SVA3 Solenoid Valve A3 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-24 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A AO-25 PMT1_GAIN PMT1 Gain 4.63 to 10 V For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. AO-26 PMT2_GAIN PMT2 Gain 4.63 to 10 V For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p13,0,"13 DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-27 PMT3_GAIN PMT3 Gain 4.63 to 10 For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. AO-28 LED_SIDE LED Side Bank 0 or 5 V Bank of 3 white LEDs to side of analog camera turning mirror. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-29 LED_END LED End Bank 0 or 5 V Bank of 3 white LEDs past the end of the analog camera turning mirror. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-30 RB_DOWN_EN Relay Board Downstream Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disables signals. 5 V = state of signal output depends on signal value. Applicable signals: HV1, HV2, LED1, LED2, TFP_RST, IGN_RST, IGN_EN AO-31 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p14,0,"14 4.4 Serial Communication Table 4 Serial Communication Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description Lippert SBC /dev/ttyS0 MFCA1_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.5, 20 SLPM. Full scale flow of static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA2_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1, 0.5, 2, 5 SLPM. Full scale flow of nitrogen bypass/Inert mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA3_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5, 1 SLPM. Full scale flow of fuel mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA1_STATE 0-10. See Error! Reference source not found.. State of the oxygen/static mixer mass flow controller. Result of a MS (get state) command. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA2_STATE 0-10. See Error! Reference source not found.. State of the nitrogen bypass mass flow controller. Result of a MS (get state) command.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p15,0,"15 Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA3_STATE 0-10. See Error! Reference source not found.. State of the fuel mass flow controller. Result of an MS (get state) command. ConnectTech serial card P5 /dev/CTI4 CUBE_SERIAL See DNA-PPCx-1G PowerDNA Gigabit Ethernet I/O Cube User Manual. UEI cube serial connection. Can be used to retrieve version numbers, set IP addresses, and update firmware. ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_AGC_MODE On or Off. Turn automatic gain control on or off ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_GAIN 6, 12, 21, and 31 dB. Set the automatic gain control gain. ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_SHUTTER 1/60, 1/100, 1/250, 1/500, 1/1000, 1/2000, 1/4000, 1/10000, 1/20000, 1/30000 seconds. Set the shutter speed. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 IGN_MOTOR_SET_POS In counts. 0 is the retracted position. Maximum extended position depends on registry values Igniter/IgniterLimits and Igniter/IgniterMaxCount and the burner type last specified by a System Define Setup command. Default maximum is 2500 counts. Axis 1 control of motion control board in AVP controlling igniter motor in CIA.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p16,0,16 Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 IGN_MOTOR_GET_POS See Signal Range for IGN_MOTION_SET_POS Axis 1 position reporting of motion control board in AVP controlling igniter motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 TFP_ MOTOR _SET_POS In counts. 0=retracted. Maximum=closer to burner. Maximum depends on burner type and registry values TfpMaxCount and TfpToBurnerOffsets. See Set TFP Position command for calculation of maximum. Axis 2 control of motion control board in AVP controlling TFP (thin filament pyrometry array) motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 TFP_ MOTOR _GET_POS See Signal Range for TFP_MOTION_SET_POS Axis 2 position reporting of motion control board in AVP controlling TFP motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 ZOOM_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-85000 counts. 0 is zoomed out. 85000 is zoomed in. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 1 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 ZOOM_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-85000 counts. 0 is zoomed out. 85000 is zoomed in. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 1 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package.,,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p17,0,"17 Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 IRIS_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-76000 counts. 0 is open. 76000 is closed. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 2 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 IRIS_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-76000 counts. 0 is open. 76000 is closed. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 2 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FOCUS_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-101000 counts. 0 is near focus. 101000 is far focus. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 3 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FOCUS_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-101000 counts. 0 is near focus. 101000 is far focus. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 3 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FILTER_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-451000 counts. Filters at 0, 120000, 240000, and 360000 counts. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 4 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FILTER_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-451000 counts. Filters at 0, 120000, 240000, and 360000 counts.",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p17,1,Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 4 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package.,,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME non-imaging data file description.pdf,p18,0,"18 4.5 Internal Ethernet Interfaces See also Error! Reference source not found., External Ethernet Interfaces where the interface to the IOP is listed. The ‘Kernels’ string points to a hardware ethernet interface on the processor. It is used in /etc/udev/rules.d/90-net.rules to ensure that the device name is always assigned to the same connector. Table 5 Internal Ethernet Interfaces Source Device Name IP Address Net Mask Kernels Description Lippert SBC eth1 [ip removed] 255.255.0.0 0000:06:00. 0 Interface to data camera when connected directly to ACME and not IPSU-G. Lippert SBC eth2 [ip removed] 255.255.255.0 0000:08:00. 0 Interface to UEI Cube. ACME Camera Package DeviceIPAddres s [ip removed] 255.255.0.0 Camera IP address. Changeable using the CLIpConfig command line utility included in ACME software install. UEI Cube ip2 [ip removed] 2 255.255.255.0 Cube main ethernet port. Labeled NIC1. (yes, for ip2) UEI Cube ip [ip removed] 255.255.255.0 Cube secondary/diagnostic ethernet port. Labeled NIC2. NOT CONNECTED.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p1,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments (ACME) Software Interface Design Description Prepared For: National Aeronautics and Space Administration John H. Glenn Research Center at Lewis Field Space Operations Project [address removed] Prepared By: ZIN Technologies, Incorporated [address removed] Under Contract NNC09BA02B, DO-110 September, 2017",,False
