PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p94,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 94 Name Offset (bytes) Size (bytes) Data Type Units or Enumeration Source Mnemonic Setup Defined 0 1 Uint 8 0=Not defined, 1=Defined ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Experiment Type 1 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command MFCA1 Gas Type 2 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command MFCA2 Gas Type 3 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command MFCA3 Gas Type 4 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command E-Field Config 5 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command E-Field Polarity 6 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Igniter Arm 7 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Burner Type 8 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Thermocouple Config 9 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Radiometer Config 10 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSU 1 11 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSU 2 12 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSU 3 13 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSU 4 14 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSUG 5 15 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Use IPSUG 6 16 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command Fiber Config 17 1 Uint 8 Table 34 ACME_ SYSTEM_DEFINE_SETUP command",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p94,1,"3.2 External Ethernet Interfaces See also Table 20, Internal Ethernet Interfaces. The ‘Kernels’ string points to a hardware ethernet interface on the processor. It is used in /etc/udev/rules.d/90-net.rules to ensure that the device name is always assigned to the same connector. Table 15 External Ethernet Interfaces Source Device Name IP Address Net Mask Kernels Description Lippert SBC eth0 [ip removed] 255.255.0.0 0000:00:19.0 Interface to IOP",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p95,0,ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 95,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p96,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 96 4.0 INTERNAL INTERFACES 4.1 DNx-AI-207 Board This analog input layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 16 differential input channels with an input range of +/-10 Volts and 18-bit resolution. Several gains are available but ACME is using a gain of 1. Table 16 DNx-AI-207 Board Signals DNx-AI-207 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-0 MFCA1_FLOW MFCA1 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA1_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA1_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-1 MFCA2_FLOW MFCA2 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Nitrogen bypass/inert mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA2_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-2 MFCA3_FLOW MFCA3 Flow Rate 0 to 5 V Fuel mass flow controller flow rate. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA3_FULL_SCALE. Device is Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302. Full scale depends on installed device. AIN-3 ION_CURRENT Ion Current -1.5 to 1.5V Measurement of ion current between E-Field grid and burner. Ion Current (A) = 1000 * Voltage/162, where Rsense is resistance of shunt resistor and RDA is the data acquisition resistance. -25 to 25 µA.. AIN-4 PTA1_OUT PTA1 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Outer Coflow pressure.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p96,1,Converted in flight software to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR. AIN-5 PTA2_OUT PTA2 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Inner Coflow/Burner pressure. Converted in flight software to to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR. AIN-6 PTA3_OUT PTA3 Pressure 0.5 to 4.5 V Chamber pressure. Converted in flight software to to 0 to 145 psia using Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4. Device is Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p97,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 97 DNx-AI-207 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-7 HV_OUT E-Field Voltage -4 to 4 V Indirect measurement of E-Field high voltage supply. -10000 to +10000 V. E-Field (V) = Voltage * 2486.1795 + 141.9733. (Emperical equation). AIN-8 PMT1_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 1 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT1_GAIN, Table 18. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. Looks through a 310 nm bandpass interference filter AIN-9 PMT2_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 2 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT2_GAIN, Table 18. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. Looks through a broadband filter with a fused silica glass window and a neutral density coating. AIN-10 PMT3_OUT Photomultiplier Tube 3 Current 0 to 4 V 0 to 4 µA. Current (µA) = Voltage * 1. Depends on PMT3_GAIN, Table 18. Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. Looks through a 430 nm bandpass interference filter. 4.2 DNx-AI-225 Board This analog input layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 25 differential input channels with an input range of +/-1.25 Volts and 24-bit resolution. ° Table 17 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-0 TC_A Rake Thermocouple A -6.45 to 55 mV Near or far array Rake A Type K thermocouple, -200 to 1250 C. BRE_CTR_180 BRE BRE Center 180 -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Center 180 (South) Type K thermocouple, 0 to 500 C.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p97,1,"AIN-1 TC_B Rake Thermocouple B 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake B Type B thermocouple, 0 to 1700 C. BRE_OFF_180 BRE BRE Offset 180 -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Offset 180 (Far South) Type K thermocouple, 0 to 500 C. AIN-2 TC_C Rake Thermocouple C 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake C Type B thermocouple, 0 to 1700 C.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p98,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 98 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion BRE_CTR BRE BRE Center -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Center Type K thermocouple on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0- 36-21427KSA. AIN-3 TC_D Rake Thermocouple D 0 to 14 mV Near or far array Rake D Type K thermocouple, -200 to 1250 C. BRE_OFF BRE BRE Offset -6.45 to 55 mV BRE Offset Type K thermocouple on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0- 36-21427KSA. AIN-4 TC_200A 200mm Thermocouple A -6.45 to 55 mV Igniter side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. -200 to 1250 C. AIN-5 TC_200B 200mm Thermocouple B -6.45 to 55 mV Relay side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. -200 to 1250 C. AIN-6 TC_BNR Burner Thermocouple -6.45 to 55 mV Type K thermocouple on burner. -200 to 1250 C. Not valid when BRE burner is installed. AIN-7 RA+60 Radiometer +60 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is Dexter Research Center (DRC) XP-0055. BRE_OFF+60 BRE +60 BRE Offset 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP- 0249. AIN-8 RA+60_CJ Radiometer +60 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF+60CJ BRE +60 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-9 RA+30 Radiometer +30 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP- 0055. BRE_OFF+30 BRE +30 BRE Offset 0 to 2.5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP- 0249.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p98,1,AIN-10 RA+30_CJ Radiometer +30 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF+30CJ BRE +30 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-11 RA_CTR Radiometer Center 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 500. Device is DRC XP- 0156. BRE_OFF-10 BRE -10 BRE Offset 0 to 2.5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP- 0249.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p99,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 99 DNx-AI-225 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AIN-12 RA_CTR_CJ Radiometer Center Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. BRE_OFF-10CJ BRE -10 BRE Offset Cold Junction AIN-13 RA-30 Radiometer -30 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP- 0055. AIN-14 RA-30_CJ Radiometer -30 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. AIN-15 RA-60 Radiometer -60 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1500. Device is DRC XP- 0055. AIN-16 RA-60_CJ Radiometer -60 Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is TI LM20. AIN-17 RA_OFF Radiometer Offset 1.25 to 5 V Thermopile output (V) = (Voltage-1.25) / 1000. Device is DRC XP- 0869. This is located on the downstream relay board. AIN-18 RA_OFF_CJ Radiometer Offset Cold Junction 0 to 2.5 V 150 to -75 Celcius. 1.57 V at 25C. Device is Texas Instruments LM20. AIN-19 TC_SPARE Spare Thermocouple N/A To use, an additional thermocouple would need to be hard wired to the Cold Junction Compensation Assembly. This is located on the downstream relay board. AIN-20 BRE_FLUX_CTR BRE BRE Heat Flux Sensor - Center 0 to 1.25 V Heat flux sensor output on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36- 21427KSA. Valid only with BRE burner installed.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p99,1,1mV = 1 Btu/ft2 AIN-21 BRE_FLUX_OFF BRE BRE Heat Flux Sensor - Offset 0 to 1.25 V Heat flux sensor output on Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36- 21427KSA. Valid only with BRE burner installed. 1mV = 1 Btu/ft2 AIN-22 N/A Not Used N/A N/A AIN-23 N/A Not Used N/A N/A AIN-24 TC_CJ Thermocouple Cold Junction 0.803 to 1.10 V Temperature on the Cold Junction Compensation Assembly. 0 to 100 C. Device is Analog Devices AD590. Temperature (Celcius) = (Voltage/0.00295) – 273.15. BRE Valid when the BRE burner is installed.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p100,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 100 4.3 DNx-AO-333 Board This analog output layer in the UEI PowerDNA Cube has 32 channels with an output range of +/-10 Volts and 16-bit resolution. Table 18 DNx-AO-333 Board DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-0 MFCA1_CTRL MFCA1 Control 0 to 5 V Static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA1_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA1_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA1_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 19. AO-1 MFCA2_CTRL MFCA2 Control 0 to 5 V Nitrogen bypass/inert mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA2_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA2_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA2_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 19. AO-2 MFCA3_CTRL MFCA3 Control 0 to 5 V Fuel mass flow controller setpoint. 0 to MFCA3_FULL_SCALE in SLPM. Full scale depends on which Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 is installed. Output voltage = Setpoint(SLPM) * 5 / MFCA3_FULL_SCALE. Or Setpoint (SLPM) = Output voltage * MFCA3_FULL_SCALE / 5. See Table 19. AO-3 PMT_PWR PMT Power 0 or 5 V Power to three photomultipler tubes. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-4 HV_CTRL E-Field HV Control 0 to 10 V Sets E-field HV supply output between about -10000 and 10000 V. EField See EFieldSetVoltage command, section 3.1.8.2, for equation..",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p100,1,"AO-5 HV_EN E-Field HV Enable 0 or 5 V E-Field high voltage supply enable. 0 V = disabled, 5 V = enabled AO-6 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A AO-7 IGN_EN Igniter Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disabled. 5 V enabled. Software sets IGN_CTRL then pulses IGN_EN. AO-8 IGN_CTRL Igniter Control -0.6 to +0.8V Sets voltage at the igniter between 0.46 to 12 V. AO-9 MFCA1_PWR MFCA1 Power 0 or 5 V Power to static mixer/oxygen MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered. AO-10 MFCA2_PWR MFCA2 Power 0 or 5 V Power to nitrogen bypass/inert MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p101,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 101 DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-11 MFCA3_PWR MFCA3 Power 0 or 5 V Power to fuel MFC. 0 V = unpowered. 5 V = powered. AO-12 RB_UP_EN Relay Board Upstream Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disables signals. 5 V = state of signal output depends on signal value. Applicable signals: SV1, SV2, SV3, SV4, SV5, SV6, SV7, SV8, SV9, PMT_PWR, MFCA1_PWR, MFCA2_PWR, MFCA3_PWR AO-13 TFP_MOTOR_RST TFP Motor Reset 0 or 5 V 0 V to rest TFP stepper motor. 5 V to enable motor. AO-14 IGN_MOTOR_RST Igniter Motor Reset 0 or 5 V 0 V to reset igniter stepper motor. 5 V to enable motor. AO-15 SVA4 Solenoid Valve A4 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-16 SVA5 Solenoid Valve A5 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-17 SVA6 Solenoid Valve A6 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-18 SVA7 Solenoid Valve A7 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-19 SVA8 Solenoid Valve A8 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-20 SVA9 Solenoid Valve A9 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p101,1,"AO-21 SVA1 Solenoid Valve A1 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-22 SVA2 Solenoid Valve A2 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-23 SVA3 Solenoid Valve A3 0 or 5 V 0 V = no power to solenoid valve. 5 V = power solenoid valve, opening this normally closed valve. AO-24 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A AO-25 PMT1_GAIN PMT1 Gain 4.63 to 10 V For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p102,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 102 DNx-AO-333 Board Signals Channel Mnemonic Name Signal Range Description, Conversion AO-26 PMT2_GAIN PMT2 Gain 4.63 to 10 V For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. AO-27 PMT3_GAIN PMT3 Gain 4.63 to 10 For recommended device control voltage of 0.5 to 1.1 V. Gain range is 5x103 to 3.5x106. Gain=2x106 * (Output voltage/9.2645)^8.643856. Or Output voltage = 10^(0.115689 * log(Gain) + 0.23786213). Device is Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2. AO-28 LED_SIDE LED Side Bank 0 or 5 V Bank of 3 white LEDs to side of analog camera turning mirror. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-29 LED_END LED End Bank 0 or 5 V Bank of 3 white LEDs past the end of the analog camera turning mirror. 0 V = off. 5 V = on. AO-30 RB_DOWN_EN Relay Board Downstream Enable 0 or 5 V 0 V = disables signals. 5 V = state of signal output depends on signal value. Applicable signals: HV1, HV2, LED1, LED2, TFP_RST, IGN_RST, IGN_EN AO-31 N/A Not Used 0 or 5 V N/A",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p103,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 103 4.4 Serial Communication Table 19 Serial Communication Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description Lippert SBC /dev/ttyS0 MFCA1_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.5, 20 SLPM. Full scale flow of static mixer/oxygen mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA2_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1, 0.5, 2, 5 SLPM. Full scale flow of nitrogen bypass/Inert mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA3_FULL_SCALE Depends on what MFC is installed. 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5, 1 SLPM. Full scale flow of fuel mass flow controller in SLPM. Pulled from gas list item 18 in the result of the SFL (System Full List) command to device. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA1_STATE 0-10. See Table 24. State of the oxygen/static mixer mass flow controller. Result of a MS (get state) command. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA2_STATE 0-10. See Table 24. State of the nitrogen bypass mass flow controller. Result of a MS (get state) command. Lippert SBC RXD1/TXD1 /dev/ttyS0 MFCA3_STATE 0-10. See Table 24. State of the fuel mass flow controller. Result of an MS (get state) command.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p103,1,"ConnectTech serial card P5 /dev/CTI4 CUBE_SERIAL See DNA-PPCx-1G PowerDNA Gigabit Ethernet I/O Cube User Manual. UEI cube serial connection. Can be used to retrieve version numbers, set IP addresses, and update firmware. ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_AGC_MODE On or Off. Turn automatic gain control on or off ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_GAIN 6, 12, 21, and 31 dB. Set the automatic gain control gain.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p104,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 104 Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description ConnectTech serial card P6 /dev/CTI5 ANALOG_CAM_SHUTTER 1/60, 1/100, 1/250, 1/500, 1/1000, 1/2000, 1/4000, 1/10000, 1/20000, 1/30000 seconds. Set the shutter speed. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 IGN_MOTOR_SET_POS In counts. 0 is the retracted position. Maximum extended position depends on registry values Igniter/IgniterLimits and Igniter/IgniterMaxCount and the burner type last specified by a System Define Setup command. Default maximum is 2500 counts. Axis 1 control of motion control board in AVP controlling igniter motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 IGN_MOTOR_GET_POS See Signal Range for IGN_MOTION_SET_POS Axis 1 position reporting of motion control board in AVP controlling igniter motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 TFP_ MOTOR _SET_POS In counts. 0=retracted. Maximum=closer to burner. Maximum depends on burner type and registry values TfpMaxCount and TfpToBurnerOffsets. See Set TFP Position command for calculation of maximum. Axis 2 control of motion control board in AVP controlling TFP (thin filament pyrometry array) motor in CIA. ConnectTech serial card P7 /dev/CTI6 and /dev/ttyS2 TFP_ MOTOR _GET_POS See Signal Range for TFP_MOTION_SET_POS Axis 2 position reporting of motion control board in AVP controlling TFP motor in CIA.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p104,1,ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 ZOOM_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-85000 counts. 0 is zoomed out. 85000 is zoomed in. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 1 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 ZOOM_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-85000 counts. 0 is zoomed out. 85000 is zoomed in. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 1 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p105,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 105 Serial Communication Source Device Name Mnemonic Signal Range Description ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 IRIS_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-76000 counts. 0 is open. 76000 is closed. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 2 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 IRIS_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-76000 counts. 0 is open. 76000 is closed. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 2 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FOCUS_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-101000 counts. 0 is near focus. 101000 is far focus. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 3 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FOCUS_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-101000 counts. 0 is near focus. 101000 is far focus. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 3 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FILTER_ MOTOR _SET_POS 0-451000 counts. Filters at 0, 120000, 240000, and 360000 counts. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 4 control of motion control board in digital camera package. ConnectTech serial card P8 /det/CTI7 and /dev/ttyS3 FILTER_ MOTOR _GET_POS 0-451000 counts.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p105,1,"Filters at 0, 120000, 240000, and 360000 counts. Not valid when digital camera is connected to the IPSU-G. Axis 4 position reporting of motion control board in digital camera package.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p106,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 106 4.5 Internal Ethernet Interfaces See also Table 15, External Ethernet Interfaces where the interface to the IOP is listed. The ‘Kernels’ string points to a hardware ethernet interface on the processor. It is used in /etc/udev/rules.d/90-net.rules to ensure that the device name is always assigned to the same connector. Table 20 Internal Ethernet Interfaces Source Device Name IP Address Net Mask Kernels Description Lippert SBC eth1 [ip removed] 255.255.0.0 0000:06:00.0 Interface to data camera when connected directly to ACME and not IPSU-G. Lippert SBC eth2 [ip removed] 255.255.255.0 0000:08:00.0 Interface to UEI Cube. ACME Camera Package DeviceIPAddress [ip removed] 255.255.0.0 Camera IP address. Changeable using the CLIpConfig command line utility included in ACME software install. UEI Cube ip2 [ip removed] 255.255.255.0 Cube main ethernet port. Labeled NIC1. (yes, for ip2) UEI Cube ip [ip removed] 255.255.255.0 Cube secondary/diagnostic ethernet port. Labeled NIC2. NOT CONNECTED.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p107,0,ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 107 6.0 ENUMERATIONS Table 21 ACME System States ACME System States Value State Description 0 NULL State at the start of software execution. 1 INITIALIZE The software is initializing all hardware and sub-systems. 2 OP_IDLE The software is ready to accept commands. 3 OP_EXPERIMENT Automated experiments can be run in this state. 4 OP_MAINTENANCE Maintenance activities can be run in this state. 5 OP_UPLINK_DOWNLINK Currently unused. 6 OFF_NOMINAL An error has occurred and sub-systems have been safed. 7 SAFED Going to this state readies the system for a shutdown or reboot command. Table 22 IPSU Phases IPSU Phases Value State Description 0 None No test point-related commands are pending to IPSUs or IPSU-Gs. 1 Opening Test Point An open test point command has been sent to all selected IPSUs and IPSU-Gs. 2 Enabling Archiving An enable archiving command has been sent to all selected IPSUs. 3 Disabling Video A disable Video command has been sent to all selected IPSUs. 4 Starting Test Point A start test point command has been sent to all selected IPSUs and IPSU-Gs. 5 Stopping Test Point A stop test point command has been sent to all selected IPSUs and IPSU-Gs. 6 Closing Test POint A close test point command has been sent to all selected IPSUs and IPSU-Gs.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p108,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 108 Table 23 IPSU Status IPSU Status Value State Description 0 None No test point-related commands have been sent to the IPSU or IPSU-G yet. 1 Command Sent Command has been sent to IPSU or IPSU-G. 2 Command Failed Last command to IPSU or IPSU-G failed. For an IPSU this means a -1 in the subCommand field of the returned command. For an IPSU-G this means that the fcfSource in the returned command was not CMD_complete = 0x81. 3 Command Successful Last command to IPSU or IPSU-G was successful. For an IPSU this means not a -1 in the subCommand field of the returned command. For an IPSU-G this means that the fcfSource in the returned command was CMD_complete = 0x81. 4 Command Timed Out The IPSU or IPSU-G did not respond to the last command sent before the timeout period was up. Timeout period is registry value Ipsu/IpsuPhaseTimerPeriodMsec. See Table 32. 5 Inactive This is an inactive IPSU as determined by the SystemDefineSetup command. . Table 24 Mass Flow Controller State Mass Flow Controller States Source: Teledyne Hastings Digital 300 Software Guide Rev D. Document # 167-082010 Value State Description 0 OFF The MFC is off. An ACME state, not retrieved from MFC. 1 INIT Initialization in progress, disables auto flow control, disables MFM alarms. This clears all alarms when beginning INIT state. 2 IDLE MFM alarms are cleared and disabled (certain alarms such as instrument failures are not cleared and remain enabled). Indicated flow values are available.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p108,1,"Flow totalizing is disabled. MFC flow control stopped, valve goes to user-defined default position. Many configuration commands are only allowed in the IDLE state 3 RESERVED 4 OPERATE Executing; MFM and MFC alarms and flow totalizing are enabled. Automatic flow control enabled if otherwise permitted. 5 ABORT Network command sets ABORT state to permit diagnosis and recovery commands to be entered if/as necessary before restoring instrument to IDLE, OPERATE or INIT state. MFC flow control stopped, valve set to user-defined default position.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p109,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 109 Mass Flow Controller States Source: Teledyne Hastings Digital 300 Software Guide Rev D. Document # 167-082010 Value State Description 6 SFAIL Recoverable error detected such as critical data not set, missing, or out of range. Reset using power down, the reset button, or setting state to INIT (=1) are the only escapes. 7 CAL Calibration state disables auto flow control,clears and disables MFM and MFC alarms. Network commands to perform flow calibration are permitted. 8 TEST Network commands to perform certain tests are permitted. May disable alarms, may disable auto flow control, depending upon specific test invoked. Tests in TEST state are generally factory-only. 9 RECOVER Setting RECOVER state while in ABORT state initiates return to IDLE state. 10 TUNE Network command to perform certain flow and flow control tests are permitted. May disable alarms, may disable auto flow control, depending upon specific test invoked. Table 25 Waveform Enumeration Table 26 Enabled Disabled Enumeration Enabled Disabled Enumeration Value State 0 Disabled 1 Enabled Table 27 TFP Waveform State Enumeration Table 28 Extinction Detection State Enumeration Waveform Enumeration Value Waveform 0 None 1 Stepped 2 Ramped 3 Rectangular Wave 4 Ramped Wave TFP Waveform Enumeration Value Waveform 0 None 1 Ramp 2 RampedWave Extinction Detection State Enumeration Value State 0 Disabled 1 Enabled 2 Detected",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p110,0,ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 110 Table 29 Extinction Detection Action Enumeration Extinction Detection Action Enumeration Value State 0 Zero 1 Step 2 Ramp 3 Step Hold 4 Ramp Hold Table 30 Solenoid Valve State Enumeration Solenoid Valve State Value State 0 Disabled (Stop flow) 1 Enabled (Allow flow) Table 31 Script State Enumeration Script State Enumeration Value State 0 None 1 Loaded 2 Running 3 Paused 4 Aborted 5 Complete,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p111,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 111 7.0 CONFIGURATION FILES 7.1 AcmeConfig.ini This is also known as the registry file. It is a text file with the format shown below. In this document and as an argument to the SetRegistryItem command the keys are referenced as Group/Key. For example, to change Value2 in the example below issue the command SetRegistryItem(“GroupA/Key2”) followed by the command SetRegistryValue(“NewValue”). The table below shows the valid keys and values, including the value in the released version of AcmeConfig.ini. [GroupA] Key1=Value1 Key2=Value2 … [GroupB] Key3=Value3 … ; Any comments are preceded with a semi-colon Table 32 AcmeConfig.ini Contents AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description AvtCamera FileFormatTiff true, false false Save images in TIFF format or raw. True = TIFF. False = raw. Only used when ACME is connected directly to the digital camera. AvtCamera SerialNumber 02-2143A-17086 Serial number of the digital camera. Needed for the software to connect to the camera. Only used when ACME is connected directly to the camera. AvtCameraMotion Filter1Position Uint32 10000 Position where filter 1 is centered in the view. AvtCameraMotion Filter2Position Uint32 120000 Position where filter 2 is centered in the view. AvtCameraMotion Filter3Position Uint32 235000 Position where filter 3 is centered in the view. AvtCameraMotion Filter4Position Uint32 350000 Position where filter 4 is centered in the view.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p112,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 112 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description System UseAnalogCamera true,false true Enable serial control of the analog camera in the CIA. System UseCiaMotionBoard true,false true Connect to and use the motion controller in the CIA controlling the igniter arm and the TFP positioning. System UseCube true,false true Use the analog input and output layers on the UEI Cube. System UseDataCamera true,false false Enable control of the digital data camera directly from ACME. System UseFcfComms true,false true Automatically start FcfCommunications (Base Classes) application during initialization. System UseLippert true,false true Enable retrieval of CPU and CPU Board temperatures from CPU using LEMT. System UseSmartmon true,false true Enable retrieval of hard drive temperatures using smartctl.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p113,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 113 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Diagnostics BreHeader Comma- separated words, no spaces ""Time, MFCA1StaticMixerFlow, MFCA2BypassFlow, MFCA3FuelFlow, IonCurrent, PTA1, PTA2, PTA3, EfieldVoltage, PMT1, PMT2, PMT3, BRECenter180, BREOffset180, BRECenter, BREOffset, TC200A, TC200B, TCBurner, RadiometerBREOffset+60, RadiometerBREOffset+60CJ, RadiometerBREOffset+30, RadiometerBREOffset+30CJ, RadiometerBREOffset-10, RadiometerBREOffset-10CJ, Ch13, Ch14, Ch15, Ch16, RadiometerOffset, RadiometerOffsetCJ, TCE, BREHeatFluxCenter, BREHeatFluxOffset, TCCJ, EfieldSetpointOut"" Specifies the header string for the diagnostic data file when the experiement type communicated by the SystemDefineSetup command is BRE. Note: Value in previous column has spaces for this document. Actual value does not have spaces.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p114,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 114 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Diagnostics Header Comma- separated words, no spaces ""Time, MFCA1StaticMixerFlow ,MFCA2BypassFlow, MFCA3FuelFlow, IonCurrent ,PTA1, PTA2, PTA3, EfieldVoltage ,PMT1 ,PMT2, PMT3, TCA, TCB ,TCC, TCD, TC200A, TC200B,TCBurner, Radiometer+60, Radiometer+60CJ, Radiometer+30, Radiometer+30CJ, RadiometerCenter ,RadiometerCenterCJ, Radiometer-30, Radiometer- 30CJ,Radiometer-60, Radiometer-60CJ, RadiometerOffset, RadiometerOffsetCJ, TCE, Ch20, Ch21, TCCJ, EfieldSetpointOut"" Specifies the header string for the diagnostic data file when the experiement type communicated by the SystemDefineSetup command is not BRE. Note: Value in previous column has spaces for this document. Actual value does not have spaces. Diagnostics SampleTimeMsec Uint32 8 Duration in msec between diagnostic data samplings for the diagnostic data file. 8 msec is equivalent to 125 Hz. Diagnostics ExtinctionDetection SampleTimeMsec Uint32 100 Time in milliseconds between data samples for averaging to detect extinction. Diagnostics ExtinctionDetection UseSimDataFile Bool false When enabled takes data from sim data file instead of analog input boards. Diagnostics ExtinctionDetection SimDataFileName String /payload/app/config/ extinctionDetectionSimData.csv Sim extinction data. Format is csv, 8 columnds of data in order of configure command plus a comment column. First line is a header.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p115,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 115 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Diagnostics ExtinctionDetection ReverseLimitCheck Bool false When false, extinction is detected when values go below limits. When true, detection is when values go above limits. EField NegativeOutputFactorA Double -10886.5 Used to convert between desired E-Field voltage and control voltage when negative supply is used. See EFieldSetVoltage command, section 3.1.8.2, for equation. EField NegativeOutputFactorB Double 1048.203 See NegativeOutputFactorA description. EField NegativeOutputFactorC Double 2.7365 See NegativeOutputFactorA description. EField NegativeMinVoltage Float 0 This is enforced so that the output to the cube does not exceed 9.99V. EField NegativeMaxVoltage Float -10000 EField PositiveOutputFactorA Double -8.79 Used to convert between desired E-Field voltage and control voltage when positive supply is isntalled. See EFieldSetVoltage command, section 3.1.8.2, for equation. EField PositiveOutputFactorB Double 1074.01 See PositiveOutputFactorA description. EField PositiveOutputFactorC Double -1.594 See PositiveOutputFactorA description. EField PositiveMaxVoltage Float 0 EField PositiveMinVoltage Float 10000 This is enforced so that the output to the cube does not exceed 9.99V. EField RampResolutionMsec Uint32 1 This is the resolution of the signal generator. FCF RvcTimeoutMsec Uint32 10000 Maximum time in msec that the FcfCommunications (ie.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p115,1,Base Classes) application waits for returns from RCV commands. This is argument 4 passed to FcfCommunications. Flow MFCA1StaticMixer FullScaleSlm Float 20 This is the full scale flow of the MFC. Only used if the full scale flow was not obtained from the configuration information request (MFC ‘slm’ command) after power-on.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p116,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 116 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Flow MFCA2Bypass FullScaleSlm Float 0.1 This is the full scale flow of the MFC. Only used if the full scale flow was not obtained from the configuration information request (MFC ‘slm’ command) after power-on. Flow MFCA3Fuel FullScaleSlm Float 0.1 This is the full scale flow of the MFC. Only used if the full scale flow was not obtained from the configuration information request (MFC ‘slm’ command) after power-on. Flow MfcBootTimeMsec Uint32 10000 Time to wait after powering on mass flow controllers before opening serial port to the MFCs and requesting configuration information (MFC ‘slm’ command). Flow MfcRampResolutionMsec Uint32 100 This is the resolution of the signal generator. Flow SimulateMfcs Bool false Simulates the mass flow controllers if true. Flow WriteMfcSetpointsToFile Bool true If a test point is open, whenever any MFC changes setpoint a timestamped row of setpoints is written to the file, testPointName_mfcSetpoitns.csv. Igniter BurnerLimits Comma- separated Uint32s ""2500, 2410, 2386, 2362, 2510, 2492, 2486, 2420, 2314""",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p116,1,"List of maximum igniter positions per burner. First value corresponds to burner type 0, second to burner type 1, etc. See burnerType parameter in SystemDefineSetup command for list of burner types. Igniter AccelerationCountsPer SecSquared Uint32 5000 This is the acceleration used to move the igniter arm when velocity is not specified in the command. Igniter CheckMotionPeriodMsec Uint32 100 While in motion how often to report position in verbose logging. Igniter ConversionFactorA Float -0.6558 Used to convert desired voltage at igniter to control voltage. See IgniterPulse command in section 3.1.5.2. Igniter ConversionFactorB Float 0.1213 See description for ConversionFactorA.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p117,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 117 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Igniter DecelerationCountsPer SecSquared Uint32 5000 This is the deceleration used to move the igniter arm when velocity is not specified in the command. Igniter HomeAccelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 5000 This is the acceleration used to move the igniter arm to home position when it is not specified in the command. Igniter HomeDecelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 5000 This is the deceleration used to move the igniter arm to home position when it is not specified in the command. Igniter HomeVelocityCountsPerSec Uint32 2000 This is the velocity used to move the igniter arm to home position when it is not specified in the command. Igniter JerkCountsPerSecCubed Uint32 0 The motion jerk parameter for all movements. Igniter MaxPosition Uint32 2500 If IgniterLimits is not defined for the current burner then this value is used as the maximum igniter position. Igniter MaxPowerVolts Float -0.11 The maximum control voltage setpoint allowed to the igniter. -0.11 corresponds to 4.5 V. Igniter MinPowerVolts Float -0.6 The minimum control voltage setpoint allowed to the igniter. Igniter PositionError Uint32 0 The position error. See PMD documentation. Igniter Profile Uint16 0 0=Trapezoidal, 1=VelocityContouring, 2=Curve, 3=Electronic Gear Igniter RetryOnError Bool False If there is a motion error (i.e. slippage) then if this is true the motor will go slow until it recovers.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p117,1,Igniter VelocityCountsPerSec Uint32 2000 This is the velocity used to move the igniter arm when velocity is not specified in the command. Ipsu HandleIpsuRvcs Bool true Can turn off handling of command responses and use timeout instead by making this false.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p118,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 118 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Ipsu IpsuCommandResponse TimoutMsec Uint32 30000 Duration in msec to wait for an IPSU or IPSU-G command response. Ipsu IpsuForDataCamera 5-6 5 This is the number of the IPSU-G that is controlling the ACME digital data camera. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraCamera Number Uint32 3 For the IPSU-G specified by IpsuForDataCamera, this is the camera number assigned to the ACME digital data camera. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion 5-6 5 This is the number of the IPSU-G that is controlling the ACME data camera motors: zoom, iris, focus, and filter. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion CommandGroup Uint32 91 (x5B) Command group assigned to ACME motion commands on the IPSU-G specified by IpsuForDataCameraMotion. Used to populate move camera axis and get position commands. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion EnablePositionRequests bool true Whether or not to request data camera motion position data from the IPSU-G. Positions are only requested between motion start and detection of motion stopped when positions no longer change. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion ModuleIdentifier Uint32 3 For the IPSU-G specified by IpsuForDataCameraMotion, this is the external module number assigned to the ACME motion controller. Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion ModuleTelemetryIdentifier Uint32 2 For GetMotionTelemetry commands sent to the IPSU-G for filter and lens positions this is the camera number.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p118,1,Ipsu IpsuForDataCameraMotion PositionRequestPeriodMsec Uint32 1500 How often to request positions from the IPSU-G when motion is in progress. Stops when values do not change.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p119,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 119 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Ipsu IpsugAutoStartStopArchive Bool true Can turn off start and stop of archive on IPSU-Gs during StartIpsus and StopIpsus command by setting this to false. Ipsu IpsugReopenExistingTest Point Bool false This is used as the reopen parameter in the TestPoint Open command issued to IPSU-G. Ipsu IpsuWaitForResponse Bool 1=true Can turn off waiting for all IPSUs to respond for a phase by setting to 0 or false. Intensifier CommandDelayMsec Uint16 200 Delay between intensifier commands to the IPSU-G for IntensifierCameraGate and IntensifiedCameraSafe commands. Intensifier CommandGroup Uint16 89 (0x59) Command group for intensifier commands to the IPSU-G. Intensifier FilterAxis Uint16 4 Intensifier motion axis. Intensifier ModuleIdentifier Uint16 1 External module id for intensifier on IPSU-G. Intensifier MotionCommandGroup Uint16 93 (0x5D) Command group for intensifier motion commands to the IPSU-G. Intensifier MotionDelaySecs Uint16 10 Time to wait between motion commands (ie. Home, wait, go to position) Intensifier MotionModuleIdentifier Uint16 2 External module id for intensifier motion on IPSU-G. Intensifier SafeFilterPosition Uint32 1960 Used during IntensifiedCameraSafe command. Intensifier SafeGainCounts Uint32 2048 Used during IntensifiedCameraSafe command. Intensifier SafeGateWidthCounts Uint16 0 Used during IntensifiedCameraSafe command.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p119,1,OpsCamera InitalGain 0-4 3=21 dB On software startup the analo ops camera is set to use this gain. The meaning of the values is shown in section 3.1.4.27. OpsCamera InitialShutter 0-9 2=1/250 On software startup the analo ops camera is set to use this shutter speed. The meaning of the values is shown in section3.1.4.28.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p120,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 120 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Fiber AccelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 1000 This is the acceleration used to move the TFP fiber array when velocity is not specified in the command. Fiber CheckMotionPeriodMsec Uint32 100 While in motion how often to report position in verbose logging. Fiber DecelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 0 This is the deceleration used to move the TFP fiber array when velocity is not specified in the command. Fiber FiberToBurnerOffsets Comma- separated Uint32s ""0, 6996, 7245, 7496, 4606, 4921, 4921, 4921, 4921""",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p120,1,"List of TFP offsets from TfpMaxCount for each burner. First value corresponds to burner type 0, second to burner type 1, etc. See burnerType parameter in SystemDefineSetup command for list of burner types. Fiber HomeAccelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 1000 This is the acceleration used to move the TFP fiber array to home position when it is not specified in the command. Fiber HomeDecelerationCounts PerSecSquared Uint32 0 This is the deceleration used to move the TFP fiber array to home position when it is not specified in the command. Fiber HomeVelocityCountsPerSec Uint32 1200 This is the velocity used to move the TFP fiber array to home position when it is not specified in the command and when moving apart from a command, such as after startup and some state changes. Fiber JerkCountsPerSecCubed Uint32 0 The motion jerk parameter for all movements. Fiber MaxPosition Uint32 23450 Maximum position for the TFP (thin filament pyrometry array) for any burner. Fiber PositionError Uint32 0 The position error. See PMD documentation. Fiber Profile Uint16 0 0=Trapezoidal, 1=VelocityContouring, 2=Curve, 3=Electronic Gear",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p121,0,ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 121 AcmeConfig.ini Contents Group Key Valid Values Value Description Fiber RetryOnError Bool false If there is a motion error (i.e. slippage) then if this is true the motor will go slow until it recovers. UeiCube DataAcqIpAddress [ip removed] Cube IP address. Note 1: For ACME to control Camera Package change NO_EXT_MOTION_ACME to EXT_MOTION_ACME.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p122,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 122 7.2 AcmeLogging.ini This file located in /payload/app/config allows filter levels to be configured so that more or less information shows up in the telemetry and file message logs. In the message log each message contains a logging category, for example “acme.diag” or “zt.fcf”. To turn off a category make a rule in AcmeLogging.ini. For example, “acme.diag=false” turns off any message with the acme.diag category. Comments in the file indicate available categories. 7.3 Motion_ACME.ini This file located in /payload/app/config contains configuration for motion control of the camera package when ACME is controlling the camera motion instead of IPSU-G. It specifies the camera serial port (serialPortNumber=3 means use /dev/ttyS3) and parameters for each axis. While no longer used it may still be included to show what IPSU-G should have for this file. 7.4 Script Files Script files are used to conduct automated operations using the commands: SetScriptDirectory, LoadScript, RunScript, AbortScript, PauseScript, ResumeScript, and ChangeScriptParameter. They are named with a .js extension (for java script) and are typically stored in the /payload/app/scripts/ directory or any sub-directory of /payload/app/scripts, but can be anywhere as long as the SetScriptDirectory and/or LoadScript commands specify the location. The language used to write script files is technically ECMAScript-262 ( http://www.ecma- international.org/publications/files/ECMA-ST/Ecma-262.pdf).",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p122,1,"A brief summary can be currently found at https://wiki.qt.io/JavaScript. Many ACME functions and variables have been made visible to the scripts. All commands and their parameters can be used. All current telemetry is available. Public methods in controllers derived from XSystemController can be called. Any other objects passed to the QT macro Q_DECLARE_METATYPE(object) in the ACME source code can be used. Several helper functions are preloaded to the script engine and can also be used. print(message) logs a message. sendCommand(command) sends the specified command to the command handler. uSleep(time) pauses script execution for the specified number of milliseconds. More helper functions are loaded from the script file “/payload/app/scripts/helpers.js” if it exists. Here is an example of a basic ACME script: // BasicScript.js // When RunScript command is received this says to execute the run function below AcmeAvionicsController.runScript.connect(run); //This variable must be named parameters so the ground and flight software can manipulate the values. var parameters = { parameter1:1.0, parameter2:4, parameter3:true }; // from helpers.js. This tells the ground software the parameters and values so they can be // displayed and modified using the ChangeScriptParameter command printParams();",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p123,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 123 function run() { //The keyword ‘running’ is important for the ground software. print(""BasicScript running""); if ( parameters.parameter1 != 5 ) { // do something } // examples of filling in command parameters and sending to main program FlowSetSolenoidValveState.solendoidValve = 3; FlowSetSolenoidValveState.state = 1; sendCommand(FlowSetSolenoidValveState); // example of looking at current telemetry If ( FlowTelemetry.MFCA3FuelFlowSlpm > parameters.parameter3) { // do something } // script can pause itself. No parameters. sendCommand(PauseScript); print(“Script is paused. Press resume when ready.”); // now operator must issue ResumeScript command from ground // call a function in this file doSomethingElse(); // the keyword ‘completed’ is important for the ground software. Print(“BasicScript completed”); } Function doSomethingElse() { // more code }",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p124,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 124 8.0 OUTPUT FILES 8.1 Data Output File Data output files are created using the SystemOpenTestPoint command which creates a file named and stored at /payload/sci/testpointName_x/testpointName_x_data.csv, where testpointName is the parameter received in the SystemOpenTestPoint command and _x is optional to avoid duplicate files, where x = 1,2,3, etc. The file contains a two-line header. The first line has the date and time, documentation of the setup received in a SystemDefineSetup command, and the PMT gains. The second line has the column headings for the subsequent rows of data. The text of the column headings is defined by the Diagnostics/Header registry entry or the Diagnostics/BreHeader entry depending on whether the SystemDefineSetup command experimentType parameter was BRE or not. The column headings should match the data which is the following: - A timestamp in the format HH:MM:SS:mmm, where mmm is milliseconds. - 11 channels of analog input from the cube DNx-AI-207 board in the order shown in Table 16. - 25 channels of analog input from the cube DNx-AI-225 board in the order shown in Table 17. (The names of many of these values change depending on whether it is a BRE test or not, hence the two options for header.) - Channel AO-4 of the DNx-AO-333 analog output board. This is the E-Field control voltage.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p124,1,"Rows of comma-separated data is added to the file between DataRecordingStart and DataRecordingStop commands at a rate defined by the Diagnostics/SampleTimeMsec registry entry, see Table 32, defaulting to 8 msec for 125 Hz sampling. 8.2 Mass Flow Controller Setpoint File If the registry value Flow/WriteMfcSetpointsToFile is true when the SystemOpenTestPoint command is executed then a file of MFC setpoints is created alongside the data output file. The name of the file will be /payload/sci/testpointName_x/testpointName_x_mfcSetpoints.csv. The first row of text contains the same header as the data output file. The second row contains the headers, “Time,MFCA1Setpoint(V),MFCA2Setpoint(V),MFCA3Setpoint(V)”. Subsequent rows are written whenever one of the three MFCs change setpoints and includes the changed setpoint and the current setpoints of the other two MFCs, and a timestamp with millisecond resolution. The file is close when the SystemCloseTestPoint command is executed. 8.3 Message Log File Software messages are logged to files named and stored at /payload/logs/YYYY-MM-DD_hh- mmACME.log, where YYYY is year, MM is month, DD is day of month, hh is hour, and mm is minutes. The date in the name is when the log file is created, soon after software startup. Each message line in the file begins with a timestamp and a logging category. The timestamp is of the format YYYY-MM-DD DDD hh:mm:ss:mmm, where DDD is day of the year, mmm is milliseconds, and the rest are self-explanatory.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p124,2,See section 1.1 for information about the logging category and how to filter them out if desired.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p125,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 125 8.4 Command Log File The message log file, section 8.3, includes messages showing commands received and their parameters. Command log files contain only the details of each command received. The files are named and stored at /payload/logs/YYYY-MM-DD_hh-mmACMECommands.log. The format is for each command received a timestamped line of text with the command name followed by timestamped lines of text showing each parameter name and parameter value, including header information. 9.0 DIRECTORY STRUCTURE The files described in the previous two sections are stored on the solid state drive in the following locations. Table 33 Directory Structure Directory Strucure Path Contents /payload Root directory for ACME files. The script, startup.sh, looks here during each software startup to see if there is new software in a tar file to install. /payload/app Root directory for ACME application files. /payload/app/bin AcmeMp and FcfCommunications executables are located here. /payload/app/config Configurations files: AcmeConfig.ini AcmeLogging.ini /payload/app/scripts Science Qt script files including the automatically loaded helpers.js script. /payload/app/scripts/shell System bash scripts for startup, software updates, and directory listings. /payload/logs Message log files and command log files. /payload/sci Root directory for ACME science files. /payload/sci/YYDDDtt Data output files and Mass Flow Controller Setpoint files.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p125,1,"The names of the directories are what is specified in the TestPointOpen commands, tentatively to follow the convention of YY=year (ie. 17 for 2017), DDD=GMT day (001-365), and tt=test points of the day (ie. A1, A2, B1, …).",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p126,0,ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 126 10.0 DATA FILE CONVERSION This section describes how to convert the headers and sensor readings in the data output file to engineering values. The raw data is in units of volts read directly from the UEI data acquisition system. Converions of the data depend on whether the experiment type is BRE or not. See sub- section 10.2 for non-BRE or sub-section 10.3 for BRE. 10.1 Metadata Header The first row of the data output file is a comma-separate list of metadata documenting the system configuration when the data was collected.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p126,1,Table 34 Data File Metadata Header Data File Metadata Header Name Possible Values Timestamp Formatted as year-month-day GMTday hr:min:sec:millisecond Experiment 0 Flame Design 1 Coflow 2 S-Flame 3 E-Field 4 BRE Test Point Name of test point MFCA1 Gas 0 Oxygen/Nitrogen (21/79) 1 Oxygen/Nitrogen (30/70) 2 Oxygen/Nitrogen (40/60) 3 Oxygen/Nitrogen (85/15) 4 Oxygen/Helium (30/70) MFCA1 Full Scale 0 to 20 SLPM MFCA2 Gas 0 Nitrogen 1 Helium MFCA2 Full Scale 0 to 20 SLPM MFCA3 Gas 0 Methane 1 Methane/Nitrogen (30/70) 2 Methane/Nitrogen (40/60) 3 Methane/Nitrogen (45/55) 4 Ethylene 5 Ethylene/Nitrogen (30/70) 6 Ethylene/Nitrogen (50/50) 7 Hydrogen 8 Hydrogen/Methane (44.4/55.6) 9 Hydrogen/Methane (55.6/44.4) 10 Hydrogen/Methane (66.7/33.3) 11 Hydrogen/Methane/Helium (20/25/55) 12 Hydrogen/Methane/Helium (25/20/55) 13 Hydrogen/Methane/Helium (30/15/55) 14 Hydrogen/Helium (45/55) 15 Methane/Helium (45/55) 16 Ethylene/Helium (20/80) 17 Ethylene/Helium (25/75),,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p127,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 127 18 Ethylene/Helium (30/70) MFCA3 Full Scale 0 to 20 SLPM EField 0 Mesh Removed 1 Mesh in 35 mm position 2 Mesh in 40 mm position EFieldPol 0 Not installed 1 Negative 2 Positive Igniter 0 0 mm 1 10 mm 2 30 mm Burner 0 Spherical (1/4"") 1 Spherical (3/8"") 2 Spherical (1/2"") 3 Coflow 4 Gas Jet(1.3mm) 5 Gas Jet(2.1mm) 6 BRE (25mm) 7 BRE (50mm) Thermocouple 0 Near 1 Far 2 Removed Radiometer 0 Standard 1 BRE IPSU 1 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point (HiBMs) IPSU 2 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point IPSU 3 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point IPSU 4 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point IPSU 5 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point (ACME camera and/or Intensified Camera) IPSU 6 0 Do not archive images 1 Archive images during test point Fiber 0 Not installed 1 Installed PMT 1 Gain 0 to 10 Volts PMT 2 Gain 0 to 10 Volts PMT 3 Gain 0 to 10 Volts",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p128,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 128 10.2 Data Conversions (non-BRE) Each paragraph name in this section refers to a column in the data output file. The Voltage variable in each equation is the data value. 10.2.1 Time Description: Timestamp in the format hour:min:sec:msec. The date can be found the the first row header. 10.2.2 MFCA1StaticMixerFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA1 sourced from the CIR static mixer manifold. This is the oxidizer. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA1 Full Scale ,where MFCA1 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.2.3 MFCA2BypassFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA2 sourced from the CIR nitrogen or nitrogen bypass manifold. This is the inert. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA2 Full Scale ,where MFCA2 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.2.4 MFCA3FuelFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA3 sourced from the CIR fuel manifold. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA3 Full Scale ,where MFCA3 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.2.5 IonCurrent Description: Measurement of ion current between E-Field grid and burner Conversion: Ion Current (microAmps) = 1000 * Voltage / 162 10.2.6 PTA1 Description: Inner coflow/burner pressure. Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p129,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 129 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.2.7 PTA2 Description: Outer coflow burner pressure. Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.2.8 PTA3 Description: Chamber pressure Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.2.9 EfieldVoltage Description: Indirect measurement of the E-Field high voltage supply. Conversion source: Determined empirically. Conversion: E-Field (V) = Voltage * 2486.1795 + 141.9733 10.2.10 PMT1 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a 310 nm bandpass interference filter Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: Depends on PMT gain.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p129,1,"Gain = 3V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1.991881x2 - 0.005211x + 0.000200 Gain = 4V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 196.835980x3 + 0.345545x2 + 0.519914x + 0.000150 Gain = 5V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1,104.055224x3 + 34.407322x2 + 2.770232x + 0.000277 Gain = 5.5V Irradiance (W/cm2) = -58,849.143398x4 + 11,868.553546x3 - 224.738423x2 + 10.187086x + 0.000282 Gain = 6V Irradiance (W/cm2) = -55,617.012418x4 + 22,186.536267x3 - 645.571330x2 + 22.895739x + 0.000400 Gain = 7V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 3,308,609.058167x4 - 166,821.231989x3 + 3,599.519526x2 + 39.920446x + 0.003750 Gain = 8V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 395,393.992726x3 - 7,363.493027x2 + 253.097826x + 0.002500",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p130,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 130 10.2.11 PMT2 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a broadband filter with a fused silica glass window and a neutral density coating. Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: depends on PMT gain. Gain = 2V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 8.585779x2 + 0.156690x + 0.000105 Gain = 2.5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -43.824964x3 + 169.992980x2 + 1.665894x - 0.000060 Gain = 3V: Irradiance (W/cm^2) = 291,761.896381x5 - 88,314.764348x4 + 8,801.002262x3 + 65.786376x2 + 3.172557x + 0.000010 Gain = 3.5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 459,377.096347x4 - 39,905.504054x3 + 1,814.542253x2 + 15.361730x + 0.000260 Gain = 4V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 2,092.641446x2 + 40.832842x - 0.000930 Gain = 5V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 728,809,327.944092x4 - 11,745,484.619257x3 + 60,902.178128x2 + 271.865031x - 0.007000 Gain = 6V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 71,216.045377x2 + 1,600.544829x - 0.043000 10.2.12 PMT3 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a 430 nm bandpass interference filter. Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: depends on PMT gain. Gain = 3V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -1,764.688010x4 + 508.863505x3 - 15.508597x2 + 0.393871x + 0.000070 Gain = 4V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -14,425.292616x4 + 4,236.185250x3 - 46.099632x2 + 2.012753x + 0.000600 Gain = 4.5V:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p130,1,"Irradiance (W/cm2) = -2,955,659.559357x5 + 543,397.470716x4 - 19,411.363291x3 + 505.687643x2 + 5.655574x + 0.002100 Gain = 5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 911,016.817407x4 - 44,193.276271x3 + 1,087.860546x2 + 8.544647x + 0.003600 Gain = 6V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 7,785.072945x3 + 2,717.730343x2 + 50.108622x + 0.019400 Gain = 7V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 703,610.180561x3 - 11,656.854323x2 + 337.786210x + 0.074000 Gain = 8V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 165,632.254213x2 + 451.923332x + 0.285000",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p131,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 131 10.2.13 TCA Description: Thermocouple at position A on the near or far thermcouple rake. Device: Marlin 92420280-107 for near assembly, Marlin 92420280-087 for far assembly Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.14 TCB Description: Thermocouple at position B on the near or far thermcouple rake. Device: Marlin 92420281-053 for near assembly, Marlin 92420281-042 for far assembly Conversion: Use the Type B thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.15 TCC Description: Thermocouple at position C on the near or far thermcouple rake. Device: Marlin 92420281-048 for near assembly, Marlin 92420281-034 for far assembly Conversion: Use the Type B thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.16 TCD Description: Thermocouple at position D on the near or far thermcouple rake. Device: Marlin 92420280-087 for near assembly, Marlin 92420280-087 for far assembly Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.17 TC200A Description: Igniter side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. Device: Marlin 9242083-052 Conversion:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p131,1,"Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.18 TC200B Description: Relay side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. Device: Marlin 92420283-038 Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C).",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p132,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 132 10.2.19 TCBurner Description: Thermocouple on the burner Device: Depends on burner: 1.3 mm gas jet burner Marlin 92420308-667 2.1 mm gas jet burner Marlin 92420308-667 1/4"" spherical burner Marlin 92420308-705 3/8"" spherical burner Marlin 92420308-705 1/2"" spherical burner Marlin 92420308-705 Coflow burner No thermocouple Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.2.20 Radiometer+60 Description: Radiometer at the 60mm position on the standard radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0055 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.002622 * Voltage - 0.003370 10.2.21 Radiometer+60CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the 60mm radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.2.22 Radiometer+30 Description: Radiometer at the 30mm position on the standard radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0055 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001794 * Voltage - 0.002309 10.2.23 Radiometer+30CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the 30mm radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒)",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p133,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 133 10.2.24 RadiometerCenter Description: Radiometer at the center position on the standard radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0156 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.002894 * Voltage - 0.003932 10.2.25 RadiometerCenterCJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the center radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.2.26 Radiometer-30 Description: Radiometer at the -30mm position on the standard radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0055 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.002397 * Voltage - 0.003077 10.2.27 Radiometer-30CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the -30mm radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.2.28 Radiometer-60 Description: Radiometer at the -60mm position on the standard radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0055 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.002591 * Voltage - 0.003300 10.2.29 Radiometer-60CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the -60mm radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p133,1,𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.2.30 RadiometerOffset Description: Radiometer located on the downstream relay board.,,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p134,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 134 Device: Dexter Research Center DX-0869 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001798 * Voltage - 0.002307 10.2.31 RadiometerOffsetCJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the offset radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.2.32 TCE Description: Not used – spare 10.2.33 Ch20 Description: Not used during non-BRE experiments 10.2.34 Ch21 Description: Not used during non-BRE experiments 10.2.35 TCCJ Description: Temperature sensor located on the cold junction compensation assembly used for cold junction compensation of thermocouples. Device: Analog Devices AD590 Conversion: Temperature (C) = 338.98305 * Voltage - 273.15 10.2.36 EfieldSetpointOut Description: Control voltage output to the E-Field supply to achieve E-Field voltage from 0 to +/- 10kV. Conversion: E-Field Voltage (V) = C * EfieldSetpointOut2 + B * EfieldSetpointOut + A, where A, B,and C depend on supply polarity: Negative polarity Positive polarity A = -10886.5 A = -8.79 B = 1048.203 B = 1074.01 C = 2.7365 C = -1.594 The avionics software uses the inverse of this equation to determine the control voltage for the commanded E-Field voltage:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p135,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 135 𝐸𝑓𝑖𝑒𝑙𝑑𝑆𝑒𝑡𝑝𝑜𝑖𝑛𝑡𝑂𝑢𝑡 = −B + √𝐵2 − 4C(A − EFieldVoltage) 2𝐶 10.3 Data Conversions (BRE) When the experiment type is BRE as set by the SystemDefineSetup command some data columns change name and conversion to reflect the connection of the BRE burner and the BRE radiometer array and the removal of the thermcouple rake. 10.3.1 Time Description: Timestamp in the format hour:min:sec:msec. The date can be found the the first row header. 10.3.2 MFCA1StaticMixerFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA1 sourced from the CIR static mixer manifold. This is the oxidizer. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA1 Full Scale ,where MFCA1 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.3.3 MFCA2BypassFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA2 sourced from the CIR nitrogen or nitrogen bypass manifold. This is the inert. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA2 Full Scale ,where MFCA2 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.3.4 MFCA3FuelFlow Description: Measured flow from MFCA3 sourced from the CIR fuel manifold. Device: Teledyne Hastings HFC-D-302 Conversion: Flow rate (SLPM) = Voltage / 5.0 * MFCA3 Full Scale ,where MFCA3 Full Scale is indicated in the meta data header. 10.3.5 IonCurrent Description: Measurement of ion current between E-Field grid and burner Conversion: Ion Current (microAmps) = 1000 * Voltage / 162",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p136,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 136 10.3.6 PTA1 Description: Inner coflow/burner pressure. Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.3.7 PTA2 Description: Outer coflow burner pressure. Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.3.8 PTA3 Description: Chamber pressure Device: Measurement Specialties EPRB-2-VR33-10B-/CM1/ATR Conversion: Pressure (psia) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 Pressure (atm) = (Voltage – 0.5) * 14.5038 * 10 / 4 / 14.69595 10.3.9 EfieldVoltage Description: Indirect measurement of the E-Field high voltage supply. Conversion source: Determined empirically. Conversion: E-Field (V) = Voltage * 2486.1795 + 141.9733 10.3.10 PMT1 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a 310 nm bandpass interference filter Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: Depends on PMT gain. Gain = 3V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1.991881x2 - 0.005211x + 0.000200 Gain = 4V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 196.835980x3 + 0.345545x2 + 0.519914x + 0.000150 Gain = 5V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1,104.055224x3 + 34.407322x2 + 2.770232x + 0.000277 Gain = 5.5V Irradiance (W/cm2) = -58,849.143398x4 + 11,868.553546x3 - 224.738423x2 + 10.187086x + 0.000282",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p137,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 137 Gain = 6V Irradiance (W/cm2) = -55,617.012418x4 + 22,186.536267x3 - 645.571330x2 + 22.895739x + 0.000400 Gain = 7V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 3,308,609.058167x4 - 166,821.231989x3 + 3,599.519526x2 + 39.920446x + 0.003750 Gain = 8V Irradiance (W/cm2) = 395,393.992726x3 - 7,363.493027x2 + 253.097826x + 0.002500 10.3.11 PMT2 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a broadband filter with a fused silica glass window and a neutral density coating. Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: depends on PMT gain. Gain = 2V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 8.585779x2 + 0.156690x + 0.000105 Gain = 2.5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -43.824964x3 + 169.992980x2 + 1.665894x - 0.000060 Gain = 3V: Irradiance (W/cm^2) = 291,761.896381x5 - 88,314.764348x4 + 8,801.002262x3 + 65.786376x2 + 3.172557x + 0.000010 Gain = 3.5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 459,377.096347x4 - 39,905.504054x3 + 1,814.542253x2 + 15.361730x + 0.000260 Gain = 4V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 2,092.641446x2 + 40.832842x - 0.000930 Gain = 5V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 728,809,327.944092x4 - 11,745,484.619257x3 + 60,902.178128x2 + 271.865031x - 0.007000 Gain = 6V; Irradiance (W/cm2) = 71,216.045377x2 + 1,600.544829x - 0.043000 10.3.12 PMT3 Description: Photomultiplier tube with a 430 nm bandpass interference filter. Device: Hamamatsu H10722-10-MOD2 Conversion source: ACME-RPT-0013, PMT Characterization Report, Rev - Conversion: depends on PMT gain. Gain = 3V:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p137,1,"Irradiance (W/cm2) = -1,764.688010x4 + 508.863505x3 - 15.508597x2 + 0.393871x + 0.000070 Gain = 4V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -14,425.292616x4 + 4,236.185250x3 - 46.099632x2 + 2.012753x + 0.000600 Gain = 4.5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = -2,955,659.559357x5 + 543,397.470716x4 - 19,411.363291x3 + 505.687643x2 + 5.655574x + 0.002100",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p138,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 138 Gain = 5V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 911,016.817407x4 - 44,193.276271x3 + 1,087.860546x2 + 8.544647x + 0.003600 Gain = 6V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 7,785.072945x3 + 2,717.730343x2 + 50.108622x + 0.019400 Gain = 7V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 703,610.180561x3 - 11,656.854323x2 + 337.786210x + 0.074000 Gain = 8V: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 165,632.254213x2 + 451.923332x + 0.285000 10.3.13 BRECenter180 Description: Thermocouple at the south position on the BRE burner. Device: Marlin 92420321 Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.3.14 BREOffset180 Description: Thermocouple at the far south position on the BRE burner. Device: Marlin 92420321 Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.3.15 BRECenter Description: Thermocouple on the BRE burner center heat flux transducer. Device: Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36-21427KSA. Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.3.16 BREOffset Description: Thermocouple on the BRE burner offset heat flux transducer. Device: Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36-21427KSA. Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C).",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p138,1,"10.3.17 TC200A Description: Igniter side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. Device: Marlin 9242083-052 Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C).",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p139,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 139 10.3.18 TC200B Description: Relay side Type K thermocouple, 200 mm from axis. Device: Marlin 92420283-038 Conversion: Use the Type K thermocouple conversion in Section 0 using the converted TCCJ column, Section 10.2.35, for cold junction temperature (C). 10.3.19 TCBurner Description: Thermocouple on the burner. No connection when the BRE burner is installed. 10.3.20 RadiometerBREOffset+60 Description: Radiometer at the 60mm position on the BRE radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0249 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-012, BRE Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001140 * Voltage - 0.001481 10.3.21 RadiometerBREOffset+60CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the 60mm BRE radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.3.22 RadiometerBREOffset+30 Description: Radiometer at the 30mm position on the BRE radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0249 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-012, BRE Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001127 * Voltage - 0.001579 10.3.23 RadiometerBREOffset+30CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the 30mm BRE radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.3.24 RadiometerBREOffset-10 Description:",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p139,1,"Radiometer at the -10mm position on the BRE radiometer assembly. Device: Dexter Research Center XP-0249 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-012, BRE Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p140,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 140 Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001188 * Voltage - 0.001583 10.3.25 RadiometerBREOffset-10CJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the -10mm BRE radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.3.26 Ch13 Description: Not used during BRE experiments 10.3.27 Ch14 Description: Not used during BRE experiments 10.3.28 Ch15 Description: Not used during BRE experiments 10.3.29 Ch16 Description: Not used during BRE experiments 10.3.30 RadiometerOffset Description: Radiometer located on the downstream relay board. Device: Dexter Research Center DX-0869 Thermopile Detector Conversion Source: ACME-RPT-011, Radiometer Characterization Report, Rev -. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 0.001798 * Voltage - 0.002307 10.3.31 RadiometerOffsetCJ Description: Cold junction temperature sensor associated with the offset radiometer. Device: TI LM20 Conversion: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −1481.96 + √2196200 + 257700(1.8639 − 𝑉𝑜𝑙𝑡𝑎𝑔𝑒) 10.3.32 TCE Description: Not used – spare 10.3.33 BREHeatFluxCenter Description: BRE burner center heat flux sensor. Device: Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36-21427KSA.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p141,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 141 Conversion Source: Device quote indicates that output is 10 BTU/ft2 at 10 mV. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1135.6538527 * Voltage 10.3.34 BREHeatFluxOffset Description: BRE burner offset heat flux sensor. Device: Medtherm 8-2.688-10SB-0-0-36-21427KSA. Conversion Source: Device quote indicates that output is 10 BTU/ft2 at 10 mV. Conversion: Irradiance (W/cm2) = 1135.6538527 * Voltage 10.3.35 TCCJ Description: Temperature sensor located on the cold junction compensation assembly used for cold junction compensation of thermocouples. Device: Analog Devices AD590 Conversion: Temperature (C) = 338.98305 * Voltage - 273.15 10.3.36 EfieldSetpointOut Description: Control voltage output to the E-Field supply to achieve E-Field voltage from 0 to +/- 10kV. Conversion: E-Field Voltage (V) = C * EfieldSetpointOut2 + B * EfieldSetpointOut + A, where A, B,and C depend on supply polarity: Negative polarity Positive polarity A = -10886.5 A = -8.79 B = 1048.203 B = 1074.01 C = 2.7365 C = -1.594 The avionics software uses the inverse of this equation to determine the control voltage for the commanded E-Field voltage: 𝐸𝑓𝑖𝑒𝑙𝑑𝑆𝑒𝑡𝑝𝑜𝑖𝑛𝑡𝑂𝑢𝑡 = −B + √𝐵2 − 4C(A − EFieldVoltage) 2𝐶",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p142,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 142 10.4 Type K Thermocouple Conversion Input to this conversion is thermocouple output in millivolts and cold junction temperature in Celcius. First convert cold junction temperature (C), cjTemp, to millivolts in regard to a type K thermocouple: 𝑐𝑗𝑀𝑣 = −0.176004136860E − 01 + 0.389212049750E − 01 ∗ cjTemp + 0.185587700320E − 04 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝2 − 0.994575928740E − 07 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝3 + 0.318409457190E − 09 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝4 − 0.560728448890E − 12 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝5 + 0.560750590590E − 15 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝6 − 0.320207200030E − 18 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝7 + 0.971511471520E − 22 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝8 − 0.121047212750E − 25 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝9 + 𝑎0 ∗ 𝑒𝑎1(𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝−𝑎2)2 ,where a0 = 0.118597600000E+00 a1 = -0.118343200000E-03 a2 = 0.126968600000E+03 Next add cjMv to thermocouple output: totalMv = cjMv + tcMv If totalMv is between 0 and 20.644 mV 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = 25.08355 ∗ totalMv + 0.07860106 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣2 − 0.2503131 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣3 + 0.08315270 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣4 − 0.01228034 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣5 + 0.0009804036 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣6 − 0.00004413030 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣7 + 0.000001057734 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣8 − 0.00000001052755 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣9 If totalMv is between 20.644 and 54.886 mV 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = −131.8058 + 48.30222 ∗ totalMv − 1.646031 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣2 + 0.05464731 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣3 − 0.0009650715 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣4 + 0.000008802193 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣5 − 0.00000003110810 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣6 If totalMv is less than 0 then the temperature is between -200 and 0 C and is likely invalid for this application. If totalMv is greater than 54.886 then the response is out of range of the thermocouple.",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p143,0,"ACME-DOC-010 Rev D 143 10.5 Type B Thermocouple Conversion Input to this conversion is thermocouple output in millivolts and cold junction temperature in Celcius. First convert cold junction temperature (C), cjTemp, to millivolts in regard to a type B thermocouple: If cjTemp < 630 C use: 𝑐𝑗𝑀𝑣 = −0.246508183460E − 03 ∗ cjTemp + 0.590404211710E − 05 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝2 − 0.132579316360E − 08 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝3 + 0.156682919010E − 11 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝4 − 0.169445292400E − 14 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝5 + 0.629903470940E − 18 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝6 If cjTemp >= 630 C use: 𝑐𝑗𝑀𝑣 = −0.389381686210E + 01 + 0.285717474700E − 01 ∗ cjTemp − 0.848851047850E − 04 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝2 + 0.157852801640E − 06 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝3 − 0.168353448640E − 09 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝4 + 0.111097940130E − 12 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝5 − 0.445154310330E − 16 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝6 + 0.989756408210E − 20 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝7 − 0.937913302890E − 24 ∗ 𝑐𝑗𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝8 Next add cjMv to thermocouple output. totalMv = cjMv + tcMv If totalMv is between 0.291 and 2.431 mV use: 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = 98.423321 + 699.71500 ∗ totalMv − 847.65304 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣2 + 1005.2644 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣3 − 833.45952 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣4 + 455.08542 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣5 − 155.23037 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣6 + 29.886750 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣7 − 2.4742860 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣8 If totalMv is between 2.431 and 13.820 mV 𝑇𝑒𝑚𝑝𝑒𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 (𝐶) = 213.15071 + 285.10504 ∗ totalMv − 52.742887 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣2 + 9.9160804 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣3 − 1.2965303 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣4 + 0.11195870 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣5 − 0.0060625199 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣6 + 0.00018661696 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣7 − 0.0000024878585 ∗ 𝑡𝑜𝑡𝑎𝑙𝑀𝑣8",,False
PSI-23,Reference Data,PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Reference Data/PSI-23_Reference Data_ACME-DOC-010_D.pdf,p143,1,If totalMv is less than 0.291 mV or greater than 13.820 mV then the response is out of range of the thermcouple.,,False
