PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME_Integrated_Science_Requirements_RevB.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME_Integrated_Science_Requirements_RevB.pdf,p97,0,"ACME-SRD-001.B Integrated Science Requirements Document (ISRD) 2013-SEPT-30 97 Figure 9. Schematic of the base of the updated coflow burner shown in Figure 5, where the base serves as an inlet plenum (normally for fuel or fuel-inert mixtures).",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME_Integrated_Science_Requirements_RevB.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME_Integrated_Science_Requirements_RevB.pdf,p98,0,"ACME-SRD-001.B Integrated Science Requirements Document (ISRD) 2013-SEPT-30 98 Appendix C: Electric Field Design Reference Figure 10. Electric field schematic. An effective resistance of 200 giga-ohms is r ecommended for the insulation between the mesh electrode and the chamber. With that resistan ce, leaking current at 10 kV would be 0.05 mA, which is sufficiently small in comparison with estimated flame current of ~ 1 mA. + - H.V Chamber Resistance of mesh support, Re Nozzle Mesh electrode Shunt for current measurement, Rs Low voltage input, e.g., 0-24VDC Feed-through Gas supply tubes Insulator",,False
