PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,p17,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration Electrodes: Burner (1.5) and Mesh (1.6)() () Burner as Electrode (1.5) - doesn’t apply to spherical burners • Resistance <1 Ohm along/across burner (i.e., same potential) • Insulation burner insulated from the chamber Electrode Mesh (1.6) • Shape flat circle • Material copper (mesh and ring) • Mesh 16-22 wires/inch 0.38-0.64 mm diameter wire • Edge 2-3 mm diameter ring •Size ≥80 mm diameter (ring OD) • Orientation orthogonal and on chamber axis • Position 25 or 40 mm ‘above’ window centers • Removable during spaceflight www.nasa.gov 17 gp g",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,p18,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration Electric Field (1.7)() • Voltage range -10 to +10 kV set within ±0.1% of set point • Step change any polarity and magnitude within range ≤5 ms rise time • Alternating polarity sequence of steps at 0-100 Hz (mimic AC field) • Uplink voltage, polarity, step changes, timing • No conductive contact mesh and burner (except for temp. measurement) • Conductive free zone ≥30 mm more than mesh diameter from burner to ≥20 mm downstream of mesh • Current leakage <100 nanoamps (at ±10 kV with a 35-mm spacing) • Removable high voltage power supplies, associated electronics www.nasa.gov 18",,False
