PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_ACME Integrated Science Requirements Definition Review 20100505.pdf,p22,0,"National Aeronautics and Space Administration Ambient Environment (1.11)() • Composition uplinkable and variable to ±0.01 mole fraction • Contaminants ≤0.01 mole fraction and dry, unless waived • Atmosphere well mixed • Quiescent 300 s hold period before ignition • Pressure 0.1 to 3 bar within ±3% of set point • Temperature 290-310 K, uniform within ±5 K • Free volume ≥80 liters, symmetric as possible • Free zone – spherical flames ≥200 mm diameter – non-spherical ≥150 mm diameter cylinder, ≥200 mm up, etc. • Disturbance limit burner flow, combustion, probe motion, g-jitter • No test prohibition during thruster firing, docking, or undocking • ‘Black’ background no reflection or emission in view of sensor • Emissivity ≥0.5 except for burners, probe tips, igniter, etc. www.nasa.gov 22 Req’t for dynamic venting was disallowed because of difficulty & cost!",,False
