PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p1,0,"ACME-REQ-001 Rev. K Advanced Combustion Microgravity Experiment (ACME) Engineering Requirements Document (ERD) April, 2014 Prepared For: National Aeronautics and Space Administration John H. Glenn Research Center at Lewis Field Space Operations Project [address removed] Prepared By: ZIN Technologies, Incorporated [address removed] Under Contract NNC14CA02C, <DO-XXX>",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p2,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME- REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page ii of vii PREFACE The Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments (ACME) is a next generation mini- facility designed to support Principal Investigators (PI) interested in studying various aspects of advanced gaseous combustion in a microgravity environment. ACME will be integrated into the Fluids and Combustion Facility’s (FCF) Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) onboard the International Space Station in the US Lab Module. The ACME mission is to perform microgravity experiments to study fire suppression/flame extinguishment investigations using the Combustion Integrated Rack. The ACME will allow investigation using pure fuels and mixtures of fuels at various chamber atmosphere pressures, compositions, and oxygen concentrations. The microgravity environment allows for measurement and observation of flame formation and extinguishment processes that cannot be made in sustained gravity. The modular design of the ACME allows for flexibility in configuring for specific experiments and easy maintainability of the hardware. This hardware will provide the apparatus for dispensing, deploying and igniting fuel. When new experiments are proposed the additional experiment specific hardware will be provided. This requirements document reflects such a case, including only the new requirements of the ACME investigation.",,False
