PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p49,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 42 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1130 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.1 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer – 20 cm/s ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm outside the inner tube wall, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for a matched velocity in the inner and outer tubes of 20 cm/s. BURNER 530_1140 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.1 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer – 30 cm/s ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm outside the inner tube wall, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for a matched velocity in the inner and outer tubes of 30 cm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p49,1,"BURNER 530_1150 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.1 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer – 40 cm/s ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm outside the inner tube wall, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for a matched velocity in the inner and outer tubes of 40 cm/s. BURNER 530_1160 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.1 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer – 50 cm/s ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm outside the inner tube wall, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for a matched velocity in the inner and outer tubes of 50 cm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p50,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 43 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1170 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.2 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer 10 cm/s – 0 Degrees ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm; outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90 % of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis, with a zero-degree angular position, that is within 0.5- mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for a matched velocity in the inner and outer tubes of 10 cm/s. BURNER 530_1180 1.4.10, 1.4.10.1 1.4.11 1.4.11.2 Coflow Flow Profile – Inner Boundary Layer 10 cm/s – 45 Degrees ACME shall provide a flow profile of the coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an inner tube boundary layer thickness of less than 0.75mm; outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90 % of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis, with a 45-degree angular position, that is within 0.5-mm downstream of the inner tube outlet;",,False
