PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p57,1,"BURNER 530_1470 1.4.10, 1.4.10.2 1.4.11 1.4.11.3 Coflow Flow Profile – Outer Boundary Layer 30:10 ACME shall provide a coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an outer tube boundary layer thickness of less than 3.0mm outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for velocities, in cm/s, not matched in the inner and outer tubes at 30:10 respectively. BURNER 530_1480 1.4.10, 1.4.10.2 1.4.11 1.4.11.3 Coflow Flow Profile – Outer Boundary Layer 30:50 ACME shall provide a coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an outer tube boundary layer thickness of less than 3.0mm outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for velocities, in cm/s, not matched in the inner and outer tubes at 30:50 respectively.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p58,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 51 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1490 1.4.10, 1.4.10.2 1.4.11 1.4.11.3 Coflow Flow Profile – Outer Boundary Layer 50:10 ACME shall provide a coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an outer tube boundary layer thickness of less than 3.0mm outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for velocities, in cm/s, not matched in the inner and outer tubes at 50:10 respectively. BURNER 530_1500 1.4.10, 1.4.10.2 1.4.11 1.4.11.3 Coflow Flow Profile – Outer Boundary Layer 50:30 ACME shall provide a coflow burner at 1g using a cold flow, with no flame, that has an outer tube boundary layer thickness of less than 3.0mm outside the inner tube, into the annulus, to the position where the axial velocity reaches 90% of the plug flow velocity; across one diameter orthogonal to the burner axis that is within 0.5mm downstream of the inner tube outlet; for velocities, in cm/s, not matched in the inner and outer tubes at 50:30 respectively.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p58,1,"BURNER 530_1510 1.4.12.a Coflow Flame Profile – Edge Axisymmetric – 10 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g such that the variation in radius of the visible flame edge with angular position is less than 10% of the mean radius for all radial positions from the flame base to tip; for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 10 cm/s. BURNER 530_1520 1.4.12.a Coflow Flame Profile – Edge Axisymmetric – 20 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the variation in radius of the visible flame edge with angular position is less than 10% of the mean radius for all radial positions from the flame base to tip; for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 20 cm/s. BURNER 530_1530 1.4.12.a Coflow Flame Profile – Edge Axisymmetric – 30 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the variation in radius of the visible flame edge with angular position is less than 10% of the mean radius for all radial positions from the flame base to tip; for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 30 cm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p59,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 52 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1540 1.4.12.a Coflow Flame Profile – Edge Axisymmetric – 40 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the variation in radius of the visible flame edge with angular position is less than 10% of the mean radius for all radial positions from the flame base to tip; for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 40 cm/s. BURNER 530_1550 1.4.12.a Coflow Flame Profile – Edge Axisymmetric – 50 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the variation in radius of the visible flame edge with angular position is less than 10% of the mean radius for all radial positions from the flame base to tip; for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 50 cm/s. BURNER 530_1560 1.4.12.b Coflow Flame Profile – Base Axisymmetric – 10 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the plane of the flame’s base is orthogonal to the burner axis where the variation in axial distance from the visible flame base to burner outlet, along the circumference of the base, is no more than 1mm for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 10 cm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p59,1,"BURNER 530_1570 1.4.12.b Coflow Flame Profile – Base Axisymmetric – 20 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the plane of the flame’s base is orthogonal to the burner axis where the variation in axial distance from the visible flame base to burner outlet, along the circumference of the base, is no more than 1mm for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 20 cm/s. BURNER 530_1580 1.4.12.b Coflow Flame Profile – Base Axisymmetric – 30 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, with a temperature sensor installed, such that the plane of the flame’s base is orthogonal to the burner axis where the variation in axial distance from the visible flame base to burner outlet, along the circumference of the base, is no more than 1mm for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 30 cm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p60,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 53 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1590 1.4.12.b Coflow Flame Profile – Base Axisymmetric – 40 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, such that the plane of the flame’s base is orthogonal to the burner axis where the variation in axial distance from the visible flame base to burner outlet, along the circumference of the base, is no more than 1mm for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 40 cm/s. BURNER 530_1600 1.4.12.b Coflow Flame Profile – Base Axisymmetric – 50 cm/s ACME shall provide an axisymmetric, 50/50, CH4/N2 flame profile of the coflow burner at 1g, with a temperature sensor installed, such that the plane of the flame’s base is orthogonal to the burner axis where the variation in axial distance from the visible flame base to burner outlet, along the circumference of the base, is no more than 1mm for matched velocities in the inner and outer tubes of 50 cm/s. BURNER 530_1610 1.4.12 Coflow Burner Flame – Axisymmetric Drop Test Matched Velocity 10:50 ACME shall provide coflow burners such that the axisymmetric of a 50/50 CH4/N2 flame shall be demonstrated in drop tests for a limited set of the following conditions: a range of flow velocities in 10 cm/s increments from 10 to 50 cm/s where the inner and outer tube velocities are matched.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p60,1,"BURNER 530_1620 1.4.13, 1.4.13.1 Coflow Burner Coincident ACME shall position co-flow burners such that the supply tube axis is coincident with the CIR chamber axis within ± 2mm, along its length, and orthogonal to the CIR chamber window axes. BURNER 530_1630 1.4.13, 1.4.13.2 Coflow Burner Position ACME shall position the coflow burners such that the tip is within ± 2mm, 12mm upstream from the intersection of the CIR window axes. BURNER 530_1640 1.4.14 Coflow Burner – Inner Tube Material ACME shall provide the coflow burner inner tube fabricated from stainless steel tubing. BURNER 530_1650 1.4.15 Coflow Burner Temperature ACME shall provide the coflow burner capable of withstanding temperatures of 0-1000 degrees Celsius within a 50mm radius of the burner outlet center. 1.5 Burner as Electrode BURNER 530_1660 1.5.1 Gas-Jet Burner as Electrode ACME shall provide each gas-jet burner with a resistance of less than 1 Ohm from the tip to the insulator and across its entire outlet surface.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p61,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 54 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1670 1.5.1 Coflow Burner as Electrode ACME shall provide each coflow burner with a resistance of less than 1 Ohm from the tip to the insulator and across its entire outlet surface. BURNER 530_1680 1.5.2 1.7.5 Gas-Jet Burner – Electrically Insulated The ACME gas-jet burners shall have a resistance of greater than 10 mega Ohms from the burner tip to the burner support with the exception of the return path and the thermocouple. BURNER 530_1690 1.5.2 1.7.5 Coflow Burner – Electrically Insulated ACME shall provide coflow burners that are electrically insulated from any mechanism that supports it within the chamber with the exception of wiring associated with the burner temperature measurement. 1.1 BRE Burner (BRE) BURNER 530_1700 1.13.1 BRE - Outlet Plate ACME shall provide each BRE burner with a circular gas-permeable outlet plate. BURNER 530_1710 1.13.1 BRE - 25mm Burner ACME shall provide a circular BRE burner with a diameter of 25mm ± 1.0mm and is known within ± 0.1mm. BURNER 530_1860 1.13.1 BRE - 25mm Burner Inner wall ACME shall provide a 25mm BRE burner with a housing inner wall diameter of 25mm ± 1mm. BURNER 530_1870 1.13.1 BRE - 50mm Burner ACME shall provide a circular BRE burner with a diameter of 50mm ± 1.0mm and is known within ± 0.1mm.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p61,1,BURNER 530_1880 1.13.1 BRE - 50mm Burner Inner wall ACME shall provide a 50mm BRE burner with a housing inner wall diameter of 50mm ± 1mm. BURNER 530_1890 1.13.2 BRE - Outlet Plate Bevel ACME shall provide each BRE burner with an outlet plate that expands in a bevel from the outlet surface to the outer edge of the burner's cylindrical wall. BURNER 530_1720 1.13.3 BRE - Outlet Plate Orthogonally ACME shall provide each BRE burner with an outlet plate orthogonal to the burner axis ± 0.1mm. BURNER 530_1900 1.13.3 BRE - Outlet Plate Flatness ACME shall provide each BRE burner with an outlet plate flat to within ± 0.1mm. BURNER 530_1730 1.13.4 3.4.1 3.10 BRE - Outlet Plate Thickness ACME shall provide each BRE burner with an outlet plate that is 5.3 ± 0.1mm thick.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p62,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 55 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1910 1.13.4 BRE - Outlet Holes ACME shall provide a BRE burner with an outlet plate with at least 60 holes across the entire outlet surface, with uniform diameters of no more than 1/15th of the burner diameter. BURNER 530_1920 1.13.4 BRE- Outlet Hole Rings ACME shall provide a BRE burner with holes in the outlet plate in a uniform circular arrangement of concentric rings with a constant ring-to-ring spacing and a constant hole-to-hole spacing where the ratio of those two spacing's shall be between 0.5 and 2. BURNER 530_1930 1.13.4 BRE Outlet Hole Size ACME shall provide a BRE burner with holes in the outlet surface where the open area fraction of the holes to the outlet surface is between 0.2 and 0.4. BURNER 530_1940 1.13.4 BRE Inner Hole Pattern Distance ACME shall provide a BRE burner with holes in the outlet where the distance between the burner center and the innermost ring of holes shall be equal to the ring-to-ring spacing. BURNER 530_1950 1.13.4 BRE Outer Hole Pattern Distance ACME shall provide a BRE burner with holes in the outlet where the distance between the outermost ring of holes and the edge of the outlet plate’s surface shall be less than the ring-to-ring spacing and one half that distance.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p62,1,"BURNER 530_1960 1.13.4 BRE Center Heat Flux Sensor Hole ACME shall provide a BRE burner with a hole sized such that gas can flow through an annulus around the center heat flux sensor, where the cross-sectional area of that annulus equals the cross-sectional area of other holes without sensors. BURNER 530_1970 1.13.4 BRE Offset Heat Flux Sensor Hole ACME shall provide a BRE burner with a hole sized such that if the offset heat flux sensor position coincides with an outlet hole the gas can flow through an annulus around the sensor, where the cross-sectional area of that annulus equals the cross-sectional area of the other holes without sensors. BURNER 530_1740 1.13.5 BRE - Outlet Plate Emissivity ACME shall provide a BRE burner with an outlet plate that has an emissivity of 0.75 for 0.6-15 µm. BURNER 530_1750 1.13.6 BRE -Burner Wall Thickness ACME shall provide each BRE burner with a cylindrical wall that is no more than 1mm thick within 25mm of the outlet plate.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p63,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 56 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description BURNER 530_1760 1.13.7 BRE-Honeycomb Cylinder ACME shall provide each BRE burner with a ceramic honeycomb cylinder that is 1 to 2mm upstream of the outlet plate which has open cells that are parallel with the burner axis and fully span the burner cross section. BURNER 530_1980 1.13.7 BRE- Honeycomb Cell Size ACME shall provide each BRE burner with a honeycomb cylinder that has a cross sectional area of each cell that is no more than 2% of the surface area of a hemisphere with a radius equal to the cylinder’s. BURNER 530_1990 1.13.8 BRE - Housing Insulation ACME shall provide a BRE burner that has a thermally insulated outer cylindrical wall from the outlet plate to at least 50mm upstream, with a 6 ± 2mm of insulation with a thermal conductivity of no more than 0.06 W/mK at 260 degreesC (550 degrees F) BURNER 530_1800 1.13.12 1.13.12.1 BRE - Coincidence ACME shall position each BRE burner such that its axis is coincident with the CIR chamber axis ± 2mm. BURNER 530_1810 1.13.12 1.13.12.1 BRE- Orthogonal ACME shall position each BRE burner orthogonal to the CIR chamber window axes. BURNER 530_1820 1.13.12 1.13.12.2 BRE - Position ACME shall position each BRE burner such that the plane of the CIR chamber window centers are 10 ± 2mm downstream of the inner tube outlet.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p63,1,BURNER 530_1830 1.13.13 BRE - Burner Outlet Material ACME shall provide BRE burners with an outlet plate fabricated from copper. BURNER 530_2000 1.13.13 BRE - Burner Wall Material ACME shall provide BRE burners with a cylindrical wall fabricated from stainless. BURNER 530_1840 1.13.14 BRE - Burner Temperature ACME shall provide BRE burners that are capable of withstanding temperatures of 0-400 degrees C within 10mm of the burner outlet with the exception of the heat flux sensors. 1.6 Electrode Mesh E-FIELD 580_0010 1.6.1 Electrode Mesh – Material Dimensions ACME shall provide an electrode mesh that is composed of copper mesh with 16 to 22 wires per 25.4mm (1 inch) with a wire diameter of 0.38 to 0.64mm (0.015 to 0.025 inches). E-FIELD 580_0020 1.6.2 Electrode Mesh – Attached Electrically ACME shall provide the mesh electrode electrically attached to a ring.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p64,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 57 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description E-FIELD 580_0030 1.6.2 Electrode Mesh – Structural Description ACME shall provide the mesh electrode copper ring with a 2 to 3mm cross-sectional diameter with an accuracy of ± 0.2mm. E-FIELD 580_0040 1.6.2 Electrode Mesh – Material Quality ACME shall provide the mesh electrode free of electrical discharge at the maximum system potential. E-FIELD 580_0050 1.6.3 Electrode Mesh – OD ACME shall provide the mesh electrode ring forming the edge with a maximized outer diameter of at least 80 ± 1mm. E-FIELD 580_0060 1.6.3 Electrode Mesh – Burner Distance ACME shall provide the mesh electrode such that the axial distance from the burner tip to the electrode mesh is shorter than the distance between the electrode mesh and any other conductive surface. E-FIELD 580_0070 1.6.4 Electrode Mesh – Axis Centered ACME shall provide the electrode mesh positioned so that its center is on the CIR chamber axis within ± 2mm. E-FIELD 580_0080 1.6.4 Electrode Mesh – Orthogonal Plane ACME shall provide the electrode mesh positioned so that its center is orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis within ± 3 degrees. E-FIELD 580_0090 1.6.5 Electrode Mesh – CIA Orientation Default ACME shall provide the electrode mesh positioned within ± 1mm at a default 25mm downstream of the chamber window axes.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p64,1,E-FIELD 580_0100 1.6.5 Electrode Mesh – CIA Orientation 2 ACME shall provide the electrode mesh positioned within ± 1mm 40mm downstream of the chamber window axes. E-FIELD 580_0110 1.6.6 Electrode Mesh – ORU ACME shall provide the electrode mesh as an ORU and removable from the ACME Chamber Insert Assembly (CIA) during spaceflight. 1.7 Electric Field E-FIELD 580_0120 1.7.1 2.5.1 2.5.4 Electric Field – DC Range ACME shall provide an electric field generator capable of an output of ± 10 kV DC at no load with an equivalent DC output impedance of 50 Mega-ohms. E-FIELD 580_0130 1.7.1 Electric Field – DC Range Accuracy ACME shall provide an electric field generator such that the voltage monitoring signal of the output is within an accuracy of ± 0.12% with a temperature coefficient of± 200 ppm per degree Celsius.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p65,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 58 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description E-FIELD 580_0140 1.7.2 Electric Field – Ramping Stepped Voltage 100V ACME shall provide an electric field with the capability to step the voltage potential of up to 100V. E-FIELD 580_0141 1.7.2 Electric Field – Ramping Stepped Voltage 10kV ACME shall provide an electric field with the capability to step the voltage potential of up to10 kV. E-FIELD 580_0150 1.7.3 Electric Field – Frequency ACME shall provide an electric field with the capability to select the stepped voltage frequency between 0-1 Hertz for the specified voltage range and accuracy. E-FIELD 580_0151 1.7.3 Electric Field- Step Magnitude ACME shall provide an electric field with step magnitudes of no more than 10 kV. E-FIELD 580_0320 1.7.6 Electric Field – Hardware Zone of Exclusion (ZoE) ACME shall provide electric field with a cylindrical zone of exclusion, kept free of any electrically conductive objects during operation of the electric field, which has a 30-mm greater diameter than the electrode mesh and extends from the burner to 20mm downstream of the mesh. E-FIELD 580_0330 1.7.7 Electric Field – Default Current Leakage ACME shall provide an electric field such that the current leakage between the electrode mesh and the burner, measured in air at 1 bar absolute, is less than 100 nanoamps;",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p65,1,"with operational accuracy of ± 1 kV at both -10 kV and +10 kV and with the 35mm default spacing, accurate to ± 2mm. E-FIELD 580_0340 1.7.8 Electric Field – ORU Power Supply 1 ACME shall provide the high voltage power supply 1 as an ORU and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight. E-FIELD 580_0350 1.7.8 Electric Field – ORU Power Supply 2 ACME shall provide the high voltage power supply 2 as an ORU and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight. E-FIELD 580_0360 1.7.8 Electric Field – ORU HV Supply I/F Circuitry ACME shall provide the high voltage supply interface circuitry as an ORU and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight. E-FIELD 580_0370 1.7.8 Electric Field – ORU HV Passive Network ACME shall provide the high voltage passive network as an ORU and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight. 1.1 Ignition",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p66,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 59 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description IGN 540_0010 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 6.4 OD, Position 0 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 6.4mm O.D. tip at position zero, the intersection of the CIR chamber and window axes ± 2mm high and low. IGN 540_0020 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 6.4 OD, Position 30 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 6.4mm O.D. tip at position 30, 30mm ± 2mm upstream of the CIR window axes. IGN 540_0030 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 9.5 OD, Position 0 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 9.5mm O.D. tip at position zero, the intersection of the CIR chamber and window axes ± 2mm. IGN 540_0040 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 9.5 OD, Position 30 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 9.5mm O.D.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p66,1,"tip at position 30, 30mm ± 2mm upstream of the CIR window axes. IGN 540_0050 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 12.7 OD, Position 0 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 12.7mm O.D. tip at position zero, the intersection of the CIR chamber and window axes ± 2mm IGN 540_0060 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Spherical 12.7 OD, Position 30 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the spherical burner with a 12.7mm O.D. tip at position 30, 30mm ± 2mm upstream of the CIR window axes.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p67,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 60 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description IGN 540_0070 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Gas-Jet, Position 10 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the gas-jet burner at position 10, 10mm ± 2mm upstream from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. IGN 540_0080 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Gas-Jet, Position 30 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the gas-jet burner at position 30, 30mm ± 2mm upstream from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. IGN 540_0090 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Coflow, Position 0 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the coflow burner at position zero, the intersection of the CIR chamber and window axes ± 2mm. IGN 540_0100 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability – Coflow, Position 12 ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions in 1g at the limiting conditions in the test matrices within 1 second of igniter activation for the coflow burner at position 12, 12mm ± 2mm upstream from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p67,1,"IGN 540_0101 1.10.1 Ignition Reliability - BRE ACME shall provide an igniter that ignites all initial flow conditions within 1 second of igniter activation for the BRE burner. 1.12 Data Synchronization and Recording CDS 620_0010 1.12.2 Data Recording – Storage for Non-Imaging Duration Default ACME AVP CSCI shall provide data recording storage capacity for 12 mins of simultaneous non- imaging data, such that all non-imaging measurements begin at an uplinked time that is at most 5 minutes prior to ignition and continues to an uplinked time at most 5 minutes after extinction detection unless otherwise noted. CDS 620_0020 1.12.3 Data Recording – Storage for Imaging Duration Default ACME AVP CSCI shall provide up to 4 mins of simultaneous image data recording storage capacity such that all imaging measurements begin at an uplinked time that is at most 1 minute prior to ignition and continues to an uplinked time at most 1 minute after extinction detection. 2.1 Chamber Pressure",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p68,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 61 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS 570_0010 2.1.1 Chamber Pressure – Accuracy ACME shall ensure the absolute chamber pressure is measured with an accuracy of ± 1% of reading. MEAS 570_0020 2.1.2 Chamber Pressure – Range ACME shall ensure the pressure measurement range is 0.1 to 4 bar absolute. MEAS 570_0030 2.1.3 Chamber Pressure – Sampling Frequency ACME shall ensure the chamber pressure is measured at 1 sample per second or faster with a response time of 0.5 second or less. 2.3 Gas Flow Rate FLOW 520_0760 2.3.1 Gas Flow Rate – Accuracy ACME shall provide each gas flow rate measurement with an accuracy of ± 5% of the reading or better. 2.4 Burner Pressure Differential MEAS 570_0060 2.4.1 Burner Pressure Differential Accuracy ACME shall provide the pressure differential between the BRE and spherical burner supply tube inlet and the chamber with accuracy of ± 2 % of the reading. MEAS 570_0070 2.4.1 Burner Pressure Differential – Orientation ACME shall provide the pressure differential for the BRE and spherical burner measured downstream of any valves. MEAS 570_0080 2.4.2 Burner Pressure Differential – Range ACME shall provide a pressure differential measurement range for the spherical burner that is from 0.1 to 1.5 times the pressure drop across the spherical burner at a flow rate of 5 slpm, on a N2 basis, in cold flow testing (i.e., with no flame).",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p68,1,"2.5 Electric Potential E-FIELD 580_0380 2.5.1, 2.5.4 Electric Potential – Accuracy ACME shall provide electric potential measurement between the mesh electrode and the high voltage (HV) ground terminal to an accuracy of within the larger of 20 VDC or ± 1% of the reading. E-FIELD 580_0390 2.5.2 Electric Potential – Range ACME shall provide an electric potential measurement range of ± 10 kilovolts. 3.1 ACME Analog Camera OpsCam 550_0010 3.1.1 Analog Camera – Wavelength Response ACME shall provide a wavelength response of 400 to 700 nanometers. OpsCam 550_0020 3.1.2 Analog Camera – Focusing ACME shall focus the analog camera on the CIR chamber axis where the Field of View (FOV) plane includes the CIR chamber axis.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p69,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 62 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description OpsCam 550_0030 3.1.3 Analog Camera – FOV ACME shall provide an analog camera FOV of at least a 90mm diameter circle centered on the intersection of the CIR window axes. OpsCam 550_0040 3.1.4 Analog Camera – Adjustable Settings ACME shall provide the analog camera with the ability to adjust at least the gain (or iris) setting. OpsCam 550_0070 3.1.5 Analog Camera – Frame Rate ACME shall provide the analog camera with a minimum of 25 frames per second. OpsCam 550_0080 3.1.6 Analog Camera – Near-Real Time Downlink ACME shall provide the analog camera with near real-time downlink. OpsCam 550_0110 3.1.7 Analog Camera– ORU ACME shall provide the analog camera system as an ORU. OpsCam 550_0120 3.1.8 Analog Camera – Illumination ACME shall provide analog camera system with a white light source for illuminating the imaging views before, during, or after tests. 3.2 ACME Data Camera DataCam 310_0010 3.2.1 Data Camera – Spectral Range ACME shall provide a data camera with a wavelength response of 400 to 700 nanometers. DataCam 310_0020 3.2.2 Data Camera – Sensitivity ACME shall provide a data camera with a sensitivity, especially to dim blue light at 431 nanometers, matching or exceeding cameras equipped with a Sony ICX285 2/3” Progressive scan CCD.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p69,1,DataCam 310_0030 3.2.3 Data Camera – f-number ACME shall provide a data camera lens with an f- number of no more than f2.8 and as small as possible. DataCam 310_0040 3.2.4 3.2.4.1 Data Camera – Spatial Resolution ACME shall provide a data camera with a spatial resolution at the focal plane is 0.2% or less of the corresponding FOV dimension; when simultaneously imaging at its maximum framing rate with full sensor. DataCam 310_0050 3.2.4 3.2.4.2 Data Camera – Bit Depth ACME shall provide a data camera with a bit depth of at least 3x12; when simultaneously imaging at its maximum framing rate with full sensor. DataCam 310_0060 3.2.5 Data Camera – Focusing ACME shall provide data camera that is focused on the CIR chamber axis. DataCam 310_0070 3.2.6 3.2.10 Data Camera – FOV Centered ACME shall provide a data camera with a FOV for each imaging system centered on and perpendicular to a CIR window axis.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p70,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 63 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DataCam 310_0080 3.2.7 3.2.10 Data Camera – FOV Spherical Flames ACME shall provide a data camera with a FOV of at least 90mm in diameter for the spherical and BRE flames. DataCam 310_0090 3.2.8 3.2.10 Data Camera – FOV Gas-Jet & Coflow Flames ACME shall provide a data camera with a FOV of 35mm along the chamber axis and at least 20mm orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis for the gas-jet and coflow flames. DataCam 310_100 3.2.9 3.2.10 Data Camera FOV – Rectangular FOV ACME shall provide a data camera with the long dimension of the FOV aligned with the chamber axis, if the FOV is rectangular. DataCam 310_0120 3.2.11 Data Camera – Filter Option ACME shall provide the capability to utilize an optical filter with data color imaging system. DataCam 310_0140 3.2.11 Data Camera – BG7 Filter ACME shall provide a BG7 Schott glass filter with a transmittance from 400-700 nm matching within ± 5% of 1mm thickness for the data color camera. DataCam 310_0141 3.2.11 Data Camera - Band Pass Filter 1 ACME shall provide a 430 nm band pass filter with transmission curves that match within ± 5% of transmittance data for a 10nm full width at half maximum transmission.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p70,1,"DataCam 310_0142 3.2.11 Data Camera - Band Pass Filter 2 ACME shall provide a 450 nm band pass filter with transmission curves that match within ± 5% of Thorlab transmittance data for a 10nm full width at half maximum transmission (FWHM.) DataCam 310_0143 3.2.11 Data Camera - Filter Position ACME shall provide a filter barrel with filter positions 0-3 as empty, BG7, 430nm, and 450nm. DataCam 310_0150 3.2.12 Data Camera – Frame Rate ACME data camera shall provide 20 frames/s or faster when imaging the full sensor at a bit depth of at least 3x12. DataCam 310_0160 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings Bit Depth ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the bit depth settings of the data camera between tests prior to ignition. DataCam 310_0190 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings, Gain ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the gain settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control. DataCam 310_0220 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings Iris ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the iris settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control. DataCam 310_0250 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings, Exposure Time ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the exposure time settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p71,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 64 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DataCam 310_0280 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings, Framing Rate ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the framing rate settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control. DataCam 310_0310 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings, Binning ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the binning settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control. DataCam 310_0340 3.2.13 Data Camera – Adjustable Settings, Region Of Interest (ROI) ACME data camera shall provide the ability to adjust the Region Of Interest (ROI) settings between tests prior to ignition via uplink control. DataCam 310_0470 3.2.15 Data Color Imaging – ORU ACME shall provide the data color imaging system(s) as an ORU and removable from the Optics Bench UML during spaceflight. 3.4 Burner Temperature Measurement MEAS 570_0120 3.4.1.1 Spherical Temperature – Location ACME shall provide spherical burner surface temperature measurement at a location between 20 degrees and 90 degrees of the burner tube. MEAS 570_0130 3.4.1.1 Spherical Temperature – Probe Non-Visible The ACME burner design shall ensure the probe is not visible during mission science in at least one view of the data color imaging.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p71,1,"MEAS 570_0150 3.4.1.2 Gas-Jet Surface Temperature – Location ACME shall provide a gas-jet burner surface temperature measurements on the exterior surface of the burner as close as possible to its outlet tip where the measurement device does not disturb the axisymmetric of the flow and flame. MEAS 570_0170 3.4.1.4 Burner Temperature – Probe Size ACME shall provide temperature measurements of all burner types such that, if a probe used, it is smaller than 250 microns in thickness. MEAS 570_0180 3.4.1.5 Burner Temperature – Accuracy ACME shall provide temperature measurements, of all burner types, with a precision of ± 2 degrees Celsius and an accuracy of ± 5 degrees Celsius. MEAS 570_0190 3.4.1.6 Gas-Jet Temperature – Range ACME shall provide a temperature measurement with a range of 0 to 300 degrees Celsius for the gas-jet burner. MEAS 570_0200 3.4.1.7 Spherical Temperature – Range ACME shall provide a spherical burner surface temperature measurement range of 0 to 700 degrees Celsius.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p72,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 65 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS 570_0201 3.4.1.9 BRE Temperature Measurements - Heat Flux Location ACME shall provide a BRE burner outlet surface temperature measurements at both heat flux measurement locations. MEAS 570_0202 3.4.1.9 BRE Temperature Measurements - Additional Locations - 25mm Burner ACME shall provide an additional BRE burner outlet surface temperature measurements not in an outlet hole and at 180 degrees from the offset heat flux sensor at radial positions of 5 ± 0.5mm and 10 ± 0.5mm for the 25mm burner. MEAS 570_0203 3.4.1.9 BRE Temperature Measurements - Additional Locations - 50mm Burner ACME shall provide an additional BRE burner outlet surface temperature measurements not in an outlet hole and at 180 degrees from the offset heat flux sensor at radial positions of 5 ± 0.5mm and 15 ± 0.5mm for the 50mm burner. MEAS 570_0204 3.4.1.10 BRE Temperature Measurements - Probe ACME shall provide temperature measurement probes that are .3mm in diameter or less that are thermally bonded to the burner outlet plate. MEAS 570_0205 3.4.1.11 BRE - Temperature Range ACME shall provide a BRE burner surface temperature measurement range of 0 to 500 degrees Celsius.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p72,1,"3.4.3 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature DIAG 560_0010 3.4.3.2 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature ACME shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements made simultaneously on 5 or more lines spaced 5mm ± 0.5mm apart from neighboring lines. DIAG 560_0020 3.4.3.3 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – TFP Reposition Between tests ACME shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements with the ability to reposition the measurement lines or fibers between tests to uplinked positions. DIAG 560_0030 3.4.3.3 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – TFP Reposition During Tests ACME shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements with the ability to reposition the measurement lines, or fibers, during tests to uplinked positions. DIAG 560_0060 3.4.3.3 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Axial Position ACME shall provide the ability to move the axial position along its length of a TFP fiber relative to the burner as a function of time within ± 1mm.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p73,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 66 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG 560_0090 3.4.3.4 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Fiber Retractable ACME shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements where the fibers, if used, shall be retractable with minimal disturbance to beyond 100mm from the burner. DIAG 560_0110 3.4.3.4 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Fiber Removable ACME shall provide the TFP fiber array fully removable for replacement. DIAG 560_0130 3.4.3.9 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Fiber Orientation 1 ACME shall provide fiber orientation such that they intersect with and are orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis. DIAG 560_0150 3.4.3.9 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Fiber Orientation 2 ACME shall provide fiber orientation such that they are orthogonal, with a tolerance of ± 25 degrees, to the line of sight of the corresponding imaging system. DIAG 560_0160 3.4.3.13 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – TFP Fibers as ORU ACME shall provide the fibers mounted within ORU(s) and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight, if the hot soot-free region temperature measurement is made by TFP.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p73,1,"3.4.4 Far-Field Temperature Measurement MEAS 570_0230 3.4.4.1, 3.4.4.2 Far-Field Temperature – Avoidance Region ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements along unobstructed lines passing through the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes that avoid the region within 20 degrees of the burner supply tube. MEAS 570_0240 3.4.4.3 Far-Field Temperature – Near Radial Array ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements from at least the following radial locations measured in mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 13, 25, 50, 100, 200, and 200 in a direction orthogonal to the other 200mm position (when the intersection of the CIR window axes is considered the origin of the two rays.)",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p74,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 67 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS 570_0250 3.4.4.4 Far-Field Temperature – Distant Radial Array ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements from at least the following radial locations measured in mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 45, 60, 100, 100 (in a direction orthogonal to the other like- distance position, when the intersection of the CIR window axes is considered the origin of the two rays), 200, 200 (in a direction orthogonal to the other like-distance position, when the intersection of the CIR window axes is considered the origin of the two rays.) MEAS 570_0260 3.4.4.5 Far-Field Temperature – Positioning Accuracy ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements with each position known in three dimensions to within ± 3mm or less. MEAS 570_0270 3.4.4.6 Far-Field Temperature – Range Inside 40-mm ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements in the range of 700-1700 degrees Celsius for the ""near"" radial array for positions inside 40mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 13 and 25mm. MEAS 570_0280 3.4.4.6 Far-Field Temperature – Range Outside 40- mm ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements in the range of 0-1250 degrees Celsius for each radial array for positions outside of 40mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 45, 60, 100, and 200mm.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p74,1,"MEAS 570_0290 3.4.4.7 Far-Field Temperature – Sensor Precision Inside 40-mm ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements such that the temperature sensors have precisions for each radial array of ± 1.2C for the positions inside 40mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 13 and 25mm. MEAS 570_0300 3.4.4.7 Far-Field Temperature – Sensor Precision Outside 40-mm ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements such that the temperature sensors have precisions for each radial array of ± 1.2C for the positions outside 40mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes: 45, 50, 60, 100, and 200mm. MEAS 570_0330 3.4.4.9 Far-Field Temperature Measurement – ZOE ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements with a cylindrical zone of exclusion with a diameter of 50mm and maximized extending from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes to 10mm beyond each temperature measurement position.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p75,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 68 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS 570_0350 3.4.4.10 Far-Field Temperature Measurement – TC Probe Parallel ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements such that if thermocouples are used, each probe (including the junction) shall be within 10 degrees of parallel to a ray from the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes to the temperature measurement position to a distance of at least 100mm from the intersection of the CIR chamber windows. MEAS 570_0360 3.4.4.11 Far-Field Temperature Measurement – TC Probe OD ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements such that each probe within a radial distance of 100mm shall have an outer diameter limit of the following or smaller: 0.2mm within 5mm of the measurement position; 2mm within 20mm of the measurement position; 3.5mm within 50mm of the measurement position. MEAS 570_0370 3.4.4.12 Far-Field Temperature Measurement – ORU ACME shall provide far-field temperature measurements such that the sensors within 100mm of the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes that are ORU's 3.6 Radiant Emission Measurement DIAG 560_0180 3.6.2 Radiant Emission – Minimum FOV ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements such that the minimum region for each measurement is at least a 120-mm diameter FOV at the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p75,1,"DIAG 560_0190 3.6.3 Radiant Emission – Orthogonal FOV Array ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements with a linear array of five measurements made where the view from each detector is equidistant from and orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis within ± 3 degrees. DIAG 560_0200 3.6.3 Radiant Emission – Orthogonal Centered FOV ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements with one of five's FOV is centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. DIAG 560_0210 3.6.3 Radiant Emission – Orthogonal Uniform FOVs ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements where four of five FOVs are positioned uniformly, with equal spacing of no more than 30mm ± 1mm, across a span of at least 60mm ± 1mm in each direction.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p76,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 69 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG 560_0220 3.6.4 Radiant Emission – Non-Orthogonal, Additional FOV ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements where one additional FOV is also made at angle(s) other than orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis for a FOV centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. DIAG 560_0230 3.6.4 Radiant Emission – Non-Orthogonal, Additional FOV Downstream ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements where the additional measurement, non-orthogonal to the chamber axis, are uniformly spaced in an angle relative to the orthogonal direction, and cover a span from orthogonal to at least 60 degrees ± 2 degrees downstream, of the burners. DIAG 560_0240 3.6.5 Radiant Emission – Spectral Range ACME shall provide flame radiant emissions measurements where the detector has a spectral range of 0.2 to 11 microns and an irradiance range of 0.0001-0.1 W/cm2. DIAG 560_0241 3.6.8 Radiant Emissions - BRE ACME shall provide one primary and two or more secondary radiant flame emissions for BRE burner tests. DIAG 560_0242 3.6.8 Radiant Emission - BRE FOV Size ACME shall provide a field of view for the BRE radiant emission measurements that fully includes a cylindrical zone downstream of the burner surface that is 50mm in diameter by 50mm in length.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p76,1,DIAG 560_0243 3.6.8 Radiant Emission - BRE FOV Position ACME shall provide a cylindrical field of view for BRE radiant emission measurements that is aligned with the chamber and BRE burner axis. DIAG 560_0244 3.6.8 Radiant Emission - BRE FOV Shape ACME shall provide a conical field of view for each radiant emission measurement that have the same angle between the field of view edges and a plane passing through each measurements center axis. DIAG 560_0510 3.6.8 Radiant Emission -BRE Burner Exclusion From Primary ACME shall provide a primary radiant emission measurement that blocks the BRE burner from the FOV with a blocked thickness of the cylindrical zone of less than 5mm when measured parallel with the burner axis. DIAG 560_0520 3.6.8 Radiant Emission - BRE Burner Exclusion of Lense ACME shall not use lenses on the radiant emission measurements to form the field of view.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p77,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 70 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG 560_0530 3.6.8 Radiant Emission - BRE Burner Identical ACME shall use identical sensors for all radiant emission measurements. 3.7 Chemiluminescent Emission Measurement DIAG 560_0290 3.7.2 Chemiluminescent Emission – Simultaneous ACME shall provide simultaneous chemiluminescent emissions measurements at 310 and 431 nanometers with a 10 nanometer or larger FWHM, and broadband from 300 to 600 nanometers. DIAG 560_0300 3.7.3 Chemiluminescent Emission – Minimum FOV ACME shall provide chemiluminescent emissions measurements with a 120mm diameter FOV, centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. DIAG 560_0310 3.7.4 Chemiluminescent Emission – Sensitivity ACME shall provide chemiluminescent emissions measurements with a typical Radiant Sensitivity of at least 40 mA/W (as measured at the peak sensitivity wavelength.) DIAG 560_0340 3.7.6 Chemiluminescent Emission – ORU ACME shall provide chemiluminescent emissions sensors as ORU(s) and removable from the ACME CIA during spaceflight. 3.8 Ion Current Measurement E-FIELD 580_0430 3.8.1, 3.8.2, 3.8.3 Ion Current Range ACME shall provide measurements of ion current produced between the burner and mesh electrode where it's amplitude is over a range of at least 0 to 25 micro amps with an error of no more than the larger of ± 5% of the reading or ± 0.05 micro amps.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p77,1,MEAS 3.1 Heat Flux (BRE burner tests only) MEAS 570_1050 3.10.1 1.13.12 Heat Flux - Sensor ACME shall provide heat flux measurements at the outlet of the BRE burner using a Schmidt- Boelter thermopile type heat flux transducer. MEAS 570_1060 3.10.2 1.13.12 Heat Flux - 25mm Burner Center ACME shall take a heat flux measurement at the center ± 0.1mm of the 25mm BRE burner. MEAS 570_1070 3.10.2 1.13.12 Heat Flux - 50mm Burner Center ACME shall take a heat flux measurement at the center ± 0.1mm of the 50mm BRE burner. MEAS 570_1080 3.10.2 1.13.12 Heat Flux 25mm Burner Offset ACME shall take a heat flux measurement at a position with an offset radius of 10mm ± 0.1mm for the 25mm BRE burner. MEAS 570_1090 3.10.2 1.13.12 Heat Flux 50mm Burner Offset ACME shall take a heat flux measurement at a position with an offset radius of 15mm ± 0.1mm for the 50mm BRE burner.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p78,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 71 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS 570_1200 3.10.3 Heat Flux - Relative Size ACME shall provide heat flux sensors that have a diameter of less than 10% of the BRE burner's outlet surface. MEAS 570_1210 3.10.4 Heat Flux - Orientation ACME shall provide downstream facing heat flux sensors that are flush with the BRE burner outlet surface ± 0.05mm. MEAS 570_1220 3.10.4 Heat Flux - Flush Mount ACME shall provide heat flux sensors that are flush with the BRE burner outlet surface ± 0.05mm. MEAS 570_1230 3.10.5 Heat Flux - FOV ACME shall provide heat flux sensors that have no restrictions to their fields of view, geometrically by the burner. MEAS 570_1240 3.10.6 Heat Flux - Emissivity ACME shall provide heat flux sensors whose surface has an emissivity of .93 for a range of 0.6-15 microns. MEAS 570_1250 3.10.7 Heat Flux - Range ACME shall provide a heat flux measurement range of 0-50 kW/m2. MEAS 570_1260 3.10.8 Heat Flux - Precision ACME shall provide heat flux measurements with a precision of ± 1%. MEAS 570_1270 3.10.8 Heat Flux - Accuracy ACME shall provide heat flux measurements with an accuracy of ± 5% of full scale. MEAS 570_1340 3.10.9 3.10.7 Heat Flux - Measurement ACME shall provide a BRE burner where the heat flux measurements remain within 0-50 kW/m2.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p79,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 72 of 117 8.0 ACME OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENTS This section specifies operational requirements needed to support the training, testing, operations, design and development of ACME. This section specifies requirements needed to support the training, testing, operations, design and development of ACME. Table 8-1—Operational Requirements System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description 1.0 [CIR & ACME] General OPS OPS 603_0010 1.1 OPS - Flexible Control ACME shall provide flexible experiment control based on explicit functions which can be selected, repeated as needed, and ordered to create a variety of overall experiment sequences. OPS 603_0020 1.2 OPS - Console Methods ACME shall be capable of operations by all of the following methods: 1) automated software control, 2) operator control 3) mix of automated and operator control. OPS 603_0030 1.3 OPS - Varied Duration S/W Sequencing ACME shall provide for automated software control through sequences of commands that are each either instant, or timed with a variable duration that is a parameter of that function. OPS 603_0040 1.4 1.5 OPS - Extensible Interface ACME shall be capable of software upgrades. OPS 613_0140 1.12.7 1.6 OPS - Independent Functions and Status Monitoring ACME shall be capable of handling new commands while simultaneously: (1) acquiring imaging and non-imaging data. (2) flowing gas. (3) illuminating the chamber.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p79,1,"(4) projecting light from the CIR illumination package. (5) energizing the electric field. (6) sensing for flame extinction. OPS 603_0060 1.7 Command Time Log ACME shall provide a detailed time log of commands issued for each test conducted. 2.0 [CIR & ACME] Pause Functions OPS 603_0070 2.1 OPS - Automated Pausing ACME shall be capable of pausing for a duration of 0.01 to 999.0s with a precision of 0.01 s or less between functions. OPS 603_0080 2.2 OPS - Manual Pausing ACME shall be capable of pausing for a specified duration between functions, where it shall be possible to specify a duration in the range of at least 10 s to 99 minutes, with an uncertainty of no more than the larger of 1) 5 s 2)10% of the duration. 3.0 [CIR & ACME] Hardware Set Up Functions",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p80,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 73 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description OPS 503_0190 3.1 OPS Crew - External ORU Swap ACME shall be capable of installing/removing the following hardware at specified positions external to the CIR chamber: 1) ACME avionics package 2) GCIP 3) CIR and ACME imaging packages 4) IPSUs 5) CIR illumination package 6) gas bottles 7) filter cartridge. OPS 503_0200 3.2 OPS Crew - Internal ORU Swap ACME shall be capable of installing/removing the following hardware at specified positions on the ACME chamber insert assembly: 1) burner 2) igniter tip 3) electric field components 4) mass flow controllers 5) Thin Filament Pyrometry (TFP) fiber array 6) far-field thermocouple array 7) Photomultiplier Tube (PMT) array. OPS 503_0210 3.3 OPS Crew- Soot Clean Off ACME shall be capable of cleaning the soot off of gas-jet burners. 4.0 [CIR] Chamber Ops Functions OPS 523_0850 1.11.1 4.1 OPS - Venting to Specified Pressure ACME shall be capable of venting the CIR chamber atmosphere to a specified pressure within a range of 0.01 to 3 bar, with an uncertainty of no more than the greater of 0.01 bar or 1% of the specified pressure. OPS 503_0220 1.11.1 4.2 OPS - Scrubbing CIR Atmosphere ACME shall be capable of activating/deactivating scrubbing for the CIR chamber atmosphere. OPS 573_0390 4.3 OPS - CIR Chamber Sealed ACME shall be capable of verifying that the CIR chamber is sealed.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p80,1,OPS 523_0860 1.11.1 1.11.4 4.4 OPS - Filling Chamber ACME shall be capable of adding a specified gas to the CIR chamber to a specific pressure with a precision that meets the composition and pressure requirements documented in ISRD 1.11.1 and 1.11.4. OPS 503_0230 1.11.2 1.11.3 4.5 OPS - Chamber Fan ACME shall be capable of activating and deactivating the CIR chamber fan. OPS 573_0400 3.9.1 4.6 OPS - GCIP ACME shall be capable of providing species concentration measurements of the chamber atmosphere through operating the GCIP. 5.0 [CIR & ACME] Initiation & Shut Down Functions,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p81,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 74 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description OPS 523_0870 1.9.3 1.9.4 2.3.1 5.1 Powering Ops ACME OPS shall be capable of independently powering- up, in advance of operation. OPS 313_0480 3.2.11 5.2 OPS - Camera Filter ACME shall be capable of inserting and removing optical filters from the ACME data analysis camera. OPS 553_0150 3.00 5.3 OPS - Camera Setting - Analog Camera Gain ACME shall be capable of configuring the CIR camera settings for Gain. OPS 603_0090 1.12.2 1.12.7 5.4 OPS - Non-Imaging Recording ACME shall be capable of starting and stopping non- imaging data acquisition 5 minutes in advance of ignition and after extinction for: (1) Chamber pressure (2) Gas flow rates (3) Burner pressure differential – only required for spherical flame tests (4) Electric potential – for E-FIELD Flames tests only (5) Acceleration – whenever SAMS is available (6) Temperature: burner (7) Temperature: hot soot-containing regions AND/OR hot soot-free regions (8) Temperature: far-field – except for E-FIELD Flames tests (9) Soot volume fraction (10) Radiant emission (11) Chemiluminescent emission (12) Ion current – for E-FIELD Flames only. (13) Heat Flux - Only for BRE Burner tests OPS 603_0100 1.12.3 1.12.7 5.5 OPS - Imaging Record Start ACME shall be capable of starting and stopping imaging data acquisition 1 minute prior to ignition and after extinction for:",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p81,1,"(1) Color imaging for operations (2) Color imaging for data analysis (3) Ultraviolet (UV) imaging, 6.0 [ACME] Chamber Illumination Functions OPS 553_0160 3.1.8 6.1 OPS - Illumination On/Off ACME shall be capable of activating and deactivating the chamber illumination system. OPS 553_0170 3.1.8 6.2 OPS - Illumination Timing ACME OPS shall be capable of activating any bank of chamber lights for a duration of 0.03 to 999.99s with a precision of 0.01 s and then deactivating those same bank of chamber lights. OPS 553_0180 3.1.8 6.3 OPS - Illumination Flashing ACME OPS shall be capable of activating any bank of chamber lights for a duration of 0.03 to 999.99s with a precision of 0.01 s and then deactivating the same bank of chamber lights for a duration of 0.03 to 999.99s with a precision of 0.01 s for 1 to 9,999 cycles.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p82,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 75 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description 7.0 [CIR] Illumination Package Functions OPS 323_0040 3.5.4 3.5.6 7.1 OPS - CIR Illumination On ACME shall be capable of activating the CIR illumination package at a specified intensity. OPS 323_0050 3.5.4 3.5.6 7.2 OPS - CIR Active Illumination Adjust ACME shall be capable of adjusting the intensity of the illumination while the illumination package is activated. OPS 323_0060 3.5.4 3.5.6 7.3 OPS - Illumination Off ACME shall be capable of deactivating the CIR illumination package. 8.0 [ACME] Ignition Functions OPS 543_0200 1.10.2 8.1 OPS - Specifying Igniter Speed ACME shall be capable of translating the igniter at a rate of 0.0 to 50.0 mm/s with an uncertainty of less than 0.1 mm/s. OPS 503_0240 1.11.8 1.11.9 8.1 OPS - Specifying Igniter Position ACME OPS shall be capable of translating the igniter to a specified position with a precision of 1mm and over a range extending nominally from the burner tip to at least beyond the zone of exclusion. OPS 543_0210 1.10.2 1.10.3 1.10.4 8.2 OPS - Specifying Ignition Energizing Voltage ACME OPS shall be capable of energizing the igniter at a voltage of 50 to 100% of max power with a precision of 2%. OPS 543_0220 8.2 OPS - Specifying Ignition Energizing Duration ACME shall be capable of energizing the igniter for a duration of 0 to 10s with a precision of 0.1s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p82,1,9.0 [CIR & ACME] Flow Control Functions OPS 523_0880 1.9.3 1.9.4 2.3.1 9.1 OPS - MFCs Zeroing ACME shall be capable of zeroing all ACME MFCs. OPS 523_0890 9.2 OPS - Venting Gas Lines ACME shall be capable of venting all or a subset of the gas delivery lines. OPS 523_0900 9.3 OPS - Purging Gas Delivery Lines ACME shall be capable of purging all or a subset of the gas delivery lines with the gases with which those lines are currently connected. OPS 523_0910 1.9.4 9.4 OPS - Setting CIR MFCs ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of CIR MFCs for specified steady flow rates within a range of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% or less. OPS 523_0920 1.9.4 9.5 OPS - Setting ACME MFCs ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of ACME MFCs for specified steady flow rates within a range of 0 to 100% and a precision of .01% or less. OPS 523_0930 1.9.4 9.6 OPS - ACME Flows - Step ACME OPS shall be capable of setting all or a subset of ACME flows to: 1) step upward and/or downward by specified values and,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p83,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 76 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description 2) pausing to hold all flows steady for a specified wait duration with a precision of 0.1 s or less for a specified number of cycles ranging from at least 1 to 999. OPS 523_0940 1.9.4 9.7 OPS - ACME Flows - Linear Ramp ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of ACME flows to: 1) linearly ramp upward/downward by values of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% for a duration of 0.1 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1s. 2) and pausing with all flows held steady for a wait duration with a precision of 0.1 s or less. OPS 523_0950 1.9.4 9.8 OPS - ACME Flows - Step - A &B Values ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of the flows to: 1) step upward/downward by a value of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% 2) pausing with all flows held steady for a duration of 0.1 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1s. 3) stepping the flows downward/upward by a value of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1%. 4) pausing with all flows held steady for a duration with a precision of 0.1s. OPS 523_0960 1.9.4 9.9 OPS - ACME Flows - Ramp - A&B Values ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of ACME flows to: 1) ramp upward/downward by a value of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% duration of 0.1 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1 s. 2) pausing with all flows held steady for a duration of 0.0 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1 s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p83,1,3) ramping the flow downward/upward by a value of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% for a duration of 0.1 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1s. 4) pausing with all flows held steady for a duration of 0.0 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1s for 1 to 999 cycles. OPS 523_0970 1.9.4 9.10 OPS - SV Control (CIR/ACME) ACME OPS shall be capable of opening and closing the CIR and ACME solenoid valves. OPS 523_0980 1.9.4 9.11 OPS - SV Control (ACME) ACME OPS shall be capable of opening and closing all ACME solenoid valves or any specified subset thereof. 10.0 [ACME] TFP Pyrometry Functions OPS 563_0280 1.11.8 1.11.9 10.1 OPS - TFP Positioning - Operational Range ACME shall be capable of translating the TFP fiber array at,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p84,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 77 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description 3.4.3.3 3.4.3.4 a specified rate of 100 mm/s or greater, with an uncertainty of 0.1 mm/s or less, to a position within its operational range. OPS 563_0290 1.11.8 1.11.9 3.4.3.3 10.2 OPS - TFP Positioning - Specified Rate ACME shall be capable of 1) translating the TFP fiber array upward and/or downward at a specified rate to a position within its operational range. 2) pausing for a specified wait duration with a precision of 0.01 s or less and within a range of 0.00 to 999.99 s for a specified number of cycles ranging from 1 to 999. OPS 563_0300 3.4.3.3 10.3 OPS - TFP Positioning - Ramp up ACME shall be capable of 1) translating the TFP fiber array upward at a specified ramp-up value. 2) pausing for a specified high-position duration with a precision of 0.01 s or less, and within a range of at least 0.00 to 99.9 s 3) ramping the TFP fiber array downward by a specified ramp-down values as high as 100 mm/s with an uncertainty of no more than 0.1 mm/s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p84,1,"4) pausing for a specified low-position duration with a precision of 0.01 s or less, and within a range of at least 0.00 to 99.99 s for a specified number of cycles (1-999) 11.0 [ACME] Electric Field Functions OPS 583_0470 1.7.1 1.7.4 11.1 OPS - E-Field - Activate ACME shall be capable of activating the electric field at the specified polarity (positive or negative) and voltage with a precision and range at least meeting ISRD 1.7.1. OPS 583_0480 1.7.1 1.7.4 11.2 OPS - E-Field - Step Change ACME shall be capable of setting the electric field potential, by a step change by adjusting the polarity and voltage of the electric field with a precision and range outlined in ISRD 1.7.1. OPS 583_0490 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.3 OPS - E-Field - Deactivate ACME shall be capable of deactivating the electric field. OPS 583_0500 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.4 OPS - E-Field - Stepping Voltage ACME shall be capable of 1) stepping the electric field voltage upward and/or downward by a specified value outlined in ISRD 1.7.1 2) pausing with the voltage held steady for a wait duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.005 s or less for 1 to 9,999 cycles. OPS 583_0510 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.5 OPS - E-Field - Ramping Voltage ACME shall be capable of 1) ramping the electric field voltage upward and/or",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p85,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 78 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description downward at a specified step size outlined in ISRD 1.7.1 for a ramp duration of 0.005 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.01s. 2) pausing with the voltage held steady for a wait duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.01s for 1 to 9,999 cycles. OPS 583_0520 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.3 1.7.4 11.6 OPS - E-Field - Rectangular Wave ACME shall be capable of 1) stepping the electric field voltage upward by specified step-up values outlined in ISRD 1.7.1. 2) pausing with the voltage held steady for a duration of 0.005 to 999.999s and a precision of 0.005 s 3) stepping the voltage downward by a specified step- down value outlined in ISRD 1.7.1. 4) pausing with the voltage held steady for a duration of 0.005 to 999.999s and a precision of 0.005 for 1 to 9,999 cycles. OPS 583_0530 1.7.1 1.7.3 1.7.4 11.7 OPS - E-Field - Triangular Wave ACME shall be capable of 1) ramping the electric field voltage upward by a ramp size outlined in ISRD 1.7.1 for a duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.005s. 2) pausing with the voltage held steady for a duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.005s 3) ramping the electric field voltage downward by a ramp- down size outlined in ISRD 1.7.1 for a duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.005s.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p85,1,"4) pausing with the voltage held steady for a duration of 0.000 to 999.999s with a precision of 0.005 s for 1 to 9,999 cycles 12.0 [ACME] Extinction Functions OPS 563_0310 3.7.1 12.1 OPS - Flame Extinction - Detection ACME shall be capable of detecting flame extinction after ignition, by monitoring one or more non-imaging instruments and verifying that averaged measurements over a duration of 0.0 to 99.9s with a precision of 0.1s are below specified values OPS 563_0540 3.7.1 12.1 OPS - Flame Extinction - Detection Selection ACME shall be capable of specifying whether 1) any specified measurement indicates extinction. 2) half of the specified measurements indicate extinction. 3) all specified measurements indicate extinction.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p86,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 79 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG 560_0280 3.7.1 Chemiluminescent Emission – Flame Extinction ACME shall provide chemiluminescent emissions measurements where flame extinction is detected. OPS 523_0990 1.9.4 3.7.1 12.2 OPS - Flame Extinction- Gas Flow Shutoff ACME shall be capable of setting all gas flows to zero in response to extinction detection after a duration of 0.0 to 99.99s with a precision of 0.1s. OPS 523_1000 1.9.4 3.7.1 12.3 OPS - Flame Extinction - Single Step Flow ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of flows in response to extinction detection to step upward/downward 0 to 100% with a precision of .01% OPS 523_1010 1.9.4 3.7.1 12.4 OPS - Flame Extinction - Single Ramp Flow ACME shall be capable of setting any flows within a range of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% In response to extinction detection, for a ramp duration of 0.1 to 999.9s with a precision of 0.1s and holding the flows at their new values. OPS 523_1020 1.9.4 3.7.1 12.5 OPS - Flame Extinction - Stepping Flow ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of flows to 1)step upward and/or downward In response to extinction detection by a range of 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1%.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p86,1,"2) pausing with all flows held steady for duration of 0.0 to 99.9s with a precision of 0.1 s and then setting all gas flows to zero. OPS 523_1030 1.9.4 3.7.1 12.6 OPS - Flame Extinction - Ramping Flow ACME shall be capable of setting all or a subset of flows to: 1) ramp upward/downward in response to extinction detection by 0 to 100% and a precision of 0.1% over a duration of 0 to 99.9s with a precision of 0.1 s. 2) pausing with all flows held steady for a duration of 0 to 99.9s with a precision of 0.1s and then setting all gas flows to zero. OPS 563_1040 3.7.1 12.7 OPS - Flame Extinction - Shutoff ACME shall be capable of deactivating extinction detection. 3.1 [ACME] Heat Flux (BRE burner tests only) BURNER 530_2010 1.13.16 BRE - Burner Down-Mass ACME shall return both BRE burners to Earth at the end of spaceflight testing. 1.1 [ACME] General Experiment Configuration BURNER 530_0040 1.1.3 Burners - Duplicate to PS ACME shall provide at least one duplicate of each burner to the Project Scientist except where burners with different tube lengths are otherwise identical, then only one such burner is required for transfer to the Project Scientist. EMS 510_0020 1.1.6 Simultaneous Hardware Configuration ACME shall apply all configuration requirements",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p87,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 80 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description simultaneously unless otherwise specified such as those for burners, electrodes, e-field, gas supply and delivery, ignition, chamber atmosphere, data synchronization and recording, and imaging. 1.1 [CIR & ACME] Ignition IGN 540_0110 1.10.2 Ignition – Hydrodynamic Disturbance ACME shall provide ignition where the igniter is inserted at least 30 seconds prior to ignition, and removed from the free area within 0.5 second after igniter off. 1.1 [CIR] Chamber Atmosphere CIA 500_0010 1.11.1 Chamber Atmosphere – Composition CIR Support The ACME flow system shall provide the capability to vary the gas composition within the CIR chamber with an accuracy of ±0.005 mole fraction of each concentration. CIA 500_0020 1.11.1 Chamber Atmosphere – Dry Gases CIR Support The ACME flow system shall provide dry chamber gas. CIA 500_0021 1.11.1 Chamber Atmosphere - Maintain Dry The ACME flow system shall maintain a dry chamber atmosphere. CIA 500_0030 1.11.1 Chamber Atmosphere – Trace Contaminants CIR Support The ACME flow system shall provide chamber gas containing less than a mole fraction of 0.01 of contaminants H2O and CO2. CIA 500_0040 1.11.2 Chamber Atmosphere – Mixed CIR Support The ACME flow system shall provide a well mixed chamber atmosphere such that the chamber fan moves 100 times the gas volume in the chamber.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p87,1,"CIA 500_0050 1.11.3 Chamber Atmosphere – Quiescence ACME shall provide quiescent conditions of the chamber atmosphere achieved with a hold period of at least 300 seconds prior to ignition, following filling, venting or actuator motion. CIA 500_0060 1.11.3 Chamber Atmosphere – Convective Disturbances ACME shall provide chamber atmospheric conditions such that convective disturbances during a test point are limited to those caused by burner gas flow, combustion, the igniter, and the motion of the mesh electrode and any diagnostics. CIA 500_0070 1.11.3 Chamber Atmosphere – Quiescence Data Sampling ACME shall provide quiescent conditions extending through the entire duration of the data collection. CIA 500_0080 1.11.4 Chamber Atmosphere – Initial Pressure Range ACME shall provide the capability to vary the initial, pre- test chamber pressure in the range 0.1 to 3 bar absolute. CIA 500_0090 1.11.5 Chamber Atmosphere – Initial Temperature Range ACME shall provide the initial, pre-test ambient temperature of 290 to 310 degrees Kelvin. CIA 500_0100 1.11.5 Chamber Atmosphere – Initial Temperature Uniformity ACME shall provide the initial, pre-test ambient temperature that is uniform within ± 5 degrees Kelvin.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p88,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 81 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description CIA 500_0160 1.11.10 Chamber Atmosphere – Ambient Disturbances ACME shall provide a chamber atmosphere such that ambient disturbances are limited to those caused by burner flow, combustion, the igniter, the motion of any probes or the electrode mesh, and g-jitter during each test, including the entire data collection period. CIA 500_0170 1.11.11 Chamber Atmosphere – ISS Ops Disturbances ACME shall provide a chamber atmosphere such that no test points are conducted when thrusters fire or spacecraft dock or undock from ISS. 2.2 [CIR] Chamber Oxygen Concentration MEAS 570_0040 2.2.1 Chamber Oxygen Concentration - Filling/Scrubbing ACME shall measure the oxygen concentration of the chamber atmosphere after procedures for filling and/or scrubbing are completed using the CIR’s GCIP when available. MEAS 570_0050 2.2.1 Chamber Oxygen Concentration – Well-Mixed ACME shall measure the oxygen concentration of the chamber atmosphere after that atmosphere has been well- mixed using the CIR’s GCIP when available. 2.3 [CIR] Gas Flow Rate FLOW INTEG 520_0800 2.3.4 Gas Flow Rate – Recording CIR Chamber ACME shall ensure that gas flow in all supply lines to the CIR chamber is always measured and recorded during each test even if and when there is no gas flow in certain line(s). 2.5 [ACME] Electric Potential E-FIELD 580_0420 2.5.4",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p88,1,"Electric Potential – E-FIELD Flames tests only ACME shall provide electric potential measurement between the mesh electrode and the high voltage (HV) ground terminal for the E-FIELD Flames tests. 2.6 [CIR] Chamber Acceleration MEAS INTEG 570_0110 2.6.1 Chamber Acceleration Measurement ACME shall provide chamber acceleration measurement(s) through SAMS, when available, with a sensor head at or near the CIR, unless waived by the Project Scientist. 3.3 [CIR] Ultraviolet (UV) Imaging UVI 320_0010 3.3.1 UV Imaging – OH* Filter ACME shall provide ultraviolet (UV) imaging using the CIR LLL-UV Package, where camera and all associated optics are optimized for UV imaging through an OH* filter (310 nanometers) with a 10 nanometers FWHM, i.e., Full Width at Half Maximum transmission. UVI 320_0020 3.3.2 UV Imaging FOV – Spherical & BRE ACME shall provide ultraviolet imaging for 75mm diameter FOV, for the spherical and BRE flames, using the CIR LLL- UV Package. UVI 320_0030 3.3.3 UV Imaging FOV – Gas-Jet & Coflow ACME shall provide ultraviolet imaging for 60mm ± 5mm along the chamber axis and at least 30mm wide (i.e. in the",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p89,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 82 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description direction orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis), for the gas- jet and coflow flames, using the CIR LLL-UV Package. 3.4.2 [CIR] Hot Soot Region Temperature Measurement HiBMS2 320_2010 3.4.2.1 3.4.2.2 Hot Soot Region Temperature – Spherical and BRE ACME shall provide hot soot-containing region temperature measurements for spherical and BRE flames with a minimum measurement region of 85-mm diameter centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. HiBMS2 320_2020 3.4.2.1 3.4.2.3 Hot Soot Region Temperature – Gas-Jet & Coflow ACME shall provide hot soot-containing region temperature measurements for the gas-jet and coflow flames such that the measurement region is 50 ± 5mm along the chamber axis and at least 20mm wide centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. HiBMS2 320_2040 3.4.2.5 Hot Soot Region Temperature – Sensor Gain HiBMS2 shall provide hot soot-containing region temperature measurements such that the sensor has a variable gain via uplink prior to ignition. HiBMS2 320_2050 3.4.2.6 Hot Soot Region Temperature – Sampling HiBMS2 AMP CSCI shall provide hot soot-containing region temperature measurements such that the measurements occur at least every 5 seconds with a response time of 5 seconds. HiBMS2 320_2060 3.4.2.7",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p89,1,"Hot Soot Region Temperature Measurement – Control HiBMS2 shall provide hot soot-containing region temperature measurements such that the measurements start and stop according to uplink prior to ignition. 3.4.3 [CIR] Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature HiBMS2 320_2070 3.4.3.1 3.4.3.5 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Spherical & BRE HiBMS2 shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements for the spherical and BRE flames where the minimum measurement region is an 85mm diameter, in the direction orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis, centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. HiBMS2 320_2080 3.4.3.6 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Gas-Jet & Coflow HiBMS2 shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements for the gas-jet and coflow flames where the measurement region is 50mm ± 5mm along the chamber axis and at least 20mm wide, in the direction orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis, centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. DIAG 560_0120 3.4.3.8 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Fiber Size ACME shall provide 15-micron SiC fibers for hot soot-free region temperature measurement. HiBMS2 320_2100 3.4.3.10 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Sensor Gain HiBMS2 shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements such that the sensor allows variable gain via uplink prior to ignition. HiBMS2 321_2110 3.4.3.11 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Sampling The IMAG HiBMS2 HWCI shall provide hot soot-free",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p90,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 83 of 117 System SSC_ID ISRD Trace OPS Trace ERD REQ Title/Description region temperature measurements that occur at least every 5 seconds with a response time of 5 seconds. HiBMS2 322_2120 3.4.3.12 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Control The IMAG HiBMS2 HWCI shall provide hot soot-free region temperature measurements that start and stop according to uplink prior to ignition. DIAG 560_0550 3.4.3.14 Hot Soot-Free Region Temperature – Platinum Wire ACME shall provide the option of using a TFP array where the furthest downstream fiber is replaced with a platinum wire that is 200 ± 50 microns in diameter where the wire diameter is known to ± 5 microns. 3.5 [CIR] Soot Volume Fraction Measurement HiBMS1 320_1010 3.5.1 3.5.2 Soot Volume Fraction – Spherical and BRE FOV HiBMS1 shall provide soot volume fraction measurement, for the spherical and BRE flames; such that the measurement region is at least a 45mm diameter centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. HiBMS1 320_1020 3.5.1 3.5.3 Soot Volume Fraction – Gas-Jet & Coflow FOV HiBMS1 shall provide soot volume fraction measurement, for the spherical flames; such that the measurement region is at least 25mm along the CIR chamber axis and at least 25mm wide (i.e., in the direction orthogonal to the CIR chamber axis), centered on the intersection of the CIR chamber window axes. HiBMS1 320_1030 3.5.4",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p90,1,"Soot Volume Fraction – Image Types The CIR illumination package shall be available to provide soot volume fraction measurement such that there are three image types: illumination with no flame, illumination with the flame, and the flame without illumination. HiBMS1 320_1040 3.5.5 Soot Volume Fraction Measurement – Frequency HiBMS1 shall provide soot volume fraction measurement such that the measurements are made at 1 sample per second or faster with a response time of 1 second. HiBMS1 320_1050 3.5.6 Soot Volume Fraction – Control HiBMS1 shall provide soot volume fraction measurement such that the measurements start and stop according to uplink prior to ignition. 3.9 [CIR] Post-Test Gas Composition MEAS 570_0380 3.9.1, 3.9.2 Post-Test Gas Composition ACME shall be able to reference the CIR GCIP. 1.12 [ACME] Data Synchronization and Recording CDS 620_0110 1.12.5 Data Downlink - Select Image Downlink ACME shall provide the capability to downlink image data from only selected imaging systems. CDS 620_0120 1.12.6 Data Downlink - Select Data Downlink ACME shall provide the capability to downlink a fraction of the acquired image data from selected time periods. CDS 620_0130 1.12.6 Data Downlink - Select Data Time Period ACME shall provide the capability to select different time periods for each imaging system where a fraction of the data is downlinked.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p91,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 84 of 117",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p92,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 85 of 117 9.0 CARRIER REQUIRMENTS All ACME carrier requirements are contained in the ACME Interface Control Document (ICD), FCF-ICD-CIR-ACME, which will be completed by the FCF CIR Sustaining Engineering Team.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p93,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 86 of 117 10.0 DERIVED REQUIREMENTS This section specifies derived requirements for the ACME system. Derived Requirements are those requirements not directly linked to a science or operational requirement as defined by the NASA project scientist. Table 10-1—Derived Requirements System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description FLOW 520_1430 ACME Risk 021 Spare - Mass Flow Controller ACME shall provide 1 spare mass flow controller assembly for each oxidizer, inert and fuel flow rate. CIA 500_0250 ACME Risk 010 Spare - Data Cube ACME shall provide 1 spare data cube assemblies. AVP 600_0200 Spare - Hard Drive Assembly ACME shall provide 2 spare hard drive assemblies. OpsCam 550_190 Spare - OpsCam ACME shall provide 1 spare operational camera assembly. DataCam 310_610 Spare - DataCam ACME shall provide 1 spare digital color camera assemblies. DIAG 560_0510 Spare - TFP ACME shall provide 10 spare thin filament pyrometry array assemblies. MEAS 570_1330 Spare - Far Field TC Array ACME shall provide 10 spare far field thermocouple array assemblies for both the near and far positions. MEAS 570_1330 Spare - 200mm Thermocouples ACME shall provide 5 spare 200mm thermocouple assemblies for both the relay and igniter positions. IGN 540_0310 Spare - Igniter Tips ACME shall provide 20 spare igniter tips. E-FIELD 580_0640 Spare - E-FIELD Mesh Electrode ACME shall provide 1 spare E-field electrode mesh.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p93,1,E-FIELD 580_0650 Spare - E-FIELD HV Power Supply ACME shall provide 1 spare E-field high voltage power supply. BURNER 530_2030 Spare - Spherical Burners ACME shall provide 5 spare spherical burners of each size. BURNER 530_2040 Spare - Gas-Jet Burners ACME shall provide 2 spare gas jet burners of each size. BURNER 530_2050 Spare - BRE Burners ACME shall provide 1 spare BRE burner of each size. EMS 510_0110 Spare - Fuel Hose ACME shall provide 1 spare fuel hose assembly. EMS 510_0120 Spare - Oxygen Hose ACME shall provide 1 spare oxygen hose assembly. EMS 510_0130 Spare - Inert Hose ACME shall provide 1 spare Inert hose assembly. EMS 510_0140 Spare - Green Water Cooling Hose ACME shall provide 1 spare green water cooling hose assembly.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p94,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 87 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace ERD REQ Title/Description EMS 510_0150 Spare - Grey Water Cooling Hose ACME shall provide 1 spare grey water cooling hose assembly. 11.0 SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS This section specifies software requirements for the ACME Main Processor (AMP), ACME Ground Software (AGS), and Computer Software Configuration Items (CSCI). Table 11-1—Software Requirements System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description General CIR 611_0170 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.3.1 The AMP CSCI shall immediately enter Initialization state upon power on. CIR 611_0180 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.3.2 The AMP CSCI shall transition to Operational state upon successful initialization. CIR 611_0190 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.3.2.1 The AMP CSCI shall have an Idle state within the Operational state which denotes the experiment is suspended. CIR 611_0200 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.3.3 The AMP CSCI shall transition into Off- Nominal state when a significant error occurs either during initialization or nominal operation. CIR 611_0210 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.3.4 The AMP CSCI shall transition to Safed state upon command. CIR 612_0220 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.2.1.2 The AGS CSCI shall obtain telemetry once a second upon connection to the AMP CSCI. CIR 612_0230 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.2.1.2 The AGS CSCI shall display the current software state from the telemetry report.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p94,1,CIR 611_0240 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.2.1.2 The AGS CSCI shall display health and status from the telemetry report. CIR 611_0250 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.5 The AMP CSCI shall report telemetry upon command. CIR 611_0260 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.5 The AMP CSCI shall report the current software state in the telemetry report. CIR 611_0270 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.7.5 The AMP CSCI shall report health and status in the telemetry report.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p95,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 88 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description CIR 612_0280 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AGS CSCI shall communicate with the FCF IOP MP according to FCF-ICD-0076A, the FCF SW ICD. CIR 612_0290 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AGS CSCI shall communicate with the AMP CSCI according to ACME-DOC-008, the ACME Command and Telemetry ICD. CIR 611_0300 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AMP CSCI shall communicate with the FCF IOP MP according to FCF-ICD-0076A. CIR 611_0310 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AMP CSCI shall communicate with the FCF IPSU MPs according to FCF-ICD- 0076A. CIR 611_0320 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AMP CSCI shall interface with the PMD Prodigy/CMD PC/104 Motion Control Board. CIR 611_0330 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.1.1.1.5 The AMP CSCI shall interface with the AGS CSCI according to ACME-DOC-008, the ACME Command and Telemetry ICD. CIR 612_0340 FCF-ICD- CIR-ACME 8.2.1.1 The AGS CSCI shall use the TReK library to communicate with the TSC. MCS AMP 611_0010 1.12.1 Data Synchronization ACME shall have all data time stamped and synchronized to within +/- 0.03 sec and referenced within +/- 0.03 sec of GMT. MCS AGS 612_0090 1.12.5 Data Downlink – Image System - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide a command to transfer data files to the IOP.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p95,1,MCS AMP 611_0080 1.12.5 Data Downlink – Image System - Configured The AMP CSCI shall transfer data files to the IOP upon command. MCS AGS 612_0110 1.12.6 Data Downlink – Image Select - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide a command to transfer subsets of the color imaging data to the IOP MP. DataCam AMP 311_0560 3.2 Data Color Imaging Interface The AMP CSCI shall interface with the AVT GC1380CH digital color camera. MCS AMP 611_0150 1.12 Cube Interface The AMP CSCI shall interface with the UEI PowerDNA Gigabit cube. MCS AMP 611_0160 1.12 Hard Drive Interface The AMP CSCI shall store data to the SATA disk. OPS 602_0150 4.0 AGS Uplink - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide a command to uplink a sequence to the AMP CSCI. OPS 602_0160 4.0 AGS Sequence Saved The AGS CSCI shall allow a sequence to be saved to file.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p96,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 89 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description OPS 602_0170 4.0 AGS Sequence Loaded The AGS CSCI shall allow a sequence to be loaded from file. OPS 601_0110 4.0 Automated Sequence Uplink - Configured The AMP CSCI shall allow an automated sequence to be uplinked. OPS 601_0120 4.0 Automated Sequence Execute The AMP CSCI shall execute the uplinked automated sequence upon command. OPS 601_0130 4.0 Automated Sequence Accept The AMP CSCI shall only accept uplinked sequences when in Operational state. MCS AGS 612_0030 1.12.2 1.12.3 1.12.7 5.4 5.5 Data Recording - Hard Drive - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide and uplinkable command to configure the hard drive to record data up to 5 minutes before and after a test point. MCS AMP 611_0020 1.12.2 1.12.3 1.12.7 5.4 5.5 Data Recording - Hard Drive - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the hard drive to record data up to 5 minutes before and after a test point. MCS AGS 612_0350 Upstream Relay Board 1 - Enable/ Disable - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the upstream relay board 1 to enable/disable. MCS AMP 611_0360 Upstream Relay Board 1 - Enable/ Disable - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the upstream relay board 1 to enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0V or +5V through channel A012.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p96,1,MCS AGS 612_0370 Downstream Relay Board 2 - Enable/ Disable - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the downstream relay board 2 to enable/disable. MCS AMP 611_0380 Downstream Relay Board 2 - Enable/ Disable - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the downstream relay board 2 to enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0V or +5V through channel A030. Flow System,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p97,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 90 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description FLOW AGS 522_1070 1.9.1 1.9.2 1.9.4 1.11.1 4.1 4.2 4.3 4.4 4.6 9.1 9.2 9.3 9.4 9.5 9.6 9.7 9.8 9.9 9.10 9.11 Flow System - Mass Flow Controller A1- Commanded Enable/Disable The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure MFC A1 enable/disable. FLOW AMP 521_1080 1.9.1 1.9.2 1.9.4 1.11.1 4.1 4.2 4.3 4.4 4.6 9.1 9.2 9.3 9.4 9.5 9.6 9.7 9.8 9.9 9.10 9.11 Flow System - Mass Flow Controller A1 Configured Enable/Disable The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command MFC A1 to enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0 or +5V through channel AO9. FLOW AGS 522_1090 1.9.1 1.9.2 1.9.4 1.11.1 4.1 4.2 4.3 4.4 4.6 9.1 9.2 9.3 9.4 9.5 9.6 9.7 9.8 9.9 9.10 9.11 Flow System - Mass Flow Controller A2- Commanded Enable/Disable The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure MFC A2 enable/disable.",,False
