PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p114,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 107 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG AGS 562_0400 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 3 - Enable/ Disable - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure PMT3 enable/disable. DIAG AMP 561_0410 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 3 - Enable/ Disable - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command PMT3 enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0V or +10V through channel A03. DIAG AGS 562_0420 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 1 - Gain Adjust - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure PMT1 gain adjust. DIAG AMP 561_0430 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 1 - Gain Adjust - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command PMT1 gain adjust by applying a voltage of 0V to +5V through channel A025. DIAG AGS 562_0440 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 2 - Gain Adjust - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure PMT2 gain adjust. DIAG AMP 561_0450 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 2 - Gain Adjust - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command PMT2 gain adjust by applying a voltage of 0V to +5V through channel A026.",,False
