PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p115,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 108 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG AMP 561_0470 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 3 - Gain Adjust - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command PMT3 gain adjust by applying a voltage of 0V to +5V through channel A027. DIAG AMP 561_500 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube - Sampling Rate ACME shall sample chemiluminescent emission measurements at 120 samples/sec or faster with a temporal resolution of .005 s. DIAG AGS 572_0450 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 1 - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display chemiluminescent emission measurements from PMT1 from the telemetry report. DIAG AMP 571_0460 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 1 - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report chemiluminescent emission measurements from PMT1 by reading a voltage of 0V to +4V on channel Ain-8 (207). DIAG AGS 572_0470 3.7.1 3.7.5 12.1 12.2 12.3 12.4 12.5 12.6 12.7 Photomultiplier Tube 2 - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display chemiluminescent emission measurements from PMT2 from the telemetry report.",,False
