PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p119,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 112 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS AGS 572_0760 3.4.1.8 3.4.4.8 1.6 5.4 12.1 Thermocouple Cold Junction - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display temperature measurements for type K thermocouple cold junction from the telemetry report. MEAS AMP 571_0770 3.4.1.8 3.4.4.8 1.6 5.4 12.1 Thermocouple Cold Junction - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report temperature measurements for type K thermocouple cold junction by reading a voltage of .803V to + 1.1V from channel Ain-24 (225.) MEAS AGS 572_0780 3.4.1.8 3.4.4.8 1.6 5.4 12.1 Thermocouple Spare - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display temperature measurements for the thermocouple spare from the telemetry report. MEAS AMP 571_0790 3.4.1.8 3.4.4.8 1.6 5.4 12.1 Thermocouple Spare - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report temperature measurements for the thermocouple spare by reading a voltage of 0V to +1.25V from channel Ain-20 (225.) MEAS AMP 581_0600 2.5.3 5.4 Electric Potential – Sampling Frequency The AMP CSCI shall collect E-Field Electric potential measurements at 120 sample/s with a temporal resolution of 1ms. MEAS AGS 582_0610 2.5.3 5.4 Electric Potential - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display E-FIELD electric potential measurements from the telemetry report.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p119,1,MEAS AMP 581_0540 2.5.3 5.4 Electric Potential - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report E-FIELD electric potential measurements by reading a voltage of -4V to +4V from channel Ain-7 (207.) MEAS AMP 581_0450 3.8.4 5.4 Ion Current – Sampling Frequency The AMP CSCI shall collect E-Field ion current measurements at 120 Hz. MEAS AGS 582_0620 3.8.4 5.4 Ion Current - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display E-Field Ion current measurements from the telemetry report. MEAS AMP 581_0550 3.8.4 5.4 Ion Current - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report E-Field ion current measurements by reading a voltage of -1.5V to +1.5V from channel Ain- 3 (207.) MEAS AGS 572_1290 3.10.1 3.10.2 1.13.12 BRE Heat Flux Measurement Center - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display heat flux measurements for the center position sensor from the telemetry report.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p120,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 113 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description MEAS AMP 571_1300 3.10.1 3.10.2 1.13.12 BRE Heat Flux Measurement Center - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report heat flux measurements for the center position sensor by reading a voltage of 0V to +1.25V from channel Ain-20 (225.) MEAS AGS 572_1310 3.10.1 3.10.2 1.13.12 BRE Heat Flux Measurement Offset - Telemetry Display The AGS CSCI shall display heat flux measurements for the offset position sensor from the telemetry report. MEAS AMP 571_1320 3.10.1 3.10.2 1.13.12 BRE Heat Flux Measurement Offset - Telemetry Report The AMP CSCI shall report heat flux measurements for the offset position sensor by reading a voltage of 0V to +1.25V from channel Ain-21 (225.) E-Field E-FIELD AGS 582_0170 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV1 Enable/Disable - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the E-field HV1 enable/disable. E-FIELD AMP 581_0180 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV1 Enable/Disable - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the E-field HV1 enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0V or +5V through channel AO5. E-FIELD AGS 582_0560 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV2 Enable/Disable - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the E-field HV2 enable/disable.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p120,1,E-FIELD AMP 581_0570 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV2 Enable/Disable - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the E-field HV2 enable/disable by applying a voltage of 0V or +5V through channel AO6. E-FIELD AGS 582_0580 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV Control - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the E-Field HV output voltage. E-FIELD AMP 581_0590 1.7.1 1.7.2 1.7.4 11.1 11.3 Electric Field - HV Control - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the E-Field HV control by applying a voltage of 0V to +5V through channel A04.. Thin Filament Pyrometry Array,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME - Engineering Requirements Doc Rev K.pdf,p121,0,"ACME Engineering Requirements Document ACME-REQ-001 rev. K April, 2014 Page 114 of 117 System SSC_ID Parent ID/ ISRD Trace Ops Requirement Trace ERD REQ Title/Description DIAG AGS 562_0040 1.11.8 1.11.9 3.4.3.3 3.4.3.4 10.1 10.2 10.3 Thin Filament Pyrometry (TFP)- Reposition - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to change the TFP array position. DIAG AMP 561_0050 1.11.8 1.11.9 3.4.3.3 3.4.3.4 10.1 10.2 10.3 Thin Filament Pyrometry (TFP) - Reposition - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command to change the TFP array position. DIAG AGS 562_0480 1.11.8 1.11.9 3.4.3.3 3.4.3.4 10.1 10.2 10.3 Thin Filament Pyrometry (TFP) - Stepper Reset - Commanded The AGS CSCI shall provide an uplinkable command to configure the TFP stepper reset. DIAG AMP 561_0490 1.11.8 1.11.9 3.4.3.3 3.4.3.4 10.1 10.2 10.3 Thin Filament Pyrometry (TFP) - Stepper Reset - Configured The AMP CSCI shall configure upon command the TFP stepper reset by applying a voltage of 0V or +5V through channel AO13. Heat Flux Measurement MEAS AMP 571_01280 3.10.10 Heat Flux - Sampling ACME shall sample heat flux measurements at 120 samples/sec or faster with a response time of 0.5s or faster.",,False
