PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,p1,8,"| | C33 | 6 | 1126-6-SS-20 | SPACER, .25 OD. X .140 ID. X .38 LG, RAF | | C34 | A/R | TC105 | CABLE TIE MOUNTING BASE, ALUMINUM, THOMAS & BETTS | | C35 | A/R | 2216 B/A | 2216 B/A GRAY EPOXY 3M SCOTCH WELD EPOXY | | C36 | A/R | MIL-PRF-27617 | DUPONT KRYTOX 240AC TYPE III LUBRICANT | | C37 | A/R | 222MS | THREADLOCKER, LOCTITE | | C38 | A/R | 242 | THREADLOCKER, LOCTITE | | C39 | A/R | PLT1M-702Y | CABLE TIE, HALAR FLUOROPOLYMER, PANDUIT CORP., 3.9 INCH | | C40 | A/R | PLT2S-702Y | CABLE TIE, HALAR FLUOROPOLYMER, PANDUIT CORP., 7.4 INCH | | C41 | A/R | 3145 GRAY | RTV ADHESIVE/SEALANT, GRAY, DOW CORNING | | C42 | 1 | SDG32104805-008 | ESD LABEL | | C43 | 1 | BRE.0S.200.NAV | CONNECTOR COVER (LEMO) | | C44 | 1 | 667-262-M-N8 | CONNECTOR COVER (GLENAIR) | | C45 | 1 | 167-7864-1 | CONNECTOR COVER (TELEDYNE REYNOLDS) | | C46 | 1 | PSK633-9FGN | CONNECTOR COVER (POSITRONIC) | | C47 | 3 | 660-023M13N | PROTECTIVE COVER/PLUG (GLENAIR) | | C48 | A/R | S768A0BLA | BLACK POLYAMIDE/ACRYLIC TAPE, 1"" | ### NOTES (numbers marked ""flag"" are drawn inside a triangle flag symbol) 1. MATERIAL AND PROCESS CERTIFICATION REQUIRED PER QUALITY LEVEL SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW. 2. ESD HANDLING AND CONTROL PER ESTABLISHED PROCEDURES. 3. ASSEMBLY AND SOLDERING SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH NASA-STD-8739.3. 4. (flag) APPLY THREAD LOCKING COMPOUND PER ESTABLISHED PROCEDURES. 5. (flag) TORQUE VALUES NOTED ON THE DRAWING ARE EFFECTIVE TORQUE ONLY.",,True
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,p1,9,"RUNNING TORQUE IS REQUIRED FOR SELF LOCKING DEVICES AND BOLT FRICTION. RUNNING TORQUE MUST BE MEASURED AND ADDED TO THE EFFECTIVE TORQUE. RECORD RUNNING TORQUE AND FINAL TORQUE ON DRAWING OR ASSEMBLY PROCEDURE. 6. (flag) TIGHTEN ALL FLUID FITTINGS PER MANUFACTURER'S SPECIFICATIONS. 7. (flag) APPLY O-RING LUBRICANT PER ESTABLISHED PROCEDURES. 8. (flag) REFER TO CONNECTION DIAGRAM S1101EFC0315 FOR ALL HARNESS CONNECTIONS. 9. (flag) SNUG TIGHT PER ESTABLISHED PROCEDURES. 10. CHEMICAL CONVERSION COAT ANY DAMAGED OR MACHINED AREAS ON ALUMINUM PARTS PER MIL-DTL-5541, TYPE I, CLASS 3. 11. CLEAN ALL SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT-FREE CLOTH. 12. HANDLE ALL PARTS AND ASSEMBLIES WITH CLEAN, LINT-FREE, ANTI-STATIC GLOVES OR FINGER COTS. 13. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, ESD BAG, TOTES OR APPROVED ESD PACKAGING. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. 14. (flag) DISCARD TOOTHED WASHER SUPPLIED WITH ITEM C8 AND 11. 15. STAKING, BONDING AND INSPECTION SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH NASA-STD-8739.1. 16. (flag) STAKE CONNECTORS USING ITEM C41 RTV. 17. (flag) IF PRESENT, REMOVE AND DISCARD LANYARD FROM ALL CAPS. 18. (flag) ADJUST, LOCTITE AND EPOXY ARM OF ITEM 55 TFP ASSEMBLY USING C35 EPOXY AND C38 LOCTITE PER PROCESS PLAN. REFERENCE S1101MFA1529 DRAWING FOR DETAILS. 19. ASSEMBLE USING S1101MGA4559 EMS STAND. 20.",,True
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,p1,10,"(flag) APPLY LABEL TO CLEAN, DRY SURFACE IN LOCATION SHOWN. 21. TEST COMPLETED ASSEMBLY PER ACME-TST-036. 22. (flag) IF PRESENT, REMOVE INDICATED QD CAPS FROM SUBASSEMBLY AND RETURN TO STORES ### REVISION HISTORY | REV | DESCRIPTION | APPROVED | |---|---|---| | C | INCORPORATED ACME-ECO-554 AND ACME-ECO-643. | [name omitted] 10/20/16 (x3) | | B | INCORPORATED ACME-ECO-552. | [name omitted] 12/10/15 (x3) | | A | INCORPORATED ACME-ECO-383. | [name omitted] 10/13/15, 10/13/15, 10/14/15 |",,True
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,p1,11,"### TITLE BLOCK - UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED: 1. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN INCHES 2. BREAK EDGES .010-.020 3. INSIDE CORNERS R.02 MAX 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: .X ± .03, .XX ± .01, .XXX ± .005 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCE ± .5° - THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION - THIS DRAWING IS UNDER CONFIGURATION CONTROL: DO NOT REVISE WITHOUT AN APPROVED ECO. APPROVED: [name omitted] 10/20/16. PRIOR TO USE, CHECK WITH CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT FOR ANY OUTSTANDING ECOS. - DESIGNER [name omitted] 8/1/14; REVIEWER [name omitted] 8/4/14; MECHANICAL [name omitted] 8/5/14; ELECTRICAL [name omitted] 8/4/14; STRUCTURAL [name omitted] 8/6/14; SAFETY [name omitted] 8/4/14; QUALITY [name omitted] 8/6/14; MATERIALS [name omitted] 8/11/14; PROJ LEAD [name omitted] 8/6/14 - DIMENSIONS AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994 - ZIN TECHNOLOGIES [address omitted] - CONTRACT NUMBER: NNC14A02C; PROJECT CODE: S2-BT3 - NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO - TITLE: ACME CHAMBER INSERT ASSEMBLY - SIZE E; CAGE CODE 0SG68; DWG NO S1101MFA0100; REV C - SCALE 1/2; INITIAL REL DATE 8/7/14; SHEET 1 OF 5 - RELEASE LEVEL: WORKING; MODEL: S1101MFA0100; PRO/E VERSION: Wildfire 2.0",,True
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s1101mfa0100_C.pdf,p2,0,"Description: sheet 2, exploded isometric assembly views of the ACME chamber insert with item balloons, torque callouts and connector reference labels; option tables for burners, TFP arrays, E-field power supplies and mass flow controllers. Balloon numbers refer to the item lists on sheet 1; triangle flags refer to sheet 1 notes (shown here as ""flag N""). NOTES: 1. SEE SHEET 1 FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION, GENERAL NOTES AND TOLERANCES. ### View: INPUT MANIFOLD HARNESS, COLD JUNCTION COMPENSATION & BRE BURNER (LOCATION 6) ASSEMBLIES PARTIAL VIEWS NOTE: SOME ITEMS REMOVED FOR CLARITY",,True
