PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s-Flame_RDR_201005.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_s-Flame_RDR_201005.pdf,p4,0,"Merits of One-Dimensional Flames s-Flame for Fundamental Studies • Flame structure fundamentally affected by aerodynamics. • Simple flow and flame configuration facilitate experimentation, computation, analysis, and comparison, with enhanced accuracy and reliability.p, y y • Reduced effort in describing flows allows more detailed study of other aspects of flames such as chemistrychemistry. • A one-dimensional flame is the simplest possible configuration. 33 g",,False
