PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p80,0,79 79 s-Flame Operation Sequence,,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p81,0,"80 80 s-Flame I. Establish chamber at constant pressure and species concentration II. Discharge fuel mixture through porous burner at initial flow rate III. Ignite fuel mixture and retract upon successful ignition IV. Allow for spherical diffusion flame to evolve V. Apply one of the following: ▪ Maintain flow rate with same initial mixture for duration of experiment (25s) or until extinction ▪ Single step decrease in flow rate with same initial mixture at specified time, maintaining new flow rate for duration of experiment (25s) or until extinction VI. Terminate fuel supply to burner after 25s. Experiment Plan (1/2)",,False
