PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p89,0,"88 88 s-Flame • Deliver fuel, inert(s) to burner • Different flow rates • Small versus large characteristic flame sizes • Ignite at moderate flow rate, establish quasi-steady flame, step flow rate down to examine kinetic extinction at small flame radii Flow Supply and Flow Rate • Different compositions as specified by Test Matrix • Provide gas at max flow rate for at least 25s m1 m2 time Max Temperature System Damkohler Number Purely Kinetic Extinction Radiation-affected Extinction Max Temperature System Damkohler Number Purely Kinetic Extinction Radiation-affected Extinction",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p90,0,89 89 s-Flame • Different flow rates – Affect characteristic flame size (residence time) • Radiative extinction • Characteristic time to steady state – Kinetic extinction versus radiative extinction • Step in mass flow rates are utilized – Ensure ignition and establishment of quasi-steady behavior – Inward flame evolution toward kinetic extinction Flow Supply and Flow Rate,,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p91,0,"90 90 s-Flame • H2/Inert (Required) • Addresses pure hydrogen chemistry • Only H2O in radiation considerations • Only OH* chemiluminescence • CH4/Inert (Required) • Addresses methane chemistry, e.g. GRI-Mech • H2O, CO2, CO in radiation considerations • H2/CH4/Inert (Required) • Addresses chemical kinetics of blended mixture including kinetic extinction • Different characteristic radiative extinction times • OH* and CH* chemiluminescence Fuel Mixtures",,False
