PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p94,0,"93 93 s-Flame Test Matrix Rationale • Different inerts to affect diffusive properties, radiative properties, and flame temperature – N2 (Required) • Moderate flame temperature • Radiatively transparent • Normal “air” – He (Required) • Higher flame temperature • Radiatively transparent • High-Lewis number promoting pulsating instability – CO2 (Desired) • Lower flame temperature • Optically participating medium (highly reabsorptive species) • All inerts fixed at 0.55 mole fraction for non C2H2 fuel mixtures",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p95,0,"94 94 s-Flame Ambient Environment • STP • Different sets of ambient gas mixtures to alter characteristic flame temperatures, diffusive transport, and radiative properties • “Air”: 0.21 O2, 0.79 N2 (Required) • “He-Air”: 0.21 O2, 0.79 He (Required) • “CO2-Air”: 0.21 O2, 0.79 CO2 (Desired) • Specified to within 1% mole fraction • Ambient gas may be scrubbed and recycled for subsequent tests",,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p96,0,95 95 s-Flame Success Criteria,,False
PSI-23,Science Documents,PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Science Documents/PSI-23_Science Documents_s-Flame SCR 200802.pdf,p97,0,96 96 s-Flame Minimal Success • Observations of transient flame phenomena leading toward steady state flames for 1 CH4 case and 1 C2H4 case; or • Observations of flame extinction at both low and high system Damkohler number for 1 case; or • Observations of spherical soot formation in 1 C2H4 case.,,False
