PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p10,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 15 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Payload Specific Hardware • Unique hardware components • Specific Diagnostics • Unique PI fuels ACME Chamber Insert • Platform for exchangeable burner: – Gas Delivery – Retracting ignitor – Electric field generator • Infrastructure that uniquely meets the needs of PI experiments • Unique science requirements FCF Combustion Integrated Rack • Power Supply • Avionics/Control • Structural Support & Power • Common Diagnostics and Illumination • Environmental Control • Data Processing/Distribution • Fluids Control/Distribution • Combustion Containment The Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) includes support subsystems and combustion diagnostics commonly needed for combustion investigations and supplements the laboratory with unique science hardware developed for each Principal Investigator (PI). Payload specific and multi-user hardware customizes the CIR in a unique laboratory configuration to perform research effectively. Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments Insert Assembly CIR Sub-rack Payload Relationship,,False
