PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p31,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 36 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Requirements • ACME ERD – 735 Total Requirements. • 407 Engineering build-to requirements 55.37% • 107 Operations requirements 14.56% • 202 Software requirements 27.48% • 19 Derived requirements 2.59% • Integration requirements are generated by the Mission Integration and Planning Team (MIP) and are documented in FCF-ICD-CIR-ACME. This document encompasses requirements flowed down to ACME form the ISS Program and CIR. All carrier interface requirements are documented here • Safety requirements are documented in the ACME Safety Verification Tracking Log (SVTL),,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p32,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 37 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Integration Requirements • Operations • Use of chamber fan • Use of gas chromatograph (GCIP) • Rack acceleration measurement • Atmosphere and Flow • Venting to specific pressures • Atmosphere scrubbing • Vary gas composition • Provide source gases • Diagnostics • LLL-UV • OH* 310 nm Filter • LLL-UV FOV • 30, 50, 80mm lenses • HiBMS-2 • 90mm lens • Adjust gain setting • HiBMS-1 • 30, 50mm lenses • Illumination Package",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p33,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 38 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Sample Requirements from ACME Requirements Matrix System SSC_ID ISRD Trace ISRD Description Trace ERD REQ Title/Description Comply? (Y/W/N) Compliance Approach V-type V-area Verification Activities SPACE110 1.1 General Experiment Configuration Y BURNER 530_0010 1.1.1 1.1.1. The experimental hardware shall accommodate all of the burners described in sections 1.2-1.4, and 1.13, but only a single burner shall be installed at a time within the CIR chamber.* Burners – Installation ACME shall install a single burner one at a time within the CIR chamber. Y ACME design includes replaceable burners that will be installed on orbit one at a time in the CIA to support each experiment within the CIR. D ME The verification shall be considered successful when a demonstration of the flight hardware shows that a single burner can be installed in the CIA one at a time. BURNER 530_0020 1.1.2 1.1.2. All burners shall be Orbital Replacement Units (ORUs) and exchangeable during spaceflight. Burners – Exchangeable ACME shall provide that all burners are exchangeable during spaceflight. Y ACME design includes exchangeable burners that can be changed out during spacefilght. I ME The verification shall be considered successful when the inspection of each flight burner mounting plate shows that it is compatible with the flight switching manifold.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p33,1,"BURNER 530_0030 1.1.2 Burners – ORU ACME shall provide all burners as ORUs. Y ACME design includes burners that are orbital replaceable units. I PS The verification shall be considered successful when each burner is approved by HFIT for ORU classification. FLOW 520_0010 1.1.4.1 1.1.4. The gas delivery system and all burners shall be compatible with at least the following gases: 1.1.4.1. gaseous fuels: hydrogen, methane, ethane, propane, ethylene, propylene, or mixtures of any of these fuels; Flow System H/W Compatibility - Hydrogen ACME shall provide a gas delivery system that is compatible with the gaseous fuel hydrogen. Y ACME design includes a flow system that is compatible with the gaseous fuel hydrogen. A MP The verification shall be considered successful when the material analysis of the flow system hardware shows compatibility with the gaseous fuel hydrogen.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p34,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 39 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Compliance Summary • ACME-DOC-002 Requirements Compliance Matrix • Engineering build-to requirements: 100% Compliance • Operational requirements: 100% Compliance • Software requirements: 100% Compliance • Derived requirements: 100% Compliance,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p35,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 40 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Verification Planning • ACME and CIR will verify system performance • Engineering, operational, software, and derived requirements in the ACME ERD are verified in the Science & Engineering Verification Plan; ACME-PLN-003 (Baselined) • ACME requirements called out in the ERD are ACME’s responsibility to verify or obtain verification from carrier (i.e. CIR cameras, GCIP, etc.) • CIR component performance is verified and reported to ACME via the MIP Team. • ACME will also verify payload requirements passed down from the ISS Program and CIR (FCF-ICD-CIR-ACME) • Payload requirements are verified in the Payload Verification Plan (FCF-PVP-CIR-ACME) • PVP is generated by the MIP Team • ACME verifies payload requirements • ACME delivers Payload Verification Report to CIR to be rolled up and reported in the integrated rack verifications",,False
