PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p38,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 43 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Testing Plan • As Engineering Model sub-systems are built, they will be functionally tested to validate performance at that level • When the system level Engineering Model is complete we will conduct ACME functional testing between the AVP, Data Camera and CIA to validate performance at the system level • These 3 units comprising the Engineering Model will then be installed on the CIR GIU for integrated testing with the rack, validating carrier interfaces • Since the EM is built to flight drawings, it will then undergo Qual testing: Vibration, EMI and thermal • When the Flight Unit is complete the Flight AVP, CIA and Data Camera will undergo flight level environmental testing: Vibe, EMI and offgas • The remainder of flight verification testing will then occur after the flight environmental testing",,False
