PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p57,1,"1) Princeton University: Fabricate a 1/4”, 3/8”, and 1/2” spherical burner head with supply tube per ACME ISRD 1.2.1, 1.2.2, 1.2.5, and 1.2.6. 2) Princeton University: Perform preliminary tests on the above spherical burner heads following ACME ISRD 1.2.3 as a guide and conferring with NASA ACME Project Scientist. 3) Princeton University: Deliver accepted spherical burner heads to NASA Glenn Research Center (GRC). 4) NASA GRC performs additional acceptance tests as necessary (microgravity). 5) NASA GRC deliver acceptable spherical burner heads to ZIN Technologies Inc. as government furnished equipment (GFE.) via C727. 6) Zin Technologies Inc.: Accept and serialize spherical burner heads from NASA GRC. 7) Zin Technologies Inc.: Perform additional fabrication on S1101MFA1218, S1101MFA1223, and S1101MFA1228 per ACME ISRD 1.2.4, 1.2.6, and 1.2.7. This fabrication will produce the following top level assemblies: S1101MFA1216: 1/4” spherical burner assembly, S1101MFA1220: 3/8” spherical burner assembly, S1101MFA1225: 1/2” spherical burner assembly 8) Zin Technologies Inc.: Deliver S1101MFA1216, S1101MFA1220, and S1101MFA1225 to NASA GRC via a DD1149. 9) NASA GRC: Test and verify S1101MFA1216, S1101MFA1220, and S1101MFA1225 per ACME ISRD 1.2.3. 10) NASA GRC: Deliver verified spherical burner assemblies along with verification certification documents to Zin Technologies Inc. as GFE via C727.",,False
