PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p111,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 116 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Software Safety • ACME Software Litmus Test • ACME MP – Class C, Safety Critical • Software Control Risk Level – 2 (Medium) • Likelihood of Occurrence – Improbable • Software Prioritization Risk Level - 5 Software Control Risk Levels Likelihood of Occurrence Improbable Unlikely Possible Probable Likely SW 1 (High) 4 3 2 1 1 SW 2 (Moderate) 5 4 3 2 1 SW 3 (Medium) 6 5 4 3 2 SW 4 (Marginal) 7 6 5 4 3 SW 5 (Low) 7 7 6 5 4",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p112,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 117 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Software Safety • From 8719.13C: • “In general, it is expected that for Low Software Prioritization Risks (7-5s and Green in chart above) the main requirements for both acquirer and provider would be to perform the Software Safety Criticality Assessment, keep a record of it, and revisit the SSCA upon any changes to the software functionality or design to assure the software maintains its low risk status.”",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p113,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 118 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Software Safety This is applicable to Class C software with a safety risk index of 5, 6 or 7. • ZIN writing waivers to the following requirements: • for detailed design (SWE-058) • Coding standards (SEW-061) • traceability (SSS-011) • software maintenance plan (SWE-105) • software user manual (SWE-115) • Verifying S/W hazards controlled (SSS-055) • Verification of S/W safety requirements (SSS-059) • ZIN writing deviations to: • change traceability from detailed design to architectural design(SWE-049, SWE-064) • Create software safety plan • Addition of acquirer SMA to document workflow for software related documents • Updates to current documentation • Additional work with PSRP software panel",,False
