PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p129,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 134 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Software Testing • Unit Level • Informal, use Qt unit test framework as needed • Engineering Model • Black box, send commands and ensure proper operation • Integrated • With IOP and IPSU simulators • GIU • Verify software requirements as part of system verifications as much as possible",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p130,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 135 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME Structural Analysis Chris Werner – Structural Analyst,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p131,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 136 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Requirements Req. # Requirement SSP-57000 3.1.1.3 B Load Requirements Designed to withstand the on-orbit loads of 0.2 Gs acting in any direction. SSP 50835 3.1.1.2.1.5.B Pressure Loading Maintain positive margins of safety when exposed to a depressurization rate of 13.3 kPa/second (116 pounds per square inch (psi)/minute) as shown in Table E.2.7-1. SSP-57000 3.9.1.1 Pressure Be safe when exposed to the pressure transitions between 0 to 104.8 kPa (0 to 15.2 psia). SSP 50835 3.9.1.1.A Pressure Operate properly after exposure to launch and ground handling pressures ranging from 60.0 to 129.3 kPa (8.7 to 18.8 psia). GLPR 7120.5.30 Section 3.4.4 Margins of Safety All structural elements critical for safety and mission assurance shall be shown by analysis to have positive margins of safety or, in the case of containment devices, be structurally adequate against penetration. Req. # Requirement GLPR 7120.5.30 Section 3.4.6 Pressurized Systems Pressurized systems to be flown on unmanned vehicles shall meet the requirements of ANSI/AIAA S-080, Space Systems-Metallic Pressure Vessels, Pressurized Structures, and Pressure Components, and ANSI/AIAA S-081, Space Systems-Composite Overwrapped Pressure Vessels (COPV).",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p131,1,Hazard Report STD-ACME- 17.c.1 Vented Container Analysis to demonstrate the vented containers provide an internal effective vent area ratio that results in a differential pressure loading of no greater than 0.01 psid. Hazard Report ACME-2 1.1.1 Pressure system hardware shall be designed to the following factors of safety (FS): Lines/Fittings FS = 4 x MDP. Other system components FS=2.5xMDP. Hardware shall be designed to withstand thermal and vibratory loads associated with both launch/landing and during on-orbit operation. Note: requirements are paraphrased,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p132,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 137 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis – Load Requirements • On-Orbit Operation Pressures • Fuel system pressure • Water system pressure • Crew-induced loading • CIA Handles • Color Camera Package • Avionics Package • Launch loads • Quasi-static inertial loads All pressurized systems will be proof tested to 1.5 x MDP and leak tested to 1.0 x MDP Details of all structural analysis can be found in ACME-ANA-002,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p133,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 138 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis – Safety Factors • Safety Factors for Safety Critical Components are Defined in Section 5.1.2 and 5.1.3 of SSP-52005 • Non pressurized metallic structures and fasteners will use 1.25 for yield and 2 for ultimate for margins of safety calculations • Pressurized components will have a safety factor greater than 2.5 to the ultimate • Pressurized Lines and Fittings will have a safety factor greater than 4.0 • Calculated using NSTS-08307 Pre-loaded Bolt Criteria and NASA TM 106943 • Torque based on MSFC-STD-486B • Fitting Factor of 1.15 is applied to all Margins of Safety Calculations • Joint separation of 1.2 is used for structural joints (1.4 for pressurized applications) All Safety Critical Fasteners:,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p134,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 139 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis – Analysis Methods • Structures are analyzed for stress using a combination of hand calculations and Finite Element Analysis (FEA) • FEA pre and post processing is performed using Femap Version 10.1 / 10.3 • Analysis models are run using NX NASTRAN 6.0 • The maximum von Mises stress is used for safety factor and margin calculations unless maximum principle stress is larger • Metallic Material Properties are obtained from MMPDS-06 • Margins of Safety are calculated below: 1*  y y y FSMS   1*  u u u FSMS    = component stress MSu = margin of safety to ultimate u = material ultimate strength FSu = ultimate safety factor  = component stress MSy = margin of safety to yield y = material yield strength FSy = yield safety factor,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p135,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 140 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis - Pressure ACME has two custom pressurized components exposed to an MDP of 135psia Input Manifold Switching Manifold Both are made of 300 Series Stainless Steel Ftu = 75,000 psi",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p136,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 141 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis - Pressure Both components are analyzed for stress using a finite element model Input Manifold Switching Manifold Max principle stress = 3,472 psi Safety Factor = 21 Max principle stress = 496 psi Safety Factor = 151",,False
