PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p140,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 145 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis – Launch The components below are explicitly modeled in a finite element model of the CIA Structure and analyzed for launch loading. 1) E Field Power Supply 2) Data Acquisition Cube 3) Camera Assembly 4) TFP Motor Assembly 5) Component Mount Bracket (2x) 6) Frame Rail (2x) 7) Switching Manifold 8) Bulkhead (2x) 9) Input Manifold 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 1 9,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p141,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 146 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Structural Analysis – Launch CIA Structure modeled using Solid and Plate elements with Rigid elements connecting the various components. Mass elements were used to adjust weights and CG of components. If the CG was relatively close to the component, then the material of that component was adjusted for the weight. Ballast Weight for Correct Mass and CG from Pro-E Model",,False
