PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p159,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 164 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies • Compare Air Velocities: Forced versus Free Convection • Using Grashof number and Reynolds number ratio to estimate equivalent air velocities. Velocity = 0.33m/sec for PCBs • Assess Air Flow in Camera Package • Velocity assessed at 0.66m/sec • All COTS components have case temperature with more than 11oC margin on the PCBs maximum ambient temperature. • Assess Air Flow in Avionic Package • Velocity assessed at 0.66m/sec • All COTS components have velocities greater than 0.66m/sec • DNA CUBE PCBs • No air flow • CUBE PCBs sub-modeled and tuned to test data. • Minimum thermal margin: 21.0oC on the Al-225 board. ACME Thermal Analysis COTS PCBs – Thermal Results,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p160,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 165 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies • Two COTS components fail to meet the 11oC margin guideline from SMC-TR-06-11 • Camera: -1.1oC • MFCs: 7.1oC • All other COTS components have margins greater than 11oC. ACME Thermal Analysis Other COTS Components – Thermal Results MFCs Camera Insert Assembly • Possible Mitigation • Increase water flow rate • Refine thermal loads • Revise thermal allowable based on ambient conditions in 1g.,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p161,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 166 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies • All Custom Components have large thermal margins • Insert Assembly • Upstream Relay PCBs: 28.2oC • Downstream Relay PCBs: 44.8oC • Camera Package • Camera Stepper Driver PCB: 64.4oC • Camera Control Power Distribution PCB: 61.2oC • Avionic Package • Power Distribution Assembly: 56.3oC ACME Thermal Analysis Custom Components – Thermal Results,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p162,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 167 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies • All other components with the exception of two have more than 11oC thermal margin. • Exceptions: • Insert Assembly, Camera • Insert Assembly, Mass Flow Controller (MFCs) • The ACME hardware meets the touch temperature requirement of SSP 51700. • The air flow rates through the camera package and the avionic package were less than 1.4m3/min with a 100Pa pressure drop across the package. ACME Thermal Analysis Conclusion Actions • Addition work is needed to resolve the thermal margins on the mass flow controllers (MFCs) and the Camera in the Insert Assembly. • Follow the mitigation approached defined earlier.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p163,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 168 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies ACME CIR Capabilities Used by ACME Chris Rogers – CIR/ACME Integration Lead,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p164,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 169 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Combustion Integrated Rack Goal Use the space environment as a laboratory for strategic research & technology experiments in physics, chemistry and biology to support Agency goals & the Nation’s vision new for space exploration. Objectives • Develop the Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) and the Fluids Integrated Rack (FIR) to support physical and biological research on board the ISS. • Develop the Ground Infrastructure, Integration, Operations, Logistics & Maintenance plans required for FCF sustaining engineering and operations. • CIR provides the only large environmental chamber (100 liters) on ISS in which the space environment, Lunar, Mars or other desired environment may be simulated (i.e., pressure, temperature, gaseous atmospheres, particulates, etc.) for long duration, on-orbit investigations and technology validations. • CIR provides easily reconfigurable diagnostics, customizable software, passive rack-level vibration isolation, and other subsystems that will support a wide range of investigations Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) Overview",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p165,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 170 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) Overview Fuel/Oxidizer Management Assembly (FOMA) • Gas Distribution • Exhaust Vent Optics Bench Combustion Chamber Rack Door International Standard Payload Rack (ISPR) SAMS RTS Passive Rack Isolation Subsystem (PaRIS) Environmental Control (ECS) • Air Thermal Control • Fire Detection & Suppression • Water Thermal Control • Gas Interfaces (GN2, VES) Input/Output Processor (IOP) Electrical Power Control Unit (EPCU) FOMA Control Unit (FCU) PI Avionics Science Diagnostics • Illumination Package • Low Light Level (2 Units) • High Bit Depth Multi-Spectral • High Frame Rate/High Resolution OR Experiment Specific Diagnostics Laptop Computer Optics Bench Slides FCF Common Element CIR Element PI Hardware Element Image Processing and Storage ACME CIA",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p166,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 171 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Payload Specific Hardware • Unique hardware components • Specific Diagnostics • Unique PI fuels ACME Chamber Insert • Platform for exchangeable burner: – Gas Delivery – Retracting ignitor – Electric field generator • Infrastructure that uniquely meets the needs of PI experiments • Unique science requirements FCF Combustion Integrated Rack • Power Supply • Avionics/Control • Structural Support & Power • Common Diagnostics and Illumination • Environmental Control • Data Processing/Distribution • Fluids Control/Distribution • Combustion Containment The Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) includes support subsystems and combustion diagnostics commonly needed for combustion investigations and supplements the laboratory with unique science hardware developed for each Principal Investigator (PI). Payload specific and multi-user hardware customizes the CIR in a unique laboratory configuration to perform research effectively. Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments Insert Assembly CIR Sub-rack Payload Relationship,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p167,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 172 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Combustion Chamber Combustion Chamber Power and Data Interface includes: • JCTC1– Provides 40 pairs of #22 gauge wire between IRR and PI Avionics connector through the Optics Bench • JCTC2 – Provides 27 pairs of #20 wire pairs between IRR and PI Avionics connector through the Optics Bench • JCTC3– Provides 2 Fiber Optic, single-mode 9.0 core/125 Cladding, 2 RG-179 coaxial cables and 5 pairs of #16 gauge wires to the PI Avionics location through the Optics Bench. • JCTC4 – Provides 49 pairs of #22 gauge wire pairs between IRR and PI Avionics connector through the Optics Bench Combustion Chamber General Info: • PIs may operate from .02 to 3.0 ATM • CIR Combustion Chamber rated 0 to 9 ATM • CIA useable: 396 mm (W) x 600 mm (L) • Internal free volume: 105 liters • Maximum Oxygen concentration of 30% • 6 Fluid Connections include (High Pressure Gas (1) GC sample port (1), SS Coolant inlet and outlet (2), Fuel (1) and Static Mixer (1).",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p168,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 173 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Combustion Chamber Atmosphere Mixing The oxidant MFC can provide up to 30 slpm (based on nitrogen (N2)) flow. The oxygen gas concentration is a function of the gas bottle size, as listed below. • 2.25 liter bottle provides a maximum of 50% O2, balance diluent at 2000 psia. • 3.8 liter bottle provides a maximum of 30% O2, balance diluent at 2000 psia. A Nitrogen manifold can supply inert gas types such as N2, He, and CO2, as well as oxidant blends below 30% oxygen, to the chamber. In addition, this manifold provides the interface for the utilization of the ISS supplied N2. This manifold also can directly route the pressurized gas to the chamber, by-passing the regulator. The N2 MFC can provide up to 30 slpm (based on nitrogen (N2)) flow.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p169,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 174 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Provided Equipment FCF/CIR diagnostics, equipment and resources to be provided to ACME are documented in the CIR to ACME Integration Agreement (FCF-IA-MV-ACME) *The CIR N2 Bypass Hose and the CIR N2 Bypass Pressure Regulator will be funded by ACME but procured, tested and verified by CIR per line item F in Section 3.2.3 0",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p170,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 175 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies • Design based on re-packaged commercial Agilent Micro GC instrument • Un-modified vendor supplied software for analysis • 2 PCB controllers • 3 detector columns • Column A – Molecular Sieve with Backflush • Column B – PoraPlot Q • Column C – OV1701 • Structural mounting, air-cooling, power and data interfaces through Optics Bench • Sample inlet and vent I/F’s through FOMA CIR GCIP",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p171,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 176 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Small FOMA Gas Bottle • Necessary as a control to hazard FCF-ACME-05, hazard control 1.1 • Based on analysis driven by hazard control the bottle properties are: • 150cc • 1815 psia • 1.5 x MDP • DOT 3E • oxygen mixtures only • Based on current FOMA bottle design",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p172,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 177 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – Optics Bench/UML UML - Universal Mounting Location • 8 locations on rear of CIR Optics Bench • Correspond to Chamber Windows UML provides interfaces for: • Mechanical w/ Air Cooling • 28 VDC power • Ethernet (cmd, control, h&s) • Sync Bus (± 1 Hz accuracy) • Analog Video (RS170/NTSC) • PI Mounting Location – Additional unique UML for PI Avionics Package IPSU IPSU IPSU FCU PI Avionics Chamber Camera Packages",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p173,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 178 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics Packages are mounted on the Optics Bench at one of the 8 UML locations around the Chamber. Diagnostics Packages are designed to align with the centerline of the Chamber Windows. Modular build format allows for on-orbit reconfiguration of components. Changes require Crew Time! CIR Diagnostics – Package Form Camera Diagnostic Control Module Relay Filter UML Objective Lens Folding Prism,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p174,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 179 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – HiBMs/Illumination HiBMs Package • Used by ACME for Soot Volume Fraction View • Based on 1024 x 1024 CCD, 12 bit output • Frame Rate: 30 fps (60 fps via Binning) • Modular Relay Lens determines FOV • 30 mm, 50 mm, 90 mm (not on orbit) • Narrow Band Filter @ 653 nm to isolate background illumination Illumination Package • Used as backlight for HiBMs Package • Laser Diode @ 653 nm provides monochromatic, uniform background FLEX Heptane Burn",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p175,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 180 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – HiBMs-2 Fiber FLEX Heptane Burn @ 700nm HiBMs-2 Package •Used by ACME for Soot Temperature Imaging & Thin Filament Pyrometry View • Based on 1024 x 1024 CCD, 12 bit output • Frame Rate: 30 fps (60 fps via Binning) • Modular Relay Lens determines FOV • 30 mm, 50 mm, 90 mm (not on orbit) • Liquid Crystal Tunable Filter (LCTF) is switchable - Wavelengths: 650 – 1050 nm • Allows for 2 Wavelength Pyrometry • Broadband Filter (BK7) also available (in stowage) for higher light throughput.",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p176,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 181 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – LLL-UV FLEX Heptane Burn LLL-UV Package •Used by ACME for Ultraviolet Imaging View • Based on 1024 x 1024 CCD, 12 bit output • Frame Rate: 30 fps (60 fps via Binning) • Modular Relay Lens determines FOV • 50 mm, 80 mm (not on orbit) • Used w/ integrated Gen-II UV Intensifier • Flame Imaging Filter Options (on orbit): • OH* @ 310 nm • CH* @ 431 nm",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p177,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 182 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – IPSU IPSU (Image Processing & Storage Unit) • Currently 1 IPSU is required for each Camera Package • Mounted on the Optics Bench at one of the 8 UML locations around the Chamber. • Camera data interface based on custom fiber-optic link: Serial Data Link (SDL) • SDL interface is not compatible w/ any off-the-shelf Cameras • Requires Fiber-optic cable from Camera to IPSU • Images to the ground is 2 step process: • Transfer: IPSU to IOP (CIR main computer) ~ 10 mbps • Downlink: IOP to Ground via HRDL (high-rate data link) ~ 20 mbps,,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p178,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 183 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies CIR Diagnostics – IPSU-G IPSU-G (GigE upgrade to IPSU) • Currently in development by CIR & scheduled to fly in early 2016. • Supports both GigE (GigE Vision Std) & USB-3 Camera interfaces. • Supports up to 4 cameras • Not compatible w/ current CIR Cameras • Mounts on Optics Bench at UML 1, 3 or 7. • Includes a direct HRDL interface to ISS. • ACME Color Camera compatible w/ IPSU-G (Images can be Downlinked via HRDL directly) • Images from existing IPSUs to the ground is still a 2 step process, but faster: • Transfer: IPSU to IPSU-G ~ 32 mbps • Downlink: IPSU-G to Ground via HRDL (high-rate data link) ≥ 20 mbps IPSU-G",,False
