PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p183,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 188 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies FCF Utilization Process • The FCF Utilization Process is defined in FCF-PLN-0875 • Primary functions of the Integration process are: • Payload Planning • Mission Integration • Engineering Integration • Operations Planning • FCF/CIR provides the following resources • An integration liaison to assist with the Utilization Process • Integrating Sub-rack Payload into CIR • Integrating CIR/Sub-rack Payload to ISS • Services in support of Sub-rack Payload • CIR Provided Hardware (IPSUs, HiBMs, UV Imaging, IOP hard drives, etc) • Gas filling services • Launch Site Processing Support • TADs updates • Further resources provided by CIR and agreements between CIR and payload provider are documented in the CIR/Payload Unique Integration Agreement",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p184,0,ACME Critical Design Review– 189 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies FCF Utilization Process • Payload Planning • Payload Kick-Off Meeting • Documents and Templates • Develop payload to CIR Integration Agreement (IA) • Develop payload to CIR Interface Control Document (ICD) • Collect payload Integration Agreement (IA) Addenda data inputs and combine inputs for FCF submittal per increment • Preliminary Payload Data Collection and Analysis • Utilization Tools • Payload Data Inputs • Payload-Unique Integration Documentation • IA Main Volume (MV) • Utilization Schedule • External Preliminary Interface Revision Notices (PIRNs)/ Change Requests (CRs)/Exceptions,,False
