PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p196,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 201 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Concept of Operations ACME Concept of Operations • Designed for autonomous, ground tended operations • Experiment is configured/reconfigured by the crew, then operated from the ground • Experiment progress monitored by the operations team and PI’s • Ops team will uplink commands to perform experiment operations and collect data • ACME’s primary ground operations site is the GRC TSC (Telescience Support Center) ISS POIC GRC TSC CIR Ops Team ACME Ops Team Payload Investigator Crew FCF",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p197,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 202 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Operations Flow Hardware configure, power up for checkout, chamber fill, test point operations, reconfigurations, power down No No No Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes No No Uplink setup & test point parameters Preform pre-test setup procedures Perform test point operations & save data Transfer data to IOP, acquire downlink and downlink data Command FOMA to reconfigure chamber atmosphere Crew reconfigures CIA hardware Crew reconfigures gas bottles/ adsorber cartridge Install diagnostics package and avionics package Install gas bottles and adsorber cartridge Configure and install ACME CIA Power up* / experiment self- test / fill for N2 leak test Command FOMA to fill chamber with science gas Power Down*/ Uninstall ACME *Power up/Power down is done on a daily basis and after/before crew operations. Same test conditions? Finished daily test points? Change atmosphere? Change CIA hardware? Change gas bottles? Additional tests?",,False
