PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p204,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 209 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies Crew Procedures & Training Crew Procedures • Crew procedures will be written and baselined for all initial configure activities as well as nominal replacement activities (Initial July 2014, Baselined May 2015) Crew Training • Training Strategy Team (TST) meeting to be held Fall 2013 to develop training plan • Crew training will consist of an ACME class and the CIR class (Start Fall 2014) • ACME will provide a CIA trainer with working interfaces for crew training (Summer 2014)",,False
PSI-23,Engineering Documents,PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-23/Engineering Documents/PSI-23_Engineering Documents_ACME CDR_Presentation_Package.pdf,p205,0,"ACME Critical Design Review– 210 Glenn Research Center ZIN Technologies HFIT • Initial meeting with Crew Office and HFIT held September 2013 • Developed Operations Nomenclature acceptable by crew office (Final due June 2014) • HFIT looked at drawings and found no concerns • Developed initial packing strategy for shipping hardware to orbit • Developed initial labeling strategy • IPLAT review of crew interface label drawings: Initial ~ May 2014, Final ~ May 2015 • Final HFIT Hardware evaluation, COC Issued ~August 2015",,False
