PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p1,0,"BASS-II SCIENCE REQUIREMENTS • General Requirements – 20 samples for each of the 5 PIs will be flow (including 20 clear pmma rods, 20 black pmma rods (varied diameters for both); 19 SIBAL samples, 1 4 cm pmma spherical section, 20 pmma films (varied thicknesses) and 20 pmma slabs (varied thicknesses and 1 sided or 2 sided holders). Also 3 Nomex-III samples. – 27 additional igniter wires will be flown. Solid fuel ignition uses a Kanthal hot wire. – ISS nitrogen gas will be used (0 to 500 SCCM N2). Instead of connecting the Experiment Assembly to a gas bottle it is connected via the GN2 hose to the MSG GN2 interface. GN2 is used to vitiate the MSG working volume to desired O2 levels. – 8 additional flash cards will be flow for the still camera. • Parameter Measurement – Measurement of the GN2 flow rate, fan voltage, air flow velocity and direction, and flame radiation will be measured and overlaid on the Video. – The acquisition rate of 4 Hz can not be changed from SPICE/BASS. – The measurement accuracy of ±10% was met by the SPICE hardware prior to its launch. • Imaging Requirements – The field of view of the video can not be changed from BASS. – The D300s still image requirements are the same as for BASS. 4/14/2010 1",,False
PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p2,0,"BASS-II SCIENCE REQUIREMENTS • Acceleration – BASS-II testing will be scheduled around planned thruster firing or spacecraft dock or undock. – The acceleration environment will be measured by a nearby SAMS during BASS-II testing. • MSG Working Volume Gas Concentrations – Project will include steps in crew procedures to install a Compound Specific Analyzer (CSA-CP) and the CO2 sensor (CDM) into the MSG to measure the Oxygen concentration. These devices will provide readings before and after each burn of the MSG working volume well mixed gas concentrations. Calibration checks will utilize the Columbus and Node 3 O2 and CO2 readings. • Crew support – Crew time is needed to conduct the BASS-II experiments. As part of the nominal ops, the crew establishes the desired test ambient atmosphere and flow. The crew manually inserts the fuel sample, adjusts the fuel location and igniter position within the camera fields of view. The crew manually ignites the sample and triggers the still camera. The crew performs flow calibration and soot cleaning as needed. – The crew works closely with the BASS-II PI team to determine test settings and provide real-time feedback during each burn. 4/14/2010 2",,False
PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p3,0,"BASS-II SUCCESS CRITERIA • Minimal Success: 10 samples from each PI (of their total 20) will be successfully tested per PI matrices at the desired test conditions (O2, flow). Ignition is successful for these tests, and flame video data is obtained. Still camera data is obtained for at least 7 tests per PI. Valuable information informing SoFIE science requirements is obtained. • Complete Success: All PI samples (100) are tested at the desired test conditions. Video data is obtained for all tests. Ignition occurs in most of the tests (90+). Extinction is observed for tests that seek to find a flammability limit. Most of the tests (90+) provide still camera data. Valuable information informing SoFIE science requirements is obtained. 4/14/2010 3",,False
PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p4,0,"6/6/2023 The manifest includes the following items utilizing designs that have previously flown: 27 ignitors with 9 of each of the 3 different types assembled per S1183MFA0015, S1183MFA0020, and S1183MFA0025. 8 Flash Cards - 4 GB Capacity (Different vendor from original, same functionality) 15 SIBAL Samples (2 cm wide) – Previously Flown Design - S1183MFA1020 4 SIBAL Samples (1 cm wide) – Previously Flown Design - S1183MFA1025 3 NOMEX Samples (2 cm wide) – Previously Flown Design - S1183MFA1055 BASS-II Hardware Manifest",,False
PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p5,0,"6/6/2023 The manifest includes the following newly designs hardware: 8 Flat 2 cm PMMA Samples (0.1 mm thick) - S1183MFA1110-1 4 Flat 2 cm PMMA Samples (0.2 mm thick) - S1183MFA1110-2 2 Flat 2 cm PMMA Samples (0.3, 0.4, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, and 5.0 mm thick) - S1183MFA1110-3 thru S1183MFA1110-9 4 Flat 1 cm PMMA Samples (0.2 mm thick) - S1183MFA1115-1 1 Flat 1 cm PMMA Samples (1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, and 5.0 mm thick) – S1183MFA1115-2 thru S1183MFA1110-6 14 Black PMMA Rod Samples (0.25” Diameter) - S1183MFA1090-1 6 Black PMMA Rod Samples (0.375” Diameter) - S1183MFA1090-2 2 Black PMMA Rod Samples (0.500” Diameter) - S1183MFA1090-3 12 Clear PMMA Rod Samples (0.25” Diameter) - S1183MFA1095-1 4 Clear PMMA Rod Samples (0.375” Diameter) - S1183MFA1095-2 2 Clear PMMA Rod Samples (0.500” Diameter) - S1183MFA1095-3 1 Flat 2 cm PMMA one-sided Samples (1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, and 5.0 mm thick) – S1183MFA1120-1 thru S1183MFA1120-5 1 Sphere Sample 4 cm - S1183MFA1085 BASS-II Hardware Manifest",,False
