PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p13,1,"Bhattacharjee Priority Test # O2 Flow(s) Sample #/type/description brief objective of test notes 1 21 0 mm/s A.1/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study thickness effect 2 21 0 mm/s B.1/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 20 mm study thickness effect 3 21 0 mm/s D.1/PMMA/thickness 0.3 mm, width 20 mm study thickness effect 4 21 20 mm/s A.2/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/flow effect 5 21 0 mm/s C.1/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 10 mm study width effect 6 15 0 mm/s A.4/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study oxygen effect 7 21 0 mm/s E.1/PMMA/thickness 0.4 mm, width 20 mm study thickness effect 8 21 20 mm/s B.2/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/thickness/flow effect 9 21 50 mm/s A.3/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/flow effect 10 21 50 mm/s C.3/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 10 mm study width/flow effect 11 21 50 mm/s B.3/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/thickness effect 12 21 50 mm/s D.2/PMMA/thickness 0.3 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/thickness effect 13 21 50 mm/s E.2/PMMA/thickness 0.4 mm, width 20 mm study boundary layer/thickness effect 14 21 50 mm/s C.2/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 10 mm study oxygen/width effect 15 15 20 mm/s A.5/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study oxygen/flow/thickness effect 16 15 50 mm/s A.6/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm study oxygen/flow/thickness effect 17 15 50 mm/s B.4/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 20 mm study oxygen/flow/thickness effect 18 15",,False
PSI-25,Science Documents,PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-25/Science Documents/PSI-25_Science Documents_BASS-II_SRD.pdf,p13,2,"50 mm/s C.4/PMMA/thickness 0.2 mm, width 10 mm study oxygen/width effect 19 21 0 mm/s A.7/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm test data repeatability 20 21 20 mm/s A.8/PMMA/thickness 0.1 mm, width 20 mm test data repeatability Note: There are 5 types of samples categorized by the letters A-E (part No from Dr. Olson's Excel sheet). A(S1183MFA1110- 1): 0.1 mm thick 20 mm wide (8 each); B(S1183MFA1110-2): 0.2 mm thick 20 mm wide (4 each); C(S1183MFA1115-1): 0.2mm thick 10 cm wide (4 each); D(S1183MFA1110- 3): 0.3 mm thick 20 cm wide (2 each); E(S1183MFA1110-4): 0.4 mm thick 20 cm wide (2 each);",,False
