PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_FlammabilityAspectsofCottonFiberglassFabric_ASGSR2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_FlammabilityAspectsofCottonFiberglassFabric_ASGSR2012.pdf,p25,0,Digital still camera images for 2-cm-wide fuel with opposed airflow = 10 cm/s. Images are taken every 1.25 sec (starting at top and moving from left to right). Flame quickly reaches steady state and goes out when it runs out of fuel. Note: Downward flame spread (opposed flow) in 1-g with this material is not possible in normal air. 10 cm/s Airflow 2 cm,,False
PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_FlammabilityAspectsofCottonFiberglassFabric_ASGSR2012.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_FlammabilityAspectsofCottonFiberglassFabric_ASGSR2012.pdf,p26,0,"Digital still camera images showing a flame burning a 2-cm wide cotton-fiberglass fabric in opposed flow. Images are taken every 1.25 sec (starting at top and moving from left to right). The flow is decreased in discrete steps from 10 cm/s all the way down to about 1 cm/s. The flame response to flow changes is very rapid, and the flow effects on the flame and its spread rate are dramatic. Total burn time is 90 sec. Flow changes are indicated by numbers. Airflow 6 cm/s 4 cm/s 2 cm/s 10 cm/s 1.5 cm/s 1 cm/s",,False
