PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_BASS_Overview of Recent ISS Results.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_BASS_Overview of Recent ISS Results.pdf,p54,0,Top view image montage for a 1-cm wide flat acrylic sample burning in air at low flow speed (around 9 cm/s). Images progress from left to right then top to bottom (1.3 seconds between images). The air flow direction is from right to left. The flame is about 1 cm in size and can persist for a very long time at this low air flow speed. The flame goes out only in the last two frames when the air flow is completely shut off. Flow,,False
PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_BASS_Overview of Recent ISS Results.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_BASS_Overview of Recent ISS Results.pdf,p56,0,"Flow of less than 1 cm/s. Near the end of the burn, a jet of nitrogen is imposed but it fails to extinguish the flame. Finally after a series of flow reductions, the flame goes out when the flow speed is zero. Fuel: PMMA; 15-mm initial diameter; 17% O2/N2; 1 atm; Time between images: 1.3 sec Flow",,False
