PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_Flammability Aspects of Fabric_USNationalCombustion2013.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_Flammability Aspects of Fabric_USNationalCombustion2013.pdf,p27,0,"Digital still camera images showing a flame burning a 2-cm wide cotton-fiberglass fabric in opposed flow. Images are taken every 1.25 sec (starting at top and moving from left to right). The flow is decreased in discrete steps from 10 cm/s all the way down to about 1 cm/s. The flame response to flow changes is very rapid, and the flow effects on the flame and its spread rate are dramatic. Total burn time is 90 sec. Flow changes are indicated by numbers. Airflow 6 cm/s 4 cm/s 2 cm/s 10 cm/s 1.5 cm/s 1 cm/s",,False
