PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.1.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.1.pdf,p5,0,11/23/2011 Obtain Engineering Board Assessment on the acceptability of the SLICE and BASS hardware to proceed with shipment for flight ULF5 MPLM scheduled for launch in September 2010. System Acceptance Review Purpose,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.1.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.1.pdf,p6,0,"SLICE HARDWARE OVERVIEW • SLICE will utilize the SPICE hardware currently on ISS – Experiment Assembly, Cables, Control Box, Video Camera • SLICE will refurbish the SPICE Gas Bottles for re-flight • SLICE will design, fab, assemble, test new hardware – 2.1 mm and 3.2 mm burner tubes – Upgraded Nikon Still Camera – Blue-Green Filter – Ceramic Pyrometry Fiber 4/14/2010 6",,False
