PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p4,0,SLICE/BASS Project Team Project Manager Responsibility Robert Hawersaat GRC Project Manager Paul Ferkul BASS Principal Investigator Sandra Olson BASS Co-Investigator James Tien BASS Co-Investigator Fumi Takahashi BASS/SLICE Co-Investigator Marshall Long SLICE Principal Investigator Mitch Smooke SLICE Co-Investigator Dennis Stocker SLICE Co-Investigator Jay Owens Imaging/Optics Mike Johnston Research Assistant Tibor Lorik ZIN Project Lead Chuck Bunnell Mechanical/Operations Chris Bodzioney/Debra Lyden Safety Chris Dixon Mechanical Designer Kevin Dendorfer Technician Jim Bruewer Mechanical Engineer 6/16/2010 4,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p5,0,System Acceptance Review Purpose Obtain Executive Board Assessment on the acceptability of the SLICE and BASS hardware to proceed with shipment for STS-133/Flight ULF-5 MPLM scheduled for launch in September 2010. 6/16/2010 5,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p6,0,"SLICE HARDWARE OVERVIEW • SLICE will utilize the SPICE hardware currently on ISS. – Experiment Assembly, Cables, Control Box, Video Camera. • SLICE will refurbish the SPICE Gas Bottles for re-flight. • SLICE will design, fab, assemble, test new hardware. – 2.1 mm and 3.2 mm burner tubes – Upgraded Nikon Still Camera – Blue-Green Filter – Ceramic Pyrometry Fiber 6/16/2010 6",,False
