PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p11,0,SLICE HARDWARE OVERVIEW 6/16/2010 11,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p12,0,"SLICE SUCCESS CRITERIA • Minimum Success -– Still images are acquired for at least 15 different lifted flames with different combinations of fuel flow and air velocity with a single fuel, or at least 10 different lifted flames each of two fuels, or at least 5 different lifted flames each of 3 or more fuels. • High Success -– Still images are acquired of at least 30 different lifted flames total from at least 3 different fuels. The still images are acquired with a blackbody characterized camera for soot pyrometry or liftoff limits are determined for at least one fuel. • Complete Success -– Testing conducted with all 12 fuel bottles, with identification of stability limits and smoke points (within the range of the SPICE velocity limits). Still images are taken of lifted flames with a blackbody characterized camera. 6/16/2010 12",,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p13,0,SLICE PI Endorsement 6/16/2010 13,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p14,0,SLICE PRODUCT VERIFICATION TESTING • D300s Still Camera – Functional Test – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete – Radiated Emissions Test – RE02 – Complete • The original plan was to use similarity of design from the original camera however the EME panel on 5/13/10 informed the project that it will be required to perform a radiated emissions test. – Thermal Operating Test per 60054-TST-009 – Complete • 4 cycles from 10 to 45 ˚C – Materials Bake-out for 72 hours at 120 ˚F – Complete • The SPICE off-gas testing using the similar D100 camera as well as all other SPICE hardware has a total T value of 0.001152. Using this value for just the new BASS D300s camera will provide sufficient margin as well as allow the payload to remain below the 0.5 limit. – Black Body Calibration and Focus Setup using Replacement Top Window. – 6/17/10 • Burner Tubes – Perform dimensioning calibration - Complete • Replacement Top Window – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete – Anneal at 250˚F for 1 hour - Complete – Materials Bake-out for 72 hours at 120 ˚F - Complete 6/16/2010 14,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p15,0,SLICE PRODUCT VERIFICATION TESTING • Ceramic Pyrometry Fiber – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 – Complete • Engineering Vibe Test passed • Gas Bottles – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 – Complete – Pre and Post Vibe Helium Leak Test – Complete – Fill per Table above – Complete 6/16/2010 15,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p16,0,SAFETY VERIFICATIONS • SLICE is designated as a SPICE re-flight. • Out of Board Approval is expected once verifications are closed. • 77 Safety Verifications – 59 Closed Verifications – 14 Crew Procedure Controls – Procedures are being developed – 8/10 – 2 EMI TIA Approval for D300s Camera – 7/10 – 1 HFIT Inspection at turnover – 6/23/10 – 1 Stowage Configuration Verification – 7/10/10 6/16/2010 16,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p17,0,INTEGRATION VERIFICATIONS • Utilize SPICE ICD as a baseline for the integration requirements with MSG. • New verifications not addressed in the safety verifications include the following: – Fit Check for D300s Still Camera in MSG EU – Complete – Still Camera Video Interface Test in MSG EU - Complete – Labeling – Complete @ KSC • Physical and Functional Interface testing in the MSG EU with the new camera were successful. • Modified SPICE crew procedures were dry run to evaluate their status. Other than minor tweaks the procedures are adequate. 6/16/2010 17,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p18,0,SCHEDULE HIGHLIGHTS (Open Work) • All hardware assembly and test is complete! • Verification Closures are still in process as noted • Hardware Turnover @KSC – 6/24/10 • Bench Review – 7/8/10 6/16/2010 18,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p19,0,SLICE OPEN NCR Status • Radiated Emissions Exceedence of the D300s Camera. – NCR will close upon receiving an approved TIA. • Failure of the D300s camera during thermal testing. – Closure will not occur until hardware is returned to the vendor for failure analysis and repair. 6/16/2010 19,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p20,0,"SAR-1 Concerns & Issues • As-Built inspections of flight hardware was scheduled after the originally scheduled SAR-2 on 6/11/10. – The as-built inspections have been completed. DD250 is in the process of being generated with the planned turnover to GRC at 3 PM today, 6/18/10. • Stowage Configuration Drawings to close safety verification showing proper stow of the hardware will be finalized at the Bench Review scheduled for 7/8/10. – The PD will obtain the drawings once the updates have been made and include them in a memo to close the verification. • The D300s Camera completed EMI testing with the final results provided to MSG and the EME panel. Due to some small exceedances from the requirement the payload generated an NCR. MSG is generating a TIA to submit to the EME panel for approval. Approval is expected. • Crew Procedures are in draft form and are not planned to be completed until after SAR-2. – Crew procedures will be reviewed to include required safety controls. Operations will not be conducted until these safety verifications have been closed. 6/16/2010 20",,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p21,0,"BASS HARDWARE OVERVIEW • BASS will utilize the SPICE hardware currently on ISS. – Experiment Assembly, Cables, Video Camera • BASS will utilize the SLICE Still Camera. • BASS will design, fab, assemble, test new hardware. – Modified 3.2 mm burner tube – GN2 Hose Assembly – Sample Frame Assembly Insert for Experiment Assembly – 4 different fuel holder designs for a total of 41 fuel samples – BASS Control Box – Fan Flow Block Assembly – Ignitor Wire Extension Assembly 6/16/2010 21",,False
