PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p29,0,BASS PRODUCT VERIFICATION TESTING • Sample Frame Assembly – Fit Check with Engineering Assembly - Complete – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete – Materials Bake-out for 72 hours at 120 ˚F - Complete – EMI Test for Magnet Strength - Complete • Fuel Samples Assembly (41 flight units) – Fit Check with Engineering Assembly - Complete – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete • GN2 Hose Assembly – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete – Pre and Post Vibe Helium Leak Test - Complete • BASS Control Box – Functional Test with Engineering Assembly - Complete – Soft Stow Vibration per 60054-TST-007 - Complete – Materials Bake-out for 72 hours at 120 ˚F - Complete • Ignitor Wire Extension Assembly – Functional Test with Engineering Assembly – Complete 6/16/2010 29,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p30,0,SAFETY VERIFICATIONS • BASS safety package utilizes the SPICE package but it is a stand-alone payload. • 61 Safety Verifications – 46 Closed Verifications – 11 Crew Procedure Controls – Procedures are being developed – 8/10 – 2 EMI TIA Approval for D300s Camera – 1 HFIT Inspection at turnover – 6/23/10 – 1 Stowage Configuration Verification – 7/10/10 6/16/2010 30,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p31,0,"INTEGRATION VERIFICATIONS • Utilize SPICE ICD as a baseline for the integration requirements with MSG. • New verifications not addressed in the safety verifications include the following: – Fit Check for BASS Control Box & GN2 Hose in MSG EU – Complete – Labeling - Complete @ KSC – Combustion By-products compatibility assessment with MSG Filters – Complete • Physical and Functional Interface testing in the MSG EU with the new Control Box were successful. • Preliminary BASS crew procedures were dry run to evaluate their status. The procedures generally are in good shape with a couple of issues. – The number of images expected to be acquired may limit the number of runs that can be performed in each session. There are eight 4 GB flash disks that will need to be transferred to a laptop, down-linked, and verified all were received prior to flash disks being erased to be reused. – The project is still evaluating the various modes available with the new camera of acquiring images. 6/16/2010 31",,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p32,0,SCHEDULE HIGHLIGHTS (Open Work) • All hardware assembly and test is complete! • Verification Closures are still in process as noted. • Hardware Turnover @KSC – 6/24/10 • Bench Review – 7/8/10 6/16/2010 32,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p33,0,BASS OPEN NCR Status • Radiated Emissions Exceedence of the D300s Camera. – NCR will close upon receiving an approved TIA. • Failure of the D300s camera during thermal testing. – Closure will not occur until hardware is returned to the vendor for failure analysis and repair. 6/16/2010 33,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p34,0,SAR-1 Concerns & Issues • The completion of the ECLSS Assessment of combustion by-products was scheduled after the originally scheduled SAR-2 on 6/11/10. – ECLSS has provided an assessment that shows the combustion by-products are compatible with the ECLSS system. • Stowage Configuration Drawings to close safety verification showing proper stow of the hardware will be finalized at the Bench Review scheduled for 7/8/10. – The PD will obtain the drawings once the updates have been made and include them in a memo to close the verification. • Crew Procedures are in draft form and are not planned to be completed until after SAR-2. – Crew procedures will be reviewed to include required safety controls. Operations will not be conducted until these safety verifications have been closed. • The touch temperature report was not approved at the time of SAR-1. – The report is approved and in CM. 6/16/2010 34,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p35,0,"PROJECT CONCLUSION The hardware developed to support the SLICE and BASS payloads has been designed, tested, and verified using approved processes resulting in what is expected to be highly successful operations. 6/16/2010 35",,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p36,0,SAR-1 Board Assessment • Jim Cockrell will discuss the SLICE BASS System Acceptance Review (SAR-1) Board’s findings • The SLICE BASS SAR-1 Chair’s Synopsis letter is available on the eRoom • Each of the open items at SAR-1 for SLICE is addressed on chart 20 • Each of the open items at SAR-1 for BASS is addressed on chart 34 6/16/2010 36,,False
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_BASS_SysAcceptanceReview.2.pdf,p37,0,ZIN Quality Assessment • Quality – SLICE/BASS followed the ZIN Technology Quality Management System for engineering and building flight hardware. – For this re-flight SLICE/BASS: • Used Manufacturing Work Orders (MWO) prepared for cleaning and assembly operations. • Use inspection and test documents prepared for in-process and final inspection/test activities – all completed plans are nominally reviewed/approved by a ZIN Tech Quality representative. • Will achieve configuration verification through as-built inspections performed by a ZIN Tech’s Quality representative as part of the MWO process. 6/16/2010 37,,False
