PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_BASS Overview.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_BASS Overview.pptx,slide 1,0,"Principal Investigator: Paul Ferkul, NCSER Co-Investigators: Sandra Olson, NASA GRC James T’ien, CWRU Fumiaki Takahashi, NCSER Project Manager: Robert Hawersaat, NASA GRC Imaging: Jay Owens, NCSER Engineering Team: Tibor Lorik, ZIN Technologies, Inc. Chuck Bunnell, ZIN Technologies, Inc. Burning And Suppression of Solids (BASS)",,False
PSI-26,Presentations,PSI-26_Presentations_BASS Overview.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Presentations/PSI-26_Presentations_BASS Overview.pptx,slide 2,0,"Overall Experiment Hardware Summary: BASS will utilize the on-orbit SPICE hardware which was launched on STS-126 and operates on ISS. Minor modifications needed to burn solid samples. Small flow tunnel Solid samples are installed, ignited, extinguished, and recorded Video and 35mm still camera provides bulk of the data. Flame appearance, behavior, spread rate, and extinction dynamics will be measured Airflow speed is main variable; some cases will be vitiated or extinguished using nitrogen from nozzle Burning And Suppression of Solids (BASS)",,False
