PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SPICE_FanHousing.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SPICE_FanHousing.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: 7075-T651 ALUMINUM. 2. 1.6 Ra ALL OVER. 3. BEAD BLAST ALL SURFACES. POLISH EXTERIOR SURFACES TO UNIFORM LUSTER USING MEDIUM SCOTCH BRITE PAD, EXCLUDE POCKETS AND BORES. 4. IDENTIFY BY TAGGING WITH DRAWING PART NUMBER 60054MDFH002, PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. 5. QUANTITY: ONE REQUIRED. ### Dimensions (mm; boxed = basic) Front (flange) view: - Flange outline: 108 x 108 (basic); corner radii 4 X R3 - Inner pocket: □98, position ⌖ 0.2Ⓜ | A | BⓂ | CⓂ; corner radii 4 X R2 - Threaded hole pattern: 87 x 87 (basic); 4 X M3 X 0.5-6H ↧ 7, position ⌖ Ø0.2 | A | BⓂ | CⓂ - Through holes: 6 X Ø3.58/3.40, position ⌖ Ø0.2Ⓜ | A | BⓂ | CⓂ - 54 (basic) from bottom hole row to section line A-A; 36 to Detail A notch - Section A-A cut across the centre; SEE DETAIL A at the lower notch Side view: - Body depth 63; flange thickness 5; 2; R2 (2 places); R0.5 MAX Rear view: - Outline 114 x 114 (datums B, C); corner radii 4 X R3, 4 X R2, 2 X R - Opening □82, position ⌖ 0.5Ⓜ | A | BⓂ | CⓂ - Slot: 92 wide, position ⌖ 0.5Ⓜ | A | CⓂ; 6.4; 5.7 Section A-A: - □93, position ⌖ 0.2Ⓜ | A; 3; R0.5 max; SEE DETAIL B Detail A (scale 4:1): notch 1.5 wide, 3, 3; position ⌖ 0.2Ⓜ | A; R Detail B (scale 4:1): 2 X R0.5 MAX; 3",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample2mm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample2mm.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Part drawing (A2, landscape, ZIN Technologies / NASA Glenn) of a 2 mm thick clear cast-acrylic (PMMA) flat fuel sample strip with one rounded end: plan view, edge view, end view and isometric. **Title:** PMMA FLAT FUEL SAMPLE - 2MM THICK **Drawing number:** S1183MFD1066 — REV - (none) — SIZE A2 — SCALE 4/1 — SHEET 1 OF 1 **Next assembly (title block):** FLAT FUEL SAMPLE ASSEMBLY (2MM THICK) S1183MFA1065 Initial release date: 2/8/10 — BLDG: ZIN — AREA: GRC — UNITS: mm — DISCIPLINE: MECHANICAL Contract number: NNC09BA02B — Delivery order: SPACE118 — Model name: S1183MFD1066 — Pro/E Version: Wildfire 2.0 Project lead / Quality / Safety / Engineer / Designer / Reviewer: [name omitted], each dated 2/8/10 Approved: [name omitted], date 2/9/10 NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO ZIN TECHNOLOGIES (company block; address/phone omitted) Revisions table (CHG / ZONE / DESCRIPTION / APP/DATE): no entries. THIS DRAWING IS UNDER CONFIGURATION CONTROL: DO NOT REVISE WITHOUT APPROVED ECO. PRIOR TO USE CHECK FOR ANY OUTSTANDING ECO'S WITH CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT OFFICE.",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample2mm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample2mm.pdf,p1,1,"Title-block general notes (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED): 1. ALL DIMENSIONING AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN MILLIMETERS 3. BREAK EDGES: 0.2-0.5 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: 0.5-6 ±0.1; OVER 6-30 ±0.2; OVER 30-120 ±0.3; OVER 120-315 ±0.5; OVER 315-1000 ±0.8; OVER 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCES: 0° 30' THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION. ### Notes 1. MATERIAL: CAST ACRYLIC SHEET (CLEAR) MCMASTER CARR PART NUMBER: 8560K181. OR USE AN ENGINEER APPROVED EQUIVALENT. 2. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS AND ALL PROCESSES. 3. CLEAN ONLY BY IMMERSION IN MILD SOAP SOLUTION IN DISTILLED WATER. RINSE WITH DISTILLED WATER AND AIR DRY. 4. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 5. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Dimensions (mm) - Length: 50 - Width: 10 - Corner radii (one end, plan view): 2X R3.2 - Edge radius (edge view): R1 - Thickness: (2 STOCK)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Assembly drawing (A2, landscape, ZIN Technologies / NASA Glenn) of the 2 cm SIBAL flat fuel sample assembly: exploded isometric of the layered stack (frames, insulators, SIBAL sample, igniter), plan view, edge view and Detail A of the Kanthal igniter wire, with part list, commercial part list and notes. **Title:** FLAT FUEL SAMPLE ASSEMBLY (2CM) 2CM SIBAL FLAT SAMPLE **Drawing number:** S1183MFA1020 — REV A — SIZE A2 — SCALE 2/1 — SHEET 1 OF 1 **Next assembly (title block):** BURNING AND SUPPRESSION OF SOLIDS S1183MFA1000 Initial release date: 3/8/10 — BLDG: ZIN — AREA: GRC — UNITS: mm — DISCIPLINE: MECHANICAL Contract number: NNC09BA02B — Delivery order: SPACE118 — Model name: S1183MFA1020 — Pro/E Version: Wildfire 2.0 Project lead / Quality / Safety / Engineer: [name omitted], dated 3/8/10; Designer / Reviewer: [name omitted], dated 2/8/10 Approved: [name omitted], date 10/6/10 NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO ZIN TECHNOLOGIES (company block; address/phone omitted) THIS DRAWING IS UNDER CONFIGURATION CONTROL: DO NOT REVISE WITHOUT APPROVED ECO. PRIOR TO USE CHECK FOR ANY OUTSTANDING ECO'S WITH CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT OFFICE. ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | REVISED PER BASS-ECO-011 | [name omitted] - 9/29/10; [name omitted] - 9/29/10 |",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,p1,1,Title-block general notes (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED): 1. ALL DIMENSIONING AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN MILLIMETERS 3. BREAK EDGES: 0.2-0.5 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: 0.5-6 ±0.1; OVER 6-30 ±0.2; OVER 30-120 ±0.3; OVER 120-315 ±0.5; OVER 315-1000 ±0.8; OVER 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCES: 0° 30' THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION. ### Part list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 2 | S1183MFD1021 | FLAT SAMPLE FRAME - 2CM TOP / BOTTOM | | 2 | 2 | S1183MFD1023 | FLAT SAMPLE INSULATOR - 2CM TOP / BOTTOM | | 3 | 1 | S1183MFD1022 | SIBAL FLAT FUEL SAMPLE - 2CM | | 4 | 1 | S1183MFA0010 | IGNITER ASSEMBLY (FLAT) | ### Commercial part list | ITEM | QTY | MIL SPEC / VENDOR PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | AR | ITW DEVCON: 14355 | 2-TON CLEAR EPOXY RESIN | | C2 | 1 | 4744-S | BITRAN BAG | | C3 | AR | MCMASTER CARR PART NO.: 7639A61 | KAPTON TAPE |,,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Sample.pdf,p1,2,"### Notes 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT-FREE GLOVES. 3. (flag) APPLY EPOXY ADHESIVE COMPOUND (ITEM C1) BETWEEN LAYERS OF ASSEMBLY, TAKING CARE NOT TO HAVE ANY BLEED TO THE INNER OR OUTER EDGES OF THE COMPONENTS BEING BONDED TOGETHER. APPLY EQUAL PRESSURE OVER THE TOP AND BOTTOM SURFACES OF ASSEMBLY FOR THE RECOMMENDED CURING TIME OF THE ADHESIVE COMPOUND. 4. (flag) PRIOR TO INSTALLING THE IGNITOR ASSEMBLY TO THE FRAME, PLACE KAPTON TAPE (ITEM C3) ON THE FRAME WHERE THE WIRE CRIMP IS TO BE BONDED. ASSEMBLE IGNITER ASSEMBLY AS SHOWN, ASSURING THAT THE IGNITER WIRE IS PLACED SECURLY AGAINST THE FLAT SAMPLE. SECURE WIRE LEADS ALONG THE OUTER EDGE OF THE ASSEMBLY USING EPOXY (ITEM C1). 5. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH BITRAN BAG (ITEM C2). TRIM BAG TO FIT USING BAG SEALER. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. Detail A callout: KANTHAL WIRE IS WOVEN OVER AND UNDER THE SAMPLE AS SHOWN. Exploded-view stack (top to bottom, balloons): 4/C1/4 igniter; 3/C3/C1/1 frame; 3/C1/2 insulator; 3/C1/3 SIBAL sample; 3/C1/2 insulator; 3/C1/1 frame. ### Dimensions (reference, mm) - Overall length: (127) - Mounting tab: (25.4), (25.4) - Overall width: (47); inner width: (36) - Edge-view assembly thickness: (2.3)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Assembly drawing (A2, landscape, ZIN Technologies / NASA Glenn) of a 2 mm thick PMMA flat sample assembly: exploded isometric (sample frame, 2 mm PMMA sample, insulator base), plan view and edge view, with part list, commercial part list and notes. **Title:** PMMA SAMPLE ASSEMBLY (2MM THICK) **Drawing number:** S1183MFA1065 — REV A — SIZE A2 — SCALE 3/1 — SHEET 1 OF 1 **Next assembly (title block):** BURNING AND SUPRESSION OF SOLIDS S1183MFA1000 Initial release date: 3/23/10 — BLDG: ZIN — AREA: GRC — UNITS: mm — DISCIPLINE: MECHANICAL Contract number: NNC09BA02B — Delivery order: SPACE118 — Model name: S1183MFA1065 — Pro/E Version: Wildfire 2.0 Project lead: [name omitted] 3/23/10; Quality / Safety / Engineer / Designer: [name omitted], dated 3/19/10; Reviewer: [name omitted] 3/18/10 Approved: [name omitted], date 3/25/10 NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO ZIN TECHNOLOGIES (company block; address/phone omitted) THIS DRAWING IS UNDER CONFIGURATION CONTROL: DO NOT REVISE WITHOUT APPROVED ECO. PRIOR TO USE CHECK FOR ANY OUTSTANDING ECO'S WITH CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT OFFICE. ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | REVISED PER BASS-ECO-012 & BASS-ECO-016 | [name omitted] 5/21/10; [name omitted] 5/21/10 |",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,p1,1,"Title-block general notes (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED): 1. ALL DIMENSIONING AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN MILLIMETERS 3. BREAK EDGES: 0.2-0.5 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: 0.5-6 ±0.1; OVER 6-30 ±0.2; OVER 30-120 ±0.3; OVER 120-315 ±0.5; OVER 315-1000 ±0.8; OVER 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCES: 0° 30' THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION. ### Part list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | S1183MFD1067 | FLAT PMMA SAMPLE FRAME | | 2 | 1 | S1183MFD1068 | SAMPLE INSULATOR BASE | | 3 | 1 | S1183MFD1066 | PMMA FLAT FUEL SAMPLE - 2MM THICK | ### Commercial part list | ITEM | QTY | MIL SPEC / VENDOR PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | AR | ITW DEVCON: 14355 | 2-TON CLEAR EPOXY RESIN | | C2 | 1 | 4744-S | BITRAN BAG | ### Notes 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT-FREE GLOVES. 3. (flag) APPLY EPOXY ADHESIVE COMPOUND (ITEM C1) SUCH THAT ONLY APPROXIMATELY THE LAST 10MM OF THE SAMPLE (ITEM 3) IS BONDED TO THE MICA (ITEM 2) TAKING CARE TO NOT HAVE ANY BLEED TO THE OUTER EDGES. DO NOT DISTURB FOR THE RECOMMENDED CURE TIME OF THE ADHESIVE COMPOUND. 4. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH BITRAN BAG (ITEM C2). TRIM BAG TO FIT USING BAG SEALER. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. Exploded-view balloons (top to bottom): 3/C1/1 frame; 3/C1/3 PMMA sample; 3/C1/2 insulator base (mica, per note 3).",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.SampleAssembly.pdf,p1,2,"### Dimensions (reference, mm) - Mounting tab width: (25.4) - Overall height (tab to bottom edge): (41) - Frame width: (25) - Frame length: (57) - Edge-view assembly thickness: (2.1)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Spherical.Sample_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Spherical.Sample_2cm.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Assembly drawing (A2, ZIN Technologies / NASA Glenn), front and side views plus isometric view of a 2 cm PMMA spherical-section (cone with spherical cap) sample bonded to a solid fuel sample arm; with drawing list, commercial part list and notes. **Title:** 2CM SPHERICAL SAMPLE ASSEMBLY **DWG NO:** S1183MFA1085 — REV - (none) — SIZE A2 — CAGE CODE 0SG68 — SCALE 2/1 — SHEET 1 OF 1 **Next assembly:** S1183MFA1000 Contract number: NNC09BA02B — Project code: (blank) Release level: S1183MFA1085 [?] — Model: S1183MFA1085 — Pro/E Version: Wildfire 2.0 NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO ZIN TECHNOLOGIES (company block; address/phone omitted) Designer / Reviewer / Mechanical / Electrical / Structural / Safety / Quality / Materials / Proj Lead: (blank) Revision history table: no entries filled. Form: ZIN_A2_2012.frm Title-block general notes (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED; small print, same standard ZIN block as the other PSI-26 drawings): 1. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN MILLIMETERS 2. BREAK EDGES 0.25-0.50 3. INSIDE CORNERS R0.5 MAX 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: 0.5-6 ±0.1; OVER 6-30 ±0.2; OVER 30-120 ±0.3; OVER 120-315 ±0.5; OVER 315-1000 ±0.8; OVER 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCES: ±0.5° THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION. DIMENSIONS AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994. Drawing under configuration control (do not revise without an approved ECO). ### Drawing list",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Spherical.Sample_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Spherical.Sample_2cm.pdf,p1,1,"| ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | S1183MFD1031 | SOLID FUEL SAMPLE ARM | | 2 | 1 | S1183MFD1086 | 2CM PMMA SPHERICAL SECTION SAMPLE | ### Commercial part list | ITEM | QTY | MIL SPEC/VENDOR PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | A/R | FLEXBAR 15015 EPOXY | ROCKSETT, INDUSTRIAL HIGH TEMPERTURE ADHESIVE | | C2 | 1 | 4744-S | BITRAN BAG | ### Notes 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN, LINT-FREE GLOVES. 3. (flag) APPLY EPOXY ADHESIVE COMPOUND (ITEM C1) BETWEEN COMPONENTS OF ASSEMBLY, TAKING CARE NOT TO HAVE ANY BLEED TO THE OUTER EDGES OF THE COMPONENTS BEING BONDED TOGETHER. DO NOT DISTURB FOR THE RECOMMENDED CURING TIME OF THE ADHESIVE COMPOUND. 4. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. ### Dimensions (reference, mm) - Arm mounting tab: (2X Ø2) holes, (30.3) width, (25.4) tab height, (19.06) hole spacing - Arm vertical length to sample: (38.1) - Sample offset from tab: (25.4) - Overall height, side view: (55.3) - Spherical cap radius: (SR20.0) - Arm/rod thickness in side view: (10) [?] (dimension spans the sample axis region) - Balloons: 1 (sample arm), 2 (spherical sample), 3 / C1 (adhesive at joint)",,True
