PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,p1,2,"### Notes 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT-FREE GLOVES. 3. (flag) APPLY EPOXY ADHESIVE COMPOUND (ITEM C1) BETWEEN LAYERS OF ASSEMBLY, TAKING CARE NOT TO HAVE ANY BLEED TO THE INNER OR OUTER EDGES OF THE COMPONENTS BEING BONDED TOGETHER. APPLY EQUAL PRESSURE OVER THE TOP AND BOTTOM SURFACES OF ASSEMBLY FOR THE RECOMMENDED CURING TIME OF THE ADHESIVE COMPOUND. 4. (flag) PRIOR TO INSTALLING THE IGNITOR ASSEMBLY TO THE FRAME, PLACE KAPTON TAPE (ITEM C3) ON THE FRAME WHERE THE WIRE CRIMP IS TO BE BONDED. ASSEMBLE IGNITER ASSEMBLY AS SHOWN, ASSURING THAT THE IGNITER WIRE IS PLACED SECURLY AGAINST THE FLAT SAMPLE. SECURE WIRE LEADS ALONG THE OUTER EDGE OF THE ASSEMBLY USING EPOXY (ITEM C1). 5. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH BITRAN BAG (ITEM C2). TRIM BAG TO FIT USING BAG SEALER. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35D. 6. (flag) THIS ASSEMBLY S1183MFA1110 HAS INTERCHANGEABLE PARTS (S1183MFD1111) WITH VARIOUS THICKNESSES. SEE TABULATED TABLE ON THIS DWG. AND ALSO TABLE ON DWG. S1183MFD1111. Detail A (SCALE 2/1) callout: KANTHAL WIRE IS WOVEN OVER AND UNDER THE SAMPLE AS SHOWN. Exploded-view stack (top to bottom, balloons): 4/C1 (flag 4) igniter; 3/C3/C1/1 frame; 3/C1/2 insulator; 3/6/C1/3 PMMA sample; 3/C1/2 insulator; 3/C1/1 frame.",,True
