PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Samples_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat.Samples_2cm.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: CAST PMMA. ASTRA PRODUCTS, WEBSITE: astraproducts.com. SEE TABULATED TABLE ON THIS DRAWING FOR PART NUMBERS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 3. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. ### Dimensions (mm) - Length: 100 - Width: 28 - Thickness: (A STOCK) — see table - Isometric view: SCALE 1/1 ### Thickness table | DRAWING NO. | A | PART NO. ASTRA PRODUCTS INC. | |---|---|---| | S1183MFD1111-1 | 0.1 mm | 11510101 | | S1183MFD1111-2 | 0.2 mm | 11510102 | | S1183MFD1111-3 | 0.3 mm | 11510103 | | S1183MFD1111-4 | 0.4 mm | 11510104 | | S1183MFD1111-5 | 1 mm | 11510310 (as printed) | | S1183MFD1111-6 | 2 mm | 11510120 | | S1183MFD1111-7 | 3 mm | 11510130 | | S1183MFD1111-8 | 4 mm | 11519140 (as printed) | | S1183MFD1111-9 | 5 mm | 11510150 |",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Part drawing (A2, landscape, ZIN Technologies / NASA Glenn) of a thin rectangular SIBAL fuel sheet with rounded corners: plan view, edge view and isometric. **Title:** SIBAL FLAT FUEL SAMPLE - 2CM **Drawing number:** S1183MFD1022 — REV A — SIZE A2 — SCALE 2/1 — SHEET 1 OF 1 **Next assembly (title block):** FLAT FUEL SAMPLE ASSEMBLY (2CM) S1183MFA1020 Initial release date: 3/12/10 — BLDG: ZIN — AREA: GRC — UNITS: mm — DISCIPLINE: MECHANICAL Contract number: NNC09BA02B — Delivery order: SPACE118 — Model name: S1183MFD1022 — Pro/E Version: Wildfire 2.0 Project lead: [name omitted] 3/11/10; Quality / Safety / Engineer / Designer / Reviewer: [name omitted], dated 3/12/10 Approved: [name omitted], date 4/19/10 NATIONAL AERONAUTICS AND SPACE ADMINISTRATION, JOHN H. GLENN RESEARCH CENTER, LEWIS FIELD, CLEVELAND, OHIO ZIN TECHNOLOGIES (company block; address/phone omitted) THIS DRAWING IS UNDER CONFIGURATION CONTROL: DO NOT REVISE WITHOUT APPROVED ECO. PRIOR TO USE CHECK FOR ANY OUTSTANDING ECO'S WITH CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT OFFICE. ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | REVISED PER BASS-ECO-007 | [name omitted] 4/19/10; [name omitted] 4/19/10 |",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_Sibal.Flat.Fuel.Sample_2cm.pdf,p1,1,"Title-block general notes (UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED): 1. ALL DIMENSIONING AND TOLERANCING PER ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. ALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN MILLIMETERS 3. BREAK EDGES: 0.2-0.5 4. LINEAR TOLERANCES: 0.5-6 ±0.1; OVER 6-30 ±0.2; OVER 30-120 ±0.3; OVER 120-315 ±0.5; OVER 315-1000 ±0.8; OVER 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. ANGULAR TOLERANCES: 0° 30' THIRD ANGLE PROJECTION. ### Notes 1. MATERIAL: SIBAL FUEL, GRC PROVIDED. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 3. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Dimensions (mm) - Length: 100 - Width: 28 - Corner radii: 4X R1.6 - Thickness: (0.127 STOCK)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Spherical.Section.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Spherical.Section.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Detail drawing (A2) of a PMMA spherical-section (cone-shaped segment of a sphere) fuel sample with a small blind hole on the axis; front view, side view, top view, isometric view and Section A-A. Title: PMMA SPHERICAL SECTION SAMPLE DWG NO: S1183MFD1086 | REV: - | Size: A2 | CAGE code: 0SG68 | Scale: 3/1 | Sheet 1 of 1 Initial release date: 06/25/2013 | Release level: WORKING | Model: S1183MFD1086 | Pro/E version: Wildfire 5.0 Next assembly: S1183MFA1085 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; prepared by ZIN Technologies Contract number: NNC09BA02B | Project code: SPACE118 Stamp (red text on sheet): BASS-ECO-031 In Process Sign-off block: Approved, Designer, Reviewer, Mechanical, Safety, Quality, Materials, Proj Lead: [name omitted] (dates 06/10/13 to 06/19/13); Electrical, Structural: - ""This drawing is under configuration control. Do not revise without an approved ECO. Prior to use, check with configuration management for any outstanding ECOs."" Dimensions and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensions are in millimeters 2. Break edges 0.25-0.50 3. Inside corners R0.5 max 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: ±0.5°",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Spherical.Section.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Spherical.Section.pdf,p1,1,"Dimensions (mm unless noted): - Included cone angle 60°, half-angle 30° - Spherical radius SR19.05 ±.12 (datum A on the spherical surface) - Sphere/outer diameter (Ø19.05) reference - Hole Ø2.0, position tolerance Ø.25 relative to A; hole depth 7.3 - (Ø3.2) reference (counterbore/hole outline in front view) [?] - (10) reference width at cone tip - 3.7 (height of truncated tip / flat below section) - Section A-A shows the solid hatched segment with the axial blind hole. NOTES: 1. MATERIAL: DELVIES PLASTIC 1.50 INCH DIAMETER CAST ROUND CLEAR PMMA BALL. 2. MATERIAL CERTIFICATION REQUIRED PER QUALITY LEVEL SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW. 3. OPTICALLY CLEAR ALL OVER UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. 4. CLEAN ONLY BY IMMERSION IN MILD SOAP SOLUTION IN DISTILLED WATER. RINSE WITH DISTILLED WATER AND LET AIR DRY. 5. HANDLE WITH CLEAN, LINT FREE GLOVES. 6. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. Revision history: (no entries)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Blk.Rod.Sample.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Blk.Rod.Sample.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Detail drawing (A2) of a black PMMA cylindrical rod fuel sample with rounded (spherical) ends and an axial blind hole at one end; end view, side view, isometric view (scale 2/1) and a tabulated-diameter table. Title: BLACK PMMA ROD SAMPLE DWG NO: S1183MFD1091 | REV: - | Size: A2 | CAGE code: 0SG68 | Scale: 4/1 & NOTED | Sheet 1 of 1 Initial release date: 06/25/2013 | Release level: WORKING | Model: S1183MFD1091 | Pro/E version: Wildfire 5.0 Next assembly: S1183MFA1090 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; prepared by ZIN Technologies Contract number: NNC09BA02B | Project code: SPACE118 Sign-off block: Approved, Designer, Reviewer, Mechanical, Safety, Quality, Materials, Proj Lead: [name omitted] (dates 06/19/13 to 06/25/13); Electrical, Structural: - ""This drawing is under configuration control. Do not revise without an approved ECO. Prior to use, check with configuration management for any outstanding ECOs."" Dimensions and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensions are in millimeters 2. Break edges 0.25-0.50 3. Inside corners R0.5 max 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: ±0.5°",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Blk.Rod.Sample.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Blk.Rod.Sample.pdf,p1,1,"Dimensions (mm unless noted): - Overall rod length 57.28 (from datum A end face) - Rod diameter (Ø A INCH), tabulated; position tolerance Ø.2 relative to A, B - Axial hole Ø2.0, depth 6.5 (datum B on the end view) - End radius R2.33 (at hole end); opposite end SR (spherical radius, value not given) Tabulated dash numbers: | Drawing no. | A | |---|---| | S1183MFD1091-1 | .250 INCH | | S1183MFD1091-2 | .375 INCH | | S1183MFD1091-3 | .500 INCH | NOTES: 1. MATERIAL: BLACK PMMA CAST ROD, .500 INCH DIAMETER. DELVIE'S PLASTIC INC., WEBSITE delviesplastics.com 2. POLISH SURFACE TO EQUIVALENT OF OPTICALLY CLEAR ALL OVER UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. 3. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 4. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. Revision history: (no entries)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat_1cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat_1cm.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Detail drawing (A2) of a rectangular flat cast-PMMA sheet fuel sample (1 cm family), plan view, edge view showing stock thickness A, isometric view (scale 1/1), and a tabulated thickness / vendor part-number table. Title: PMMA FLAT SAMPLE (1CM) DWG NO: S1183MFD1116 | REV: - | Size: A2 | CAGE code: 0SG68 | Scale: 2/1 | Sheet 1 of 1 Initial release date: (blank) | Release level: WORKING | Model: S1183MFDA1116 [?] | Pro/E version: Wildfire 2.0 [?] Next assembly: S1183MFD1115 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; prepared by ZIN Technologies Contract number: NNC09BA02B | Project code: SPACE118 Stamps (red text on sheet): BASS-ECO-024 In Process; BASS-ECO-028 In Process Sign-off block: Approved, Designer, Reviewer, Mechanical, Safety, Quality, Materials, Proj Lead: [name omitted] (dates 06/10/13 to 06/17/13); Electrical, Structural: - ""This drawing is under configuration control. Do not revise without an approved ECO. Prior to use, check with configuration management for any outstanding ECOs."" Dimensions and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensions are in millimeters 2. Break edges 0.25-0.50 3. Inside corners R0.5 max 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: ±0.5°",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat_1cm.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_PMMA.Flat_1cm.pdf,p1,1,"Dimensions (mm): - Length 100 - Width 18 - Thickness (A STOCK), tabulated Tabulated dash numbers: | Drawing no. | A (thickness) | Part no. Astra Products Co. | |---|---|---| | S1183MFD1116-1 | 0.2 mm | 11510102 | | S1183MFD1116-2 | 1 mm | 11510310 | | S1183MFD1116-3 | 2 mm | 11510120 | | S1183MFD1116-4 | 3 mm | 11510130 | | S1183MFD1116-5 | 4 mm | 11519140 | | S1183MFD1116-6 | 5 mm | 11510150 | NOTES: 1. MATERIAL: CAST PMMA. ASTRA PRODUCTS, WEBSITE astraproducts.com. SEE TABULATED TABLE ON THIS DRAWING FOR PART NUMBERS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 3. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. MARK PART NUMBER, A DASH, AND A SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER/SOW, BY TAGGING PER SAE-AS478-35D. Revision history: (no entries)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_SPICE-front-window.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_SPICE-front-window.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Detail drawing (A0 sheet, content rotated 90°) of the main (front) window of the Smoke Points in Co-flow Experiment: a rectangular Lexan plate with a raised rounded-corner rectangular window boss, a bonded rib/block along one edge carrying three M3 tapped holes, and two edge pin holes; front view, edge views and side view. Overprinted ""CHECKPRINT""; stamp ""AUTHORIZED BY ____ DATE ____ NASA DR. NO."" (blank). Title: MAIN WINDOW (find no. H003), SMOKE POINTS IN CO-FLOW EXPERIMENT ASSEMBLY 60054MAFH000 Drawing number: 60054MDFH003 | Size: A0 | REV: - | STAT: - | BLDG/CELL: -/- | Scale: 1:1 | Sheet 1 of 1 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Lewis Research Center, Cleveland, Ohio Model name: 60054MDFH003 | Pro/E version: 19.0 | Release date: XX/XX/XX Drafter: [name omitted]; Designer: [name omitted]; Engineer: [name omitted] METRIC. Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. All dimensions are in millimeters 3. Break edges: 0.2-0.5 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: 0° 30' Revisions block (CHG / ZONE / DESCRIPTION / APPROVED): no entries.",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_SPICE-front-window.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_SPICE-front-window.pdf,p1,1,"NOTES: 1. MATERIAL: LEXAN MARGARD MR5. 2. BOND USING ETHYLENE CLORIDE, ETHYLENE CHORIDE, DICHLOROETHANE, ACS, PER FEDERAL SPEC O-C-265B. 3. SURFACES INDICATED ARE TO BE OPTICALLY CLEAR AND FREE FROM SCRATCHES AND BLEMISHES. DO NOT APPLY MASKING TAPE OR OTHER MATERIALS TO THIS SURFACE AT ANY TIME. 4. ANTIREFLECTION COAT WITH COATING ECI129 (EVAPORATED COATING INC., WILLOW GROOVE, PA). CLEAN ONLY BY IMMERSION IN MILD SOAP SOLUTION IN DISTILLED WATER, RINSE WITH DISTILLED WATER. AIR DRY, DO NOT RUB COATING WITH CLOTH, COTTON SWAB, ETC. PROTECT DURING MACHINING AND STORAGE. 5. IDENTIFY BY TAGGING WITH DRAWING PART NUMBER 60054MDFH003, PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. 6. QUANTITY: ONE REQUIRED. (Flag-note triangles 2, 3, 4 point to the bonded joint and the optical faces.) Dimensions (mm unless noted): - Plate overall 189 x 96.2 (datums B and C at edges) - Window opening/boss 165 (with position tolerance Ø0.3 Ⓜ A B Ⓜ) x 74; offset 7.4 from top edge; 4X R4.6 corner radii - Edge rib: tapped holes A_5, A_7, A_8 spaced 45.8 and 91.6 (basic); 110 (with ⊕ Ø0.5 Ⓜ A BⓂ) between rib ends in another view - 3X M3 X 0.5-6H, thread depth 4-5 [?], ⊕ Ø0.2 C A BⓂ - Hole axis height 11.7 (basic) above datum A - Stock thickness .500 INCH SHEET; 6 (boss/step height) - Edge view: 10.4 (rib depth), 6.5, 21, 2X 93 (basic), chamfer 45° X 1.5, 2X 3 (basic) - Edge pin holes A_1: 2X Ø1.93/1.88, depth 12, ⊕ Ø0.15[?] Ⓜ B A C [?]; R (radius callout, no value)",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_60054MAFH000_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_60054MAFH000_C.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Top-level assembly drawing (very long R3 sheet, content rotated 90°) of the Smoke Points in Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) hardware: housing with main/top windows, fan housing with fan and flow straightener, burner tubes, ignitor, gas supply (bottle, regulator, mass flow controller, filter, quick connect), soot screen, scale arm and captive brackets. Shows Section A-A, Section B-B / C-C, Section D-D and a view labelled ""FAN HOUSING ASSEMBLY REMOVED FOR CLARITY"", all with item balloons (H0xx = drawn parts, C nn = commercial parts). Followed by a drawing list and two commercial parts lists. Stamp ""AUTHORIZED BY ____ DATE ____ NASA DR. NO."" (blank).",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_60054MAFH000_C.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_60054MAFH000_C.pdf,p1,1,"Title: SMOKE POINTS IN CO-FLOW EXPERIMENT ASSEMBLY Project: SMOKE POINTS IN CO-FLOW EXPERIMENT, XXXXXXXXXXX Drawing number: 60054MAFH000 | REV: C | Size: R3 | Scale: 1:1 | Sheet 1 of 1 (as printed on this page) Initial rel date: XX/XX/XX | BLDG: XXX | AREA: XXX | Units: mm | Discipline: MECHANICAL | Pro/E version: 2001 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio Contract: XXX | Contractor: XXX | Task order: XXX Drafter: [name omitted]; Engineer: [name omitted]; Designer: [name omitted] ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO."" Approved: [name omitted], date 4/10/08 PDM rel level: WORKING | PDM revision: x.15+ | PDM database: GLOVEBOX | Model name: 60054MAFH000 ""Prior to use verify the intended purpose in PDM (""FOR"" attribute)"" Plot footer (edge of sheet): OBJECT: 60054MAFH000_1, DATE: 11-Apr-08 10:44:42 (user name omitted) Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. All dimensions are in millimeters 3. Break edges: 0.2-0.5 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: 0° 30'",,True
