PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Assembly drawing (A1) of the BASS solid fuel frame: a transparent window plate supported by two curved brackets, a toothed slider rail with a slider, slider cover and magnetic sample mount; exploded isometric view with balloons, side and front views with reference dimensions. Title: SOLID FUEL FRAME ASSEMBLY (BASS) Project: BURNING AND SUPPRESSION OF SOLIDS, S1183MFA0000 Drawing number: S1183MFA1000 | REV (title block): - | Size: A1 | Scale: 2/1 | Sheet 1 of 1 Initial rel date: 2/21/10 | BLDG: ZIN | AREA: GRC | Units: mm | Discipline: MECHANICAL | Pro/E version: Wildfire 2.0 Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; prepared by ZIN Technologies Contract number: NNC09BA02B | Delivery order: SPACE118 | Model name: S1183MFA1000 Sign-off block: Project Lead, Quality, Safety, Engineer, Designer, Reviewer: [name omitted] (dates 2/18/10 to 2/21/10); Approved: [name omitted], date 6/10/10 ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO."" ""Prior to use check for any outstanding ECO's with configuration management office."" Third angle projection. Unless otherwise specified: 1. All dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994 2. All dimensions are in millimeters 3. Break edges: 0.2-0.5 4. Linear tolerances: 0.5-6 ±0.1; over 6-30 ±0.2; over 30-120 ±0.3; over 120-315 ±0.5; over 315-1000 ±0.8; over 1000-2000 ±1.2 5. Angular tolerances: 0° 30'",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,p1,1,"Revisions: | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | REVISED PER BASS-ECO-006 | EM-6/10/10, CD-6/9/10, JF-6/9/10 | Part list: | Item | Qty | Part number | Description | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | S1183MFD1010 | WINDOW | | 2 | 2 | S1183MFD1012 | BRACKET | | 3 | 1 | S1183MFD1013 | SLIDER RAIL | | 4 | 1 | S1183MFD1014 | SLIDER | | 5 | 1 | S1183MFD1015 | SLIDER COVER | | 6 | 1 | S1183MFA1016 | MAGNETIC SAMPLE MOUNT ASSEMBLY | Commercial part list: | Item | Qty | Mil spec / vendor part number | Description | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 4 | MCMASTER CARR: 92095A181 | M3 X 0.5 X 8 LG SOCKET BUTTON HEAD CAP SCREW | | C2 | 2 | MRDSBHCSC0256-3 | 0.086-56 UNRC-3A X 0.188 SOCKET BUTTON HEAD CAP SCREW, 18-8 STAINLESS | | C3 | 4 | MRDSBHCSC0256-2 | 0.086-56 UNRC-3A X 0.125 SOCKET BUTTON HEAD CAP SCREW, 18-8 STAINLESS | | C4 | AR | S-46163A TYPE II, GRADE M | LOCTITE 222MS THREAD LOCKER | | C5 | AR | 3M: 2216 B/A TRANSLUCENT | SCOTCHWELD EPOXY ADHESIVE | Balloon callouts: 1 (window); 2, C4, C1 with flag note 2 (window screws); 2 (bracket); 3; C2, C4, flag 2; 4 with flag 3; 6 with flag 3; 5; C3, C4, flag 2. Reference dimensions (mm): (173.1) overall frame length; (64.1) and (55.2) widths in side view; (46.9) height; (6.4) window plate thickness; (32.4) and (108.4) slider/rail positions.",,True
PSI-26,Engineering Documents,PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Engineering Documents/PSI-26_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SolidFuelFrame.pdf,p1,2,"NOTES: 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS AND ALL PROCESSES. 2. (flag) TIGHTEN FASTENERS TO FINGER TIGHT POSITION. CONTINUE TO TIGHTEN WITH A TORQUE WRENCH UNTIL A SHARP RISE IN TORQUE IS FELT, APPROXIMATELY 1/4 TURN PAST FINGER TIGHT. 3. (flag) EPOXY ITEM 6 TO ITEM 4 USING ITEM C5, EPOXY 2216 B/A. 4. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 5. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS, OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35.",,True
