PSI-26,Science Documents,PSI-26_Science Documents_SRD_BASS.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Science Documents/PSI-26_Science Documents_SRD_BASS.pdf,p10,2,Extinguishment will be initiated by gradually increasing the mass flow rate of nitrogen in a series of step increments,,False
PSI-26,Science Documents,PSI-26_Science Documents_SRD_BASS.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Science Documents/PSI-26_Science Documents_SRD_BASS.pdf,p11,0,February 2010 11 Success Criteria • Minimal Success: 20 total tests including: eight tests with flat samples (four materials at two different flow speeds); four tests with spherical PMMA samples (four different flow speeds with nitrogen extinguishment); four tests with candles (four different flow speeds with nitrogen extinguishment); and four tests of PMMA wake flames (four different flow speeds with nitrogen extinguishment). • Complete Success: 60 flames as indicated in test matrix.,,False
PSI-26,Science Documents,PSI-26_Science Documents_DLD_BASS.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-26/Science Documents/PSI-26_Science Documents_DLD_BASS.pdf,p1,0,"PSI Data Layout Document – BASS (Burning and Suppression of Solids) Investigation BASS (Burning and Suppression of Solids) examines the burning and extinction characteristics of a wide variety of fuel samples in microgravity. The BASS experiment will guide strategies for extinguishing accidental fires in microgravity. BASS results contribute to the combustion computational models used in the design of fire detection and suppression systems in microgravity and on Earth. The BASS data available in PSI is organized into 2 datasets by the year the tests were conducted: • BASS_2012 • BASS_2013 These Experiment Data records are located on the “Data” tab within the BASS investigation in PSI. When an experiment data record is selected, the “Scientific Data and Information” tab is opened. For BASS_2012, on the “Scientific Data and Information” tab, “Images” are organized by date formatted yyyy_mm_dd. There are 21 image galleries for BASS_2012. For BASS_2013, on the “Scientific Data and Information” tab, “Audio/Video Files” and “Images” are both organized by date formatted yyyy_mm_dd. There are 12 audio/video collections and 15 image galleries for BASS_2013. Other relevant data and information about the BASS investigation can be located throughout the other tabs in the BASS record.",,False
