PSI-47,Reports,PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-47/Reports/PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,p13,0,"13 ve collected electronic data from all of the planned 15 test points to establish a large body of consistent, repeated data. Several factors contributed to the decision to not pursue additional with their hardware and a small block of time came open. DAFT had to negotiate very hard to be allowed the opportunity to f the P-Trak. Leroy Chiao used this alcohol wick when he performed DAFT-1 and -2 and both of those units run time on the P-Trak is increasing, especially during Bag #3, the count/mass ratio is declining. Although it is not certain e. ood average, but details regarding the data spread could well be lost and not retrievable, since the log functions on both the limited availability of the crew, it does not seem reasonable to think that time and procedures could be made available for Jeff or the follow on Increment 14 crew to troubleshoot the experiment. It was delivered only 6 months after being proposed and accepted, and it was understood that in some respects, the sample material (the ARD, a poly disperse particulate) was less than re tionship between the readings from the DustTrak and P-Trak. Unfortunately, an aerosol of this type is difficult to manufacture, and the project did not have time or resources to attempt such a",,False
PSI-47,Reports,PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-47/Reports/PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,p13,1,"it to either read ‘0’ or display and error code. This did not happen. The units gave readings from zero well up into the middle of their operational ranges, and s almost unbelievably clean. The readings from the devices during that part of the overall experiment though, H. Conclusion Ideally, DAFT would ha test points. They were: Crew Time: Although DAFT was planned for Increment 13, there was not enough crew time available to support all of the desired Payload activities and the prospects for actually performing the experiment at all were extremely uncertain. Fortunately for DAFT, ALTEA had some problems schedule 1 + 3 test points, and there was very little chance for another session. Isopropyl Alcohol: As mentioned in the Results section, Jeff Williams was unable to open the DAFT Alcohol Wick container -02. This limited the amount of alcohol available to support the operation o were loaded with alcohol over 3 years ago, so the amount that is remaining is highly questionable. Sample Build Up: Testing in the lab has shown that under some circumstances, especially when a significant amount of the larger ARD particles is sent to the devices, a buildup of particles can occur within the optics chamber of the P-Trak. Clearly, the data shows that the sample aerosol contained a greater proportion of larger particles than is experienced on Earth. It also shows that as the that this build up is occurring, the symptoms of that condition are consistent with the data.",,False
PSI-47,Reports,PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-47/Reports/PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,p13,2,"The lack of the electronic data collection has limited the ability of the project team to perform a more detailed analysis of the data, since it will remain unknown as to the actual range of the readings over tim The team feels that the information gathered and transmitted by Jeff does represent a g machines seem to have failed (although the possibility of operator error does remain). Based on devices. That being said, DAFT was conceived and built as a Risk Mitigation experiment, not necessarily a Science ideal. (Note: For those unfamiliar with the experiment, ideally, a mono disperse aerosol with particulates about 0.7 microns in size would have been created in a density of about 50,000 pt/cc in order to provide a mo quantifiable rela development.) The data shows that the devices were able to operate in microgravity for an extended period of time with no apparent failure. One of the major concerns was that the P-Trak would accumulate alcohol in the optics chamber and obscure them, causing the un then back; in short, they performed as expected. DAFT-1 and -2 showed that the units were ‘apparently working’ and that the air aboard the ISS i never crossed the 20% of the operational range threshold, leaving the results somewhat suspect.",,False
PSI-47,Reports,PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-47/Reports/PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,p14,0,"This latest experimental run, however, did. The project team feels that the optimal reading range for the P-Trak is from 30,000 – 100, 14 000 pt/cc (although the published range goes up to 500,000 pt/cc) and for the DustTrak; 20 – 80 mg/m3. Clearly, the latest data was within this range. e tent. aerosol created, implying that the units both functioned nominally. ME has been manufactured to the same specifications as the unit that was tested (P-Trak-01), this is not considered to be a factor. ve a good basis for acceptance within the bounds of that analysis. or t e rea hat the DAFT experiment has been a complete ccess, nufactured for SAME will perform as accur I. Earth Benefits / Spin-off Applications There are no tangible Earth benefits from this experiment.",,False
PSI-47,Reports,PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-47/Reports/PSI-47_Reports_DAFT_30Day.PostFlightReport.pdf,p14,1,"The count/mass ratio between the devices as measured on orbit, although well outside of the value determined on Earth, is both explainable and credible; and to the best of the team’s ability to analyze th data, seems very consis The problems with the equipment and the data have been discussed at some length, and although they do leave something to be desired, it does appear that there is enough consistency to determine that the readings recorded are believable and representative of the Due to the constraints listed above, DAFT-4, using the ‘unmodified’ P-Trak, was not performed. Since the flight hardware for SA The Science team has examined the data and compared the results against the empirical data accumulated for polydisperse aerosols; and determined that the results do ha F su hes sons, the SAME (DAFT) project team feels t and that it has confidence that the P-Traks as designed and ma ately and effectively on-orbit as they have in the labs.",,False
