PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,p1,0,"# Verification Information Sheet (VIS) National Aeronautics and Space Administration | Field | Value | |---|---| | Verification Number | SFSDP-VIS-0295 | | Revision | (blank) | | Level of Verification | Level 2 (Saffire-I, II and III except where stated otherwise) | | Approval Date | 3/26/2015 | | Scheduled Closure | N/A | | Verification Method | Inspection | | Prepared By | [name omitted] | Specification: SFSDP-REQ-102, Spacecraft Fire Safety Demonstration Project (SFS Demo) System Requirements Document (SRD) Requirement Paragraph: R.SFSD_S.0003, R.SFSD_S.0004, R.SFSD_S.0043 Requirement: - R.SFSD_S.0003 - SFS Demo Flame Spread Experiment Sample Count - R.SFSD_S.0004 - SFS Demo Flame Spread Sample Size - R.SFSD_S.0043 - SFS Demo Flame and Fuel Surface Temperature Measurement (Flame Spread Sample) [this line is highlighted in yellow] Success Criteria: (See Verification Additional Information Sheet for details) Verification Approach: (See Verification Additional Information Sheet for details) Documentation: 1) As-Run Flame Spread (FS) Sample Card Preparation (SFSDP-PRO-197-01) 2) Drawings 120102MFA000, 120102MFA310 No. of Attachments: (blank) Responsible/Performing Organization: [name omitted] VIS Concurrence Responsible Engineer: [digital signature omitted] GRC 2036 03/14 (1.0) — PREVIOUS EDITIONS ARE OBSOLETE. — GLPR 7123.22 Appendix D.2 — Page 1 of 3",,True
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,p2,0,"# Verification Completion Notice (VCN) Verification number: SFSDP-VIS-0295 Revision: (blank) Verification Results Summary: (Provide attachments/enclosures as required.) **R.SFSD_S.0003** - SFS Demo Flame Spread Experiment Sample Count An inspection was performed on the assembled fuel cards for Saffire-I and Saffire-III per As-Run SFSDP-PRO-197-01 Rev B, operation number 23, using drawing 120102MFA310. *A single sample was found present.* **R.SFSD_S.0004** - SFS Demo Flame Spread Sample Size An inspection was performed on the assembled fuel cards for Saffire-I and Saffire-III per As-Run SFSDP-PRO-197-01 Rev B, operation number 23, using drawing 120102MFA310. *Sample measurements met the required dimensions.* **R.SFSD_S.00043** - SFS Demo Flame and Fuel Surface Temperature Measurement (Flame Spread Sample) An inspection was performed on the assembled fuel cards for Saffire-I and Saffire-III per As-Run SFSDP-PRO-197-01 Rev B, operation number 23, using drawing 120102MFA310. *Temperature measurement sensors were installed at the required locations.* [last sentence highlighted in yellow] As run SFSDP-PRO-197-01 Rev B is located in eRoom: (M-514) AES Spacecraft Fire Demonstration Project/ Configuration Management (Includes the Documentation Database)/ Documentation Library (CM Managed CSAS)/ Document Database (Read-Only)/ Sample Card Process Plans https://collaboration.grc.nasa.gov/eRoom/fac9/AESSpacecraftFireDemonstrationProject/0_4832 Requirements Evidence of Compliance: (blank)",,True
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,p2,1,| Role | Name | Signature | Date | |---|---|---|---| | Lead V&V Engineer | [name omitted] | [signature omitted] | 03/26/2015 | | Project Chief Engineer | | | | | SMA Lead | | | | | Project Manager (if necessary) | | | | | Customer (if necessary) | | | | GRC 2036 03/14 (1.0) — PREVIOUS EDITIONS ARE OBSOLETE. — GLPR 7123.22 Appendix D.2 — Page 2 of 3,,True
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,p3,0,"# Verification Additional Information Sheet Verification number: SFSDP-VIS-0295 Revision: (blank) Additional Information: **R.SFSD_S.0003** - SFS Demo Flame Spread Experiment Sample Count The SFS Demo Structural Subsystem shall have a single sample for use in the Flame Spread experiment sample burn. Success Criteria: Verification shall be considered successful when the inspection prior to product delivery to AI&T shows that 1 sample is prepared for use in the Flame Spread experiment burn. Verification Approach: SFS Demo Flame Spread Experiment Sample Count shall be verified by Inspection. An inspection shall be performed of the loaded Flame Spread Sample holder. --- **R.SFSD_S.0004** - SFS Demo Flame Spread Sample Size The SFS Demo Structural Subsystem shall have a Flame Spread Sample having width of 12.0 in (300 mm) and length of 31.5 in (800 mm), with a goal width of 19.7 in (500 mm) and goal length of 39.4 in (1000 mm). Success Criteria: Verification shall be considered successful when the inspection prior to product delivery to AI&T shows that the SFS Demo Structural Subsystem has a Flame Spread Sample having width of 12.0 in (300 mm), length of 31.5 in (800 mm), with a goal width of 19.7 in (500 mm) and goal length of 39.4 in (1000 mm). Verification Approach: SFS Demo Flame Spread Sample Size shall be verified by Inspection for Saffire-I and Saffire-III. An inspection shall be performed of the flight hardware per the as-built assembly drawing 120102MFA310. ---",,True
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_SFSDP-VIS-0295_Saffire 1 and 3_Thermocouple Placement.pdf,p3,1,**R.SFSD_S.00043** - SFS Demo Flame and Fuel Surface Temperature Measurement (Flame Spread Sample) The SFS Demo Structural Subsystem shall measure the temperature of the Flame Spread Sample flame zone at 6 locations as specified in Table 3.7.4-7 and depicted in Figure 3.7.4-1. Success Criteria: Verification shall be considered successful when the inspection shows that the temperature measurement sensors are installed at 6 locations on the Flame Spread Sample as specified in Table 3.7.4-7 and depicted in Figure 3.7.4-1. Verification Approach: SFS Demo Flame and Fuel Surface Temperature Measurement (Flame Spread Sample) shall be verified by Inspection. An inspection shall be performed of the flight hardware per the as-built assembly drawings 120102MFA000 and 120102MFA310. GRC 2036 03/14 (1.0) — PREVIOUS EDITIONS ARE OBSOLETE. — GLPR 7123.22 Appendix D.2 — Page 3 of 3,,True
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_Saffire I Sample 1 TM graphs.docx,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_Saffire I Sample 1 TM graphs.docx,all,0,"Figure . Air speed, average fan speed, and igniter current as functions of time for Saffire-I, Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Radiometer flux and igniter current as functions of time for Saffire-I, Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Plume temperature and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Sample surface temperature and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread test). Figure . Vehicle carbon dioxide mole fraction and igniter current as function of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread test). Figure . Vehicle oxygen mole fraction and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Vehicle pressure and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Vehicle relative humidity and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread case). Figure . Vehicle temperature and igniter current as functions of time, Saffire-I Sample 1 (concurrent spread case).",,False
PSI-98,Raw Data,PSI-98_Raw Data_Saffire-I Sample 2 TM graphs.docx,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Raw Data/PSI-98_Raw Data_Saffire-I Sample 2 TM graphs.docx,all,0,"Figure 1. Saffire-I Sample 2 air speed, fan tachometer, and igniter current. Figure 2. Saffire-I Sample 2 Radiometer and igniter current. Figure 3. Saffire-I Sample 2 Plume Temperature. Figure 4. Saffire-I Sample 2 Surface Temperature Figure 5. Saffire-I Sample 2 Carbon Dioxide Concentration Figure 6. Saffire-I Sample 2 Oxygen Concentration Figure 7. Saffire-I Sample 2 Inlet Pressure Figure 8. Saffire-I Sample 2 Inlet Humidity Figure 9. Saffire-I Sample 2 Inlet Temperature",,False
PSI-98,Science Documents,PSI-98_Science Documents_SAFFIRE-I Image Directory Nomenclature.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-98/Science Documents/PSI-98_Science Documents_SAFFIRE-I Image Directory Nomenclature.pdf,p1,0,"SAFFIRE-I Image Directory Nomenclature Xn_Raw_CamOriginal RAW Camera Original - contains 8 byte offset that must be corrected prior to color interpolation. Xn_Raw_DistroMaster RAW Distribution Master - 8 byte offset corrected using ImageJ. Use this file set to distribute RAW image files and color interpolation processing. Xn_Raw2TIFF RAW_DistroMaster files color interpolated and saved as TIFF, using IrfanView Batch Conversion process. Xn_Raw2TIFF_icmad Raw2TIFF files annotated with ICMAD 'Exposure' and 'Gain' information. Data is appended to the bottom of each frame using ImageMagick script. Xn_jpeg Flight hardware generated jpeg images, created on-board from the RAW Camera Original. Xn_jpeg_corrupt Jpeg images received corrupted after downlink. Xn_jpeg2png_icmad Flight hardware generated jpeg images annotated with ICMAD 'Exposure' and 'Gain' information. Data is appended to the bottom of each frame using ImageMagick script and re-saved as .png format to prevent additional compression artifacts. ""X"" Denotes run type ""n"" Denotes run number",,False
