PSI-101,Presentations,PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Presentations/PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,slide 40,0,"40 / 38 SAME Aging Results Theory: Dashed line, Solid points Experimental: Solid Line, Open points",,False
PSI-101,Presentations,PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Presentations/PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,slide 41,0,"41 / 38 For spacecraft materials, number counts decreased by a factor of 1.7 to 2.7 over 800 seconds. The measured and predicted number decreases agree within about 20 %. The best agreement between experiment and prediction is Davm - agree within 4 %. The decrease in the geometric standard deviation is typically more than a factor of two greater than the predicted change. Aging results are relevant to partially sealed volumes and low air flow conditions. In all cases, aging resulted in approximately a factor of two decrease in number concentration and a factor of two increase in the number mean diameter with the exception of teflon SAME Aging Results",,False
PSI-101,Presentations,PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Presentations/PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,slide 42,0,42 Where p = 0.5 : Arithmetic Mean Diameter (M1 / M0) p = 1.5 : Diameter of Average Mass (M3 / M0)1/3 Moment Analysis For a log-normal particle size distribution and,,False
PSI-101,Presentations,PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Presentations/PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,slide 43,0,"43 Where i =0 : Number Concentration Moment i = 1 : Diameter Concentration Moment, Proportional to the ionization detector moment i = 3 : Mass Concentration Moment You can then calculate: Arithmetic Mean Diameter (M1 / M0) Diameter of Average Mass (M3 / M0)1/3 The moments are: Moment Analysis For a particle size distribution",,False
PSI-101,Presentations,PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Presentations/PSI-101_Presentations_SAME-R_Particle Morphology and Size Results from the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment-2.pptx,slide 44,0,"39th International Conference on Environmental Systems, July 2009 44 SAME Calibration Zeroth Moment requires separate calibration for different particle size ranges. Best choice is made iteratively after initial particle size computation.",,False
