PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_SAME VPRED Matrix PLN-005 Baseline.xls,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_SAME VPRED Matrix PLN-005 Baseline.xls,sheet VPERD matrix PLN-005 baseline,0,"sheet VPERD matrix PLN-005 baseline: 1091 non-empty rows header: Requirement Number | Requirement Source | Discipline | Requirement | System Response & Notes | Method | Series | Safety | HFIT | VDS # | Hardware | | System | | GSE Required | In MSG EU | Documents | | row 1: | | | | | | | | | | F.M. | Flt. | Full-up System | Sub-System | | | Flight Drawings | Outside Source | Documentation/ Procedures row 2: 001 | SAME EIRD 1 | Title | Smoke Generation Duct (Aging Chamber Inlet Elbow) | | NVR | | | | | | | | | | | | | row 3: 001.01 | SAME EIRD 1.a | Title | a) Configuration: Square or round duct with air flow through the duct. | | NVR | | | | | | | | | | | | | row 4: 001.01.1 | | Mechanical Engineering | The smoke generation duct shall be round with air flow through the duct. | SAME Drawing #____________ | I | | | | | | | | | | | X | | row 5: 001.02 | SAME EIRD 1.b | Title | b) Optical access: One view is required of the sample and the downstream flow. This view should be illuminated and imaged by a color video camera (visible light only). The orientation of the light relative to the imager should permit the visualization of the light scattered by the smoke. | The duct has a port downstream of the sample, with a wide-angle camera mounted to view the sample and the first portion of the flow duct. Lighting will provide image visibility in the closed tube and has been demonstrated in 1-g with sample smoke. | NVR | | | | | | | | | | | | |",,False
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,p1,0,"Description: E-size machined-part drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the SAME aging chamber: a cylindrical cup with a mounting flange, shown in Section A-A (side section), an end/plan view of the closed end with two round ports, a 1/4 NPT port and a square opening, and Section B-B through a port boss. Commercial parts list (threaded inserts) at lower left; notes at upper left. ### Title block - Title: SAME AGING CHAMBER ASSEMBLY / 60089MFHA150 (next assembly); SAME AGING CHAMBER - Drawing number: 60089MFHA151, size E, rev B - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead / quality / safety / engineer / designer / reviewer: [name omitted], all dated 07/18/05 - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 1/1; initial release date 07/18/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 8/26/05 - Check any outstanding ECO's with configuration management office ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | REV. A INCORPORATES ECO #SAME-ECO-008. | [name omitted] 07/26/05 | | B | | REV. B INCORPORATES ECO #SAME-ECO-026. | [name omitted] 8/26/05 |",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,p1,1,"### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) | | | |---|---| | .X | ± 0.03 | | .XX | ± 0.01 | | .XXX | ± 0.005 | | FRACTION | ± - | | ANGULAR | ± 0.50° | | BREAK EDGES | .01-.03 | Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,p1,2,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: 6061-T6 ALUMINUM ALLOY PER AMS-QQ-A-250/11. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 2. SAFETY CRITICAL PART (PRESSURE). 3. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 4. 64 Ra ALL MACHINED SURFACES PER ANSI/ASME B46.1. UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. 5. ELECTROLESS NICKEL COAT ALL SURFACES, EXCEPT THREADED HOLES, .0005-.0015 INCH THICKNESS PER MIL-C-26074E PRIOR TO INSTALLING THREADED INSERTS. 6. SURFACE TREAT THREADED HOLES ONLY PER MIL-C-5541, CLASS 3. USE IRIDITE 14.2 OR REQUESTER APPROVED EQUAL PER MIL-C-81706, CLASS 3, FORM II, METHOD B OR C AS APPLICABLE PRIOR TO INSTALLING INSERTS. SPOT TOUCH UP BY METHOD B. 7. ALL DIMENSIONS SHOWN ARE FINAL DIMENSIONS, AFTER NICKEL PLATING. 8. (flag note) INSTALL THREADED INSERTS PER MANUFACTURER'S SPECIFICATIONS. 9. CLEAN ALL SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL OR ETHYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT FREE CLOTH. 10. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 11. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. 12. ESTIMATED WEIGHT= 5.110 Lbs. (The flag triangles on the drawing next to items C1 and C2 read ""7"" [?]; the notes list shows the insert note as 8.)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_Drawing_SAME Aging Chamber.PDF,p1,3,"### Commercial parts list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 4 | MS51830-102 | .112-40UNC-3B THREADED INSERT, 303 SS | | C2 | 12 | MS51830-201 | .190-32 UNJF-3B, THREADED INSERT, 303 SS | ### Section A-A (dimensions in inches) - Flange outer diameter Ø9.60 - Bore Ø7.977 / 7.974 (datum B), perpendicularity Ø.005 to A, cylindricity .002 - Overall height 2X 9.15; inside depth 8.31; 8.52 (to datum A face) - Flange thickness .19; base thickness .12 - Radii: 5X R.09, 6X R.06, R.12, R.06, R.21, 4X R.06 - Base: 2X Ø3.60, Ø7.9, Ø8.31 - Datums A (flange face), B (bore), C (base) ### End view (closed end) - Flange bolt circle Ø9.000; 12X Ø.229/.223 holes, position Ø.030 A B; 12X 30°0' - (Ø.4375) TAP DRILL THRU 1/4-18 NPT (offset port); 2X 2.000 - Two round ports: 2X Ø3.000 bolt circle, 2X Ø2.00 bore, position Ø.015 C B; 3.0 and 2.820 offsets; 6X 60°0' 2 PLACES - 6X .3125-18UNC-2B TAP DRILL ▽.65 MAX, DRILL AND TAP PER MS51835-105 (2 PLACES, 12 HOLES TOTAL); item C2 (12 PLACES), flag 7 - Square opening: □1.260±.002, position Ø.010 A B, perpendicularity .02 A; 2X 1.500; (2X .750); 4X R.20; □1.85, position Ø.020 A B; datum D - 4X .190-32UNF-2B ▽.160 MIN, TAP DRILL (Ø.161) ▽.37 MAX PER MS51835-102, position Ø.014 D A B; 4X R.13; item C1 (4 PLACES), flag 7 - Section lines A-A and B-B ### Section B-B - Boss Ø1.0; .5; .53 - 2X R.06; 2X R .020/.010; 2X R.12 ALL AROUND (BOSS AND OPENING); 2X R.015 ALL AROUND (BOSS AND OPENING)",,True
