PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA417-B Kapton Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA417-B Kapton Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. (flag) SAMPLE (ITEM C1) IS ROLLED UP AND PLACED INSIDE OF THE COILS. 2. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 3. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA432 | KAPTON IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY | ### Commercial parts list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 1 | N/A | .005 THICK X .50 WIDE X 2.0 LG KAPTON FILM | ### Callouts on the views - C1 with flag 1 (rolled sample inside coil); 1 (ignitor wire coil assembly)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA432-A Kapton Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA432-A Kapton Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the ignitor wire coil for the Kapton sample: a helical coil of 0.020 in stainless steel lockwire with two straight leads, each ending in a crimped connector pin. Side view of the coil, a second side view with pins, and an end view. ### Title block - Title: KAPTON IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY; next assembly: KAPTON SAMPLE ASSEMBLY 60089MFHA417 - Drawing number: 60089MFHA432, size C, rev A - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/22/05 to 8/01/05; safety: NA - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 4/1; initial release date 7/26/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 06/15/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-161. | [name omitted] 06/15/06 | ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA432-A Kapton Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA432-A Kapton Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: TYPE 304 STAINLESS STEEL SAFETY LOCKWIRE (.020 DIA), McMASTER-CARR PART No 8860K12 AND AS NOTED IN FIELD OF DRAWING. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 2. CLEAN ALL SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL OR ETHYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT FREE CLOTH. 3. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 4. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Field of drawing (dimensions in inches) - Ø.020 WIRE FORMED AS SHOWN, PITCH 20/INCH, APPROX 8 COILS, Ø.220 ID - Coil length (.375); lead spacing .31; .033 - End view: (Ø.220); 6X R.06; 2X .44; 2X .69 - SIZE 22D CONNECTOR PIN, ALLIED ELECTRONICS PART No. 512-9156/204370-2, CRIMPED ON WIRE LEAD, 2 REQD",,True
