PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA414-A Lampwick Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA414-A Lampwick Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size assembly drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the lamp wick sample assembly: a cellulose torch wick sample (item C1) inside an ignitor wire coil (item 1) with two crimped lead pins. End view and side view. ### Title block - Title: LAMP WICK SAMPLE ASSEMBLY; next assembly: SAMPLE CAROUSEL No 1 THRU 5 ASSEMBLIES 60089MFHA433 THRU 60089MFHA437 - Drawing number: 60089MFHA414, size C, rev A - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/11/05 to 7/14/05; safety: N/A [name omitted] - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 4/1; initial release date 7/14/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 06/15/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-162. | [name omitted] 06/15/06 | ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA414-A Lampwick Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA414-A Lampwick Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 2. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA415 | IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY (FOR Ø.250 OD SAMPLES) | ### Commercial parts list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 1 | N/A | 1/8"" DIA TORCH WICK X .56 LG., MATERIAL: CELLULOSE HUGHES BOX AND CONTAINER | ### Field of drawing - Sample diameter (Ø.188) (inches) - Balloons C1 (wick) and 1 (coil)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,0,"Description: E-size fluids system schematic (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) for the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment (SAME). Shows the Fluids Control Unit (nitrogen supply from the MSG GN2 quick disconnect through filter, solenoid valve, relief valves and a 15 psig regulator to a nitrogen manifold; mass flow controller; vacuum manifold to the MSG vacuum QD), the aging chamber smoke piston (sample side / drive-vac side), the Dynamic Diagnostics Assembly (ISS and STS smoke detectors), the Dynamic Diluter (LFE, static mixer, VSO), Commercial Diagnostics Enclosures A and B (optics chamber and ion sensor each), the P-Trak enclosure and the Thermal Precipitator Module (TPM). Symbol legends along the bottom edge, general notes and balloon legend at right. Balloon tags combine a pressure letter and a gas letter (see balloon legend) with a number.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,1,"### Title block - Title: SAME FLUIDS SYSTEM SCHEMATIC; next assembly: SMOKE AEROSOL MEASUREMENT EXPERIMENT 60089MFHP000 - Drawing number: 60089MFHP000, size E, rev C - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, safety, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/21/05 to 7/26/05 - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: AutoCAD Mechanical 2004 DX - Scale: none; official date 07/23/2005; sheet 1 of 6; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical; ""AutoCad 2004"" - Tolerances: .X ±; .XX ±; .XXX ±; FRACTION ±; ANGULAR ± NA; BREAK EDGES NA (no values). Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 1/27/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | H7,8 E,D 5&6 B8 | REV. A INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-077 | [name omitted] 11/23/05 | | B | F8, D6, G1 | REV. B INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-090 | [name omitted] 1/13/06 | | C | B8 | REV. C INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-095 | [name omitted] 1/27/06 |",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,2,"### General notes 01 REFER TO CP SHEETS FOR COMPONENT INFORMATION 02 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS UPSTREAM OF AND INCLUDING PRESSURE REGULATOR (PN06) IS 200 PSIA 03 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS DIRECTLY CONNECTED TO THE DYNAMIC DIAGNOSTICS ASSEMBLY INCLUDING THE DYNAMIC DILUTER IS 15.7 PSIA 04 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS DOWNSTREAM OF AND INCLUDING CHECK VALVES (VR09, VR20) IS 40 PSIA 05 ALL COMPONENTS NOT MENTIONED IN ABOVE NOTES HAVE A MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF 29.7 PSIA 06 REFERENCES TO ASSEMBLY DRAWINGS ARE NOTED ON THE SCHEMATIC 07 ALL FLEXIBLE HARD LINES TO BE PROOF PRESSURE TESTED TO 2.0 X MDP. REFER TO SAME-TST-035. 08 FULL SYSTEM TO BE LEAK TESTED AT 1.0 X MDP OR 1.0 X HIGHEST OPERATING PRESSURE MINUMUM. REFER TO SAME-TST-036. 09 TUBING AND LINES ARE SHOWN ON COMPONENT ASSEMBLY DRAWINGS OR INTERFACE CONNECTION DRAWING ### Balloon legend | PRESSURE | GAS | |---|---| | P - POSITIVE | N - NITROGEN | | V - VACUUM | M - MSG ENVELOPE | | B - BOTH (P OR V) | R - N AND/OR MSG ENV. | | A - NEAR ATM | T - MSG ENV. AND/OR SMOKE | | | U - ANY |",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,3,"### Fluids Control Unit (see 60089MFHA220 for detail) Nitrogen supply path (heavy line, 1/8"" OD SS): - MSG GN2 QD -> PN08 / PN01 quick disconnect (PN10, PN09 quick disconnect with shut-off and cap outside the unit) -> PN05 filter (F) -> PN04 relief valve ""RELIEF VALVE 1, 220 PSIG WITH MANUAL OVERRIDE"" -> PN02 PT (pressure transducer) -> PN03 solenoid valve -> PN06 pressure regulator, 15 PSIG - Downstream of PN06: 1/8"" ID TYGON nitrogen manifold with PN12 PT; PN13, PN14, PN16 relief valves each 20 PSIG; solenoid valves PN07, PN24 (-> orifice PN25), PN15, PN27 (-> orifice PN28) - PN07 feeds 3-way/4-way solenoid valves BN08 and BN09 - Mass flow controller BN19, between 3-way solenoid valves BN18 and BN17; BN20 solenoid valve to VENT; BN02 PT; BN16 solenoid valve - Lines leave the unit through quick disconnects to BN03 VACUUM/GN2 QD1 and BN23 VACUUM/GN2 QD2 Vacuum path: - VM06 solenoid valve -> VM05 orifice -> VM07 orifice -> AT16 filter (F) -> quick disconnect - VR12, VR11, VR06 solenoid valves on vacuum branches to quick disconnects; VR04 PT on the vacuum header - VM09 solenoid valve -> VM10 orifice -> AT20 PT -> AT11 filter (F) - VR03 solenoid valve; VR02 relief valve ""RELIEF VALVE 2, 20 PSIG WITH MANUAL OVERRIDE"" - Check valves VR09 and VR20 in series, 1/8"" ID TYGON, -> VR01 quick disconnect -> VR19 MSG VACUUM QD; VR14, VR13 quick disconnect with shut-off and cap - VR10 VACUUM QD",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,4,"### Aging chamber (see 60089MFHA150 for detail) - SMOKE PISTON block: SAMPLE SIDE above the piston, DRIVE/VAC SIDE below - Sample side ports with valves operated by actuators BN21 and BN22 - Drive/vac side port BN25 to VACUUM/GN2 QD1; VACUUM/GN2 QD2 (BN23) - Line ""FROM MSG WORK VOLUME"" to the sample side ### Dynamic Diagnostics Assembly (see 60089MDBA165 for detail) - AT05 check/inlet ""FROM MSG WORK VOLUME"" -> ISS SMOKE DETECTOR -> STS SMOKE DETECTOR -> AT06 filter (F) -> TO MSG RECIRCULATION FANS - AT13 SAMPLE OULET QD (as written) between the two detectors ### Dynamic Diluter (see 60089MFHA180 for detail) - AT03 inlet (SAMPLE QD2) -> AT07 -> LFE (laminar flow element) with AT08 PT across it -> AU01 STATIC MIXER -> AU02 SAMPLE QD1 outlet - PN20 GN2 QD -> PN23 VSO (voltage sensitive orifice) feeding dilution gas into the stream ### P-Trak enclosure (see 60089MFHA500 for detail) - AU03 inlet (SAMPLE QD) -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU05 filter -> VR07 orifice -> VR05 VACUUM QD - Bypass: AU06 filter -> VR08 orifice ### Commercial Diagnostics Enclosure (A) (see 60089MFHA600 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AU07) -> AU08 filter -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU09 filter -> VR15 orifice -> VR16 VACUUM QD - SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT04) -> AT09 ION -> AT10 filter -> VM04 orifice -> vacuum",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,5,### Commercial Diagnostics Enclosure (B) (see 60089MFHA600 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AU10) -> AU11 filter -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU12 filter -> VR17 orifice -> VR18 VACUUM QD - SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT17) -> AT18 ION -> AT19 filter -> VM13 orifice -> vacuum ### Thermal Precipitator Module (TPM) (see 60089MFHA300 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AT14) and SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT15) each to a manifold of 6 solenoid-valved sample lines (12 total) -> common outlet -> VM08 VACUUM QD,,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHP000-C SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,6,"### Symbol legends Piping component symbols: butterfly valve; check valve; gate valve; relief valve; ball valve; voltage sensitive orifice; directional valves 2-way, 3-way, 4-way; pressure regulator; loader; cylinder regulator; turb flowmeter; orifice; venturi; rupture disk; quick disconnect; press gauge; filter; strainer; heat exch; pump; motor; quick disconnect with shut-off. Actuator symbols: cylinder; hand; pneu control; rotary motor; solenoid. Primary control element symbols: EP elec-pneu xdcr; EH elec-hydr xdcr; LLS liq level switch; LLT liq level xdcr; LS limit switch; PDS press diff switch; PDT press diff xdcr; PS pressure switch; PT pressure xdcr; TC thermocouple; TS temp switch. Item designations: locally mounted; control room mounted; altn control room mounted; ref drawing. Instrument letter designations: first letter B burner, E emergency, F flow, H hand, L level, P pressure, S speed, T temperature, Z position, J power, U surge; succeeding letter A alarm, C control, D differential, H high, I indicate, L low, P permissive, R record, S shutdown, Y datalog. Instrument symbols: general; prgm logic controller; data collector facility; prgm process controller; fluids system labels.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_S1171MFHA401 Pyrell Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_S1171MFHA401 Pyrell Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size assembly drawing of the Pyrell sample assembly: a Pyrell polyurethane foam sample (item C1) inside the ignitor wire coil for 0.250 in OD samples (item 1), with two crimped lead pins. Side view and end view, no dimensions on the views. ### Title block - Title: PYRELL SAMPLE ASSEMBLY; next assembly: SAMPLE CAROUSEL No 1 THRU 5 ASSEMBLIES 60089MFHA433 THRU 60089MFHA437 - Drawing number: S1171MFHA401, size C, rev - (revisions table empty) - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Contract: NNC09BA02B; delivery order: SPACE-117 - Project lead, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 03/09/10 - Project folder: U:\MRDOC\xxx; model name: S1171MFHA401; Pro/E version: 2001 - Scale 4/1; initial release date 03/09/10; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 03/09/10 ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_S1171MFHA401 Pyrell Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_S1171MFHA401 Pyrell Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 2. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA415 | IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY (FOR Ø.250 OD SAMPLES) | ### Commercial parts list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 1 | N/A | 1/4"" X 1/4"" X 1/2"" LG. PYRELL POLYURETHANE FOAM | ### Field of drawing - Balloons C1 (foam sample inside coil) and 1 (coil assembly)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,0,"Description: Scanned left half of the SAME fluids system schematic (drawing 60089MFHP000, rev E per the matching right half): the Fluids Control Unit (nitrogen supply and vacuum manifolds), the aging chamber smoke piston, and the piping, actuator, control element and item designation symbol legends along the bottom. No title block on this half. Some lines in the vacuum section are drawn as bold dashed lines (see general note 05 on the right half: components designated with bold dashed lines have a maximum design pressure of 19.7 psia).",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,1,"### Fluids Control Unit (see 60089MFHA220 for detail) Nitrogen supply path (heavy line, 1/8"" OD SS): - MSG GN2 QD -> PN08 / PN01 quick disconnect (PN10, PN09 quick disconnect with shut-off and cap outside the unit) -> PN05 filter (F) -> PN04 ""RELIEF VALVE 1, 220 PSIG WITH MANUAL OVERRIDE"" -> PN02 PT -> PN03 solenoid valve -> PN06 pressure regulator, 15 PSIG - Downstream of PN06 (1/8"" ID TYGON): PN12 PT; PN13, PN14, PN16 relief valves, each 20 PSIG; solenoid valves PN07, PN24 (-> PN25 orifice), PN15, PN27 (-> PN28 orifice) - PN07 feeds solenoid valves BN08 and BN09 (bold dashed line from BN08/BN09 down to the vacuum section) - Mass flow controller BN19 between solenoid valves BN18 and BN17; BN20 solenoid valve to VENT; BN02 PT; BN16 solenoid valve - Lines leave through quick disconnects: BN03 VACUUM/GN2 QD1; BN23 VACUUM/GN2 QD2 Vacuum section (bold dashed lines): - VM06 solenoid valve -> VM05 orifice -> VM07 orifice -> AT16 filter (F) -> quick disconnect - VR12, VR11, VR06 solenoid valves to quick disconnects; VR04 PT - VM09 solenoid valve -> VM10 orifice -> AT20 PT -> AT11 filter (F) -> quick disconnect - VR02 ""RELIEF VALVE 2, 5 PSIG WITH MANUAL OVERRIDE"" - VR20 relief valve, 5 PSIG - 1/8"" ID TYGON -> VR01 ""MSG VACUUM QUICK DISCONNECT""; VR09 check valve; VR19 MSG VACUUM QD; VR13, VR14 quick disconnect; ""MSG SHUT-OFF VALVE"" - VR10 VACUUM QD1",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p1,2,"### Aging chamber (see 60089MFHA150 for detail) - SMOKE PISTON: SAMPLE SIDE (top) / DRIVE/VAC SIDE (bottom) - Sample side valves with actuators BN21 and BN22; line ""FROM MSG WORK VOLUME"" - BN25 VACUUM/GN2 QD1 on the drive/vac side; BN23 VACUUM/GN2 QD2 ### Symbol legends (bottom edge) Piping component symbols: butterfly valve; check valve; gate valve; relief valve; ball valve; voltage sensitive orifice; directional valves 2-way, 3-way, 4-way; pressure regulator; loader; cylinder regulator; turb flowmeter; orifice; venturi; rupture disk; quick disconnect; press gauge; filter; strainer; heat exch; pump; motor; quick disconnect with shut-off. Actuator symbols: cylinder; hand; pneu control; rotary motor; solenoid. Primary control element symbols: EP elec-pneu xdcr; EH elec-hydr xdcr; LLS liq level switch; LLT liq level xdcr; LS limit switch; PDS press diff switch; PDT press diff xdcr; PS pressure switch; PT pressure xdcr; TC thermocouple; TS temp switch. Item designations: locally mounted; control room mounted; altn control room mounted; ref drawing. Instrument letter designations table cut off at the right edge [illegible].",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p2,0,"Description: Scanned right half of the SAME fluids system schematic, rev E: Dynamic Diagnostics Assembly, Dynamic Diluter, P-Trak enclosure, Commercial Diagnostics Enclosures A and B, Thermal Precipitator Module, balloon legend, general notes, instrument legends, revisions and title block. The drawing number in the title block reads 60089MFHP000 (the file name says 80089MFHP000). ### Title block - Title: SAME FLUIDS SYSTEM SCHEMATIC; next assembly: SMOKE AEROSOL MEASUREMENT EXPERIMENT 60089MFHP000 - Drawing number: 60089MFHP000, size E, rev E - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, safety, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/21/05 to 7/26/05 - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074 [?]; CAD package: AutoCAD Mechanical 2004 DX - Scale, official date and sheet fields [illegible]; units: inch; discipline: mechanical; ""AutoCad 2004"" - Tolerances: .X ±; .XX ±; .XXX ±; FRACTION ±; ANGULAR ± NA; BREAK EDGES NA. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 10/11/06",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p2,1,"### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | H7,8 E,D 5&6 B8 | REV. A INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-077 | [name omitted] 11/23/05 | | B | F8, D6, G1 | REV. B INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-090 | [name omitted] 1/13/06 | | C | B8 | REV. C INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-095 | [name omitted] 1/27/06 | | D | | REV. D INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-156 | [name omitted] 7/17/06 | | E | A8 B8 | REV. E INCORPORATED ECO No. SAME-ECO-212 | [name omitted] 10/11/06 | ### General notes 01 REFER TO CP SHEETS FOR COMPONENT INFORMATION 02 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS UPSTREAM OF AND INCLUDING PRESSURE REGULATOR (PN06) IS 200 PSIA 03 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS DIRECTLY CONNECTED TO THE DYNAMIC DIAGNOSTICS ASSEMBLY INCLUDING THE DYNAMIC DILUTER IS 15.7 PSIA 04 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS DOWNSTREAM OF AND INCLUDING CHECK VALVE (VR09,) IS 40 PSIA 05 MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF COMPONENTS DESIGNATED WITH BOLD DASHED LINES IS 19.7 PSIA 06 ALL COMPONENTS NOT MENTIONED IN ABOVE NOTES HAVE A MAXIMUM DESIGN PRESSURE OF 29.7 PSIA 07 REFERENCES TO ASSEMBLY DRAWINGS ARE NOTED ON THE SCHEMATIC 08 REFER TO SAME-TST-035 FOR PROOF PRESSURE AND LEAK TESTING 09 TUBING AND LINES ARE SHOWN ON COMPONENT ASSEMBLY DRAWINGS OR INTERFACE CONNECTION DRAWING",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p2,2,"### Balloon legend | PRESSURE | GAS | |---|---| | P - POSITIVE | N - NITROGEN | | V - VACUUM | M - MSG ENVELOPE | | B - BOTH (P OR V) | R - N AND/OR MSG ENV | | A - NEAR ATM | T - MSG ENV. AND/OR SMOKE | | | U - ANY | ### Dynamic Diagnostics Assembly (see 60089MDBA165 for detail) - AT05 inlet ""FROM MSG WORK VOLUME"" -> ISS SMOKE DETECTOR -> STS SMOKE DETECTOR -> AT06 filter (F) -> TO MSG RECIRCULATION FANS - AT13 SAMPLE OULET QD (as written) between the detectors ### Dynamic Diluter (see 60089MFHA180 for detail) - AT03 (SAMPLE QD2) -> AT07 -> LFE with AT08 PT across it -> AU01 STATIC MIXER -> AU02 SAMPLE QD1 - PN20 GN2 QD -> PN23 VSO ### P-Trak enclosure (see 60089MFHA500 for detail) - AU03 (SAMPLE QD) -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU05 filter -> VR07 orifice -> VR05 VACUUM QD; bypass AU06 filter -> VR08 orifice ### Commercial Diagnostics Enclosure (A) (see 60089MFHA600 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AU07) -> AU08 filter -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU09 filter -> VR15 orifice -> VR16 VACUUM QD - SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT04) -> AT09 ION -> AT10 filter -> VM04 orifice ### Commercial Diagnostics Enclosure (B) (see 60089MFHA600 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AU10) -> AU11 filter -> OPTICS CHAMBER -> AU12 filter -> VR17 orifice -> VR18 VACUUM QD - SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT17) -> AT18 ION -> AT19 filter -> VM13 orifice ### Thermal Precipitator Module (TPM) (see 60089MFHA300 for detail) - SAMPLE INLET 1 (AT14) and SAMPLE INLET 2 (AT15), each to 6 solenoid-valved sample lines (12 total) -> VM08 VACUUM QD",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_80089MFHP000-E SAME Fluids System Schematic.pdf,p2,3,"### Legends (bottom edge) Instrument letter designations (partly cut off at left): first letter B burner, E emergency, F flow, H hand, L level, P pressure, S speed, T temperature, Z position, J power, U surge; succeeding letter A alarm, C control, D differential, H high, I indicate, L low, P permissive, R record, S shutdown, Y datalog. Instrument symbols: general; prgm logic controller; data collector facility; prgm process controller; fluids system labels.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA416-A Silicone Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA416-A Silicone Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size assembly drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the silicone sample assembly: a silicone cord sample (item C1) inside the silicone ignitor wire coil (item 1) with two crimped lead pins. End view and side view, no dimensions on the views. ### Title block - Title: SILICONE SAMPLE ASSEMBLY; next assembly: SAMPLE CAROUSEL No 1 THRU 5 ASSEMBLIES 60089MFHA433 THRU 60089MFHA437 - Drawing number: 60089MFHA416, size C, rev A - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/11/05 to 7/14/05; safety: N/A [name omitted] - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 4/1; initial release date 7/14/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 06/15/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-162. | [name omitted] 06/15/06 | ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA416-A Silicone Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA416-A Silicone Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 2. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA419 | SILICONE IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY | ### Commercial parts list | ITEM | QTY | PART NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | C1 | 1 | 187-SIL70 | .1875 DIA SILICONE CORD X .50 LG. ZATKOFF | ### Field of drawing - Balloons C1 (silicone cord inside coil) and 1 (coil assembly)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA419 Silicone Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA419 Silicone Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the ignitor wire coil for the silicone sample: a helical coil of 0.020 in stainless steel lockwire with two leads ending in crimped connector pins. Side view and end view. ### Title block - Title: SILICONE IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY; next assembly: SILICONE SAMPLE ASSEMBLY 60089MFHA416 - Drawing number: 60089MFHA419, size C, rev - (revisions table empty) - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/11/05 to 7/14/05; safety: N/A [name omitted] - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 4/1; initial release date 7/14/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 7/15/05 ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA419 Silicone Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA419 Silicone Ignitor Wire Coil Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: TYPE 304 STAINLESS STEEL SAFETY LOCKWIRE (.020 DIA), McMASTER-CARR PART No 8860K12 AND AS NOTED IN FIELD OF DRAWING. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 2. CLEAN ALL SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL OR ETHYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT FREE CLOTH. 3. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 4. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Field of drawing (dimensions in inches) - Ø.020 WIRE FORMED AS SHOWN, PITCH 32/INCH, APPROX 10 COILS, Ø.160 ID - Coil length (.31) - End view: (Ø.160); 4X R.06; 2X .44; 2X .69 - SIZE 22D CONNECTOR PIN, ALLIED ELECTRONICS PART NO. [phone removed]/204370-2, CRIMPED ON WIRE LEAD, 2 REQD",,True
