PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA410-A Teflon Sample Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA410-A Teflon Sample Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 2. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. ### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA411 | TEFLON IGNITOR WIRE COIL ASSEMBLY | | 2 | 1 | 60089MFHD413 | TEFLON SAMPLE PART | ### Field of drawing - Lead spacing (.31) (inches) - Balloons 2 (Teflon sample inside coil) and 1 (coil assembly)",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD413 Teflon Sample Part.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD413 Teflon Sample Part.pdf,p1,0,"Description: C-size part drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the Teflon sample: a short Teflon rod with an external thread over its full length. End view and side view. ### Title block - Title: TEFLON SAMPLE PART; next assembly: TEFLON SAMPLE ASSEMBLY 60089MFHA410 - Drawing number: 60089MFHD413, size C, rev - (revisions table empty) - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 7/11/05 to 7/14/05; safety: N/A [name omitted] - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 8/1; initial release date 7/14/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 7/15/05 ### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES -. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-101,Engineering Documents,PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD413 Teflon Sample Part.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Engineering Documents/PSI-101_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD413 Teflon Sample Part.pdf,p1,1,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: .1875 DIA TEFLON ROD, Mc MASTER-CARR PART No 8546K32. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 2. 32 Ra ALL MACHINED SURFACES PER ANSI/ASME B46.1. 3. CLEAN SURFACES WITH NON-DEODORANT, NONADDITIVE SOAP AND WATER. AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT-FREE CLOTH. 4. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 5. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. 6. ESTIMATED WEIGHT= 0.010 LB. ### Field of drawing (dimensions in inches) - Length .50 - Diameter (Ø.1875) - .190-32 UNF-2A THREAD",,True
