PSI-101,Science Documents,PSI-101_Science Documents_SAME_Baseline Concept Description Document_001 Rev A.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-101/Science Documents/PSI-101_Science Documents_SAME_Baseline Concept Description Document_001 Rev A.pdf,p5,0,"SAME-DOC-001 Rev. A 1 1.0 DOCUMENT OVERVIEW 1.1 Abstract The primary purpose of this document is to provide the reviewer with a comprehensive overview of the designs and systems for the Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment (SAME). This document also provides the references to the other pertinent drawings, schematics and documents that fully describe and define SAME. 1.2 Scope The scope of this document includes a high level description of the SAME hardware and its required support systems at a PDR design maturity level. This document is not intended to be a controlling document of any sort, and therefore, the reader is advised to always request the latest revision when viewing any referenced documents. 1.3 Applicable Documents The most current draft of the Science Requirements Document (SRD) for the Smoke experiment was used as input to this document. • Exploration Investigation Requirements Document for SAME a.k.a. Smoke Aerosol Measurement Experiment, Rev. 1.01, Dr. David Urban, NASA Glenn Research Center, January 3, 2005 1.4 Referenced Documents DRAWINGS: The following drawing numbers represent the integration level assembly drawings for SAME:",,False
