PSI-102,Presentations,PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Presentations/PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,slide 23,0,"23 TEM revealed several particle morphologies Teflon and Pyrell: Aggregates Teflon aggregates: numerous primaries of same dimension Pyrell Aggregates: primaries widely distributed in size Kapton: single particles Low temperature: produced very small and low TEM density particles High temperature: TEM density increased Silicone: No TEM visible particles despite dense smoke Lamp wick: Single particles, typically large Aging showed a distinct elimination of the smallest particles TEM Results",,False
PSI-102,Presentations,PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Presentations/PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,slide 24,0,24 SAME-1&2 Results | | Geometric Mean Diameter (Dg) (µm) | Count Mean Diameter (M1/M0) (µm) | Diameter of Average Mass (M3/M0) (µm) | σg Kapton | Unaged | 0.047 | 0.062 | 0.106 | 2.072 | Aged 720 s | 0.102 | 0.121 | 0.169 | 1.790 Lampwick | Unaged | 0.103 | 0.142 | 0.271 | 2.232 | Aged 720 s | 0.269 | 0.308 | 0.401 | 1.673 Silicone | Unaged | 0.152 | 0.221 | 0.468 | 2.382 | Aged 720 s | 0.320 | 0.400 | 0.628 | 1.956 Teflon | Unaged | 0.093 | 0.111 | 0.173 | 2.081 | Aged 720 s | 0.080 | 0.115 | 0.237 | 2.342 Pyrell | Unaged | 0.177 | 0.227 | 0.377 | 2.032 | Aged 720 s | 0.348 | 0.400 | 0.529 | 1.697,,False
