PSI-102,Presentations,PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Presentations/PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,slide 40,0,"40 / 38 SAME Aging Results Theory: Dashed line, Solid points Experimental: Solid Line, Open points",,False
PSI-102,Presentations,PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Presentations/PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,slide 41,0,"41 / 38 For spacecraft materials, number counts decreased by a factor of 1.7 to 2.7 over 800 seconds. The measured and predicted number decreases agree within about 20 %. The best agreement between experiment and prediction is Davm - agree within 4 %. The decrease in the geometric standard deviation is typically more than a factor of two greater than the predicted change. Aging results are relevant to partially sealed volumes and low air flow conditions. In all cases, aging resulted in approximately a factor of two decrease in number concentration and a factor of two increase in the number mean diameter with the exception of teflon SAME Aging Results",,False
PSI-102,Presentations,PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Presentations/PSI-102_Presentations_SAME-2_ParticleMorphology and Size Results.pptx,slide 42,0,42 Where p = 0.5 : Arithmetic Mean Diameter (M1 / M0) p = 1.5 : Diameter of Average Mass (M3 / M0)1/3 Moment Analysis For a log-normal particle size distribution and,,False
