PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,p1,0,"Description: D-size assembly drawing of the SAME aging chamber assembly: cylindrical chamber with top plate, piston, fan assembly, inlet elbow/LED board, inlet and outlet gate valves and outlet elbow. Several elevation views, a top view, a bottom view, an isometric view (""THIS VIEW SHOWN WITH TOP PLATE REMOVED""), with item balloons and torque callouts. Commercial parts list and drawing list at left, notes at upper right. ### Title block - Title: AGING CHAMBER ASSEMBLY; next assembly: SAME IN MSG ASSEMBLY 60089MFHA000 - Drawing number: 60089MFHA150, size D, rev B - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead / quality / safety / engineer / designer / reviewer: [name omitted], dated 07/18/05 (project lead 07/18/06 [?]) - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 1/4; initial release date 07/18/05; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 12/19/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-134 | [name omitted] 06/22/06 | | B | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-182 | [name omitted] 12/19/06 |",,True
PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,p1,1,"### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES N/A. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994. ### Notes 1. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED FOR ALL COMMERCIAL PARTS. 2. SAFETY CRITICAL ASSEMBLY (PRESSURE). 3. SAFETY CRITICAL FASTENERS (ITEM C9) TO BE INSTALLED PER MSFC-STD-486B. 4. (flag) APPLY THREADLOCKING COMPOUND PER MIL-S-46163 TO THREADED FASTENERS. 5. (flag) APPLY TWO COMPLETE WRAPS OF TEFLON TAPE TO FITTING THREADS IN DIRECTION OF THREAD. DO NOT OVERLAP FIRST THREAD AT END OF FITTING. FIRMLY PRESS TAPE IN PLACE AT OVERLAP POINT. 6. (flag) FOLLOWING FINAL TORQUE OF FASTENERS, APPLY RTV (ITEM C13) TO EXPOSED THREADS WHERE REQUIRED TO PREVENT SHARP EDGES. 7. (flag) SECURE ALL FLEXIBLE TUBING CONNECTIONS WITH HALAR TIE WRAPS (ITEM C18). 8. (flag) SECURE FITTING WITH KAPTON TAPE IN LOCATION SHOWN, FOR STORAGE ONLY. 9. (flag) OVERWRAP FLEXIBLE TUBING WITH VITON SHRINK WRAP. SIZE ACCORDING TO FIT. 10. CLEAN ALL SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT FREE CLOTH. 11. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 12. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY PART BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35.",,True
