PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHA150-B Aging Chamber Assembly.pdf,p1,4,"### Drawing list | ITEM | QTY | DRAWING NUMBER | DESCRIPTION | |---|---|---|---| | 1 | 1 | 60089MFHA151 | SAME AGING CHAMBER | | 2 | 1 | 60089MFHA156 | CHAMBER FAN ASSEMBLY | | 3 | 1 | 60089MFHA170 | INLET ELBOW/ LED BOARD ASSEMBLY | | 4 | 1 | 60089MFHA200 | INLET GATE VALVE ASSEMBLY | | 5 | 1 | 60089MFHA240 | OUTLET GATE VALVE ASSEMBLY | | 6 | 1 | 60089MFHD152 | AGING CHAMBER PISTON | | 7 | 1 | 60089MFHD153 | AGING CHAMBER TOP FLANGE GASKET | | 8 | 1 | 60089MFHD154 | AGING CHAMBER TOP PLATE | | 9 | 4 | 60089MFHD155 | AGING CHAMBER PORT FLANGE GASKET | | 10 | 1 | 60089MFHG175 | CHAMBER OUTLET ELBOW | ### Callouts on the views - Isometric: C3, 6 ""(TWO SEALS ON PISTON)""; ""THIS VIEW SHOWN WITH TOP PLATE REMOVED"" - C9, C10, C24: TORQUE TO 30-35 IN.-LBS. (12 PLACES) - C10, C5 (12 PLACES) - C8, C11, C1: TORQUE TO 20-25 IN.-LBS. (12 PLACES), flag 4 - C11, C5 (12 PLACES) - C8, C11, C24: TORQUE TO 15-17 IN.-LBS. (12 PLACES) - C7, C1: TORQUE TO 58 ±2 IN.-OZ (4 PLACES), flag 4 - C19, C23 (2 PLACES); flag 5 with C2, C12; C4, C2; C2, C22; flag 8 with C17; flags 7, 9 with C25, C14 (2 PLACES); item 9 (4 PLACES) - Items 1 (chamber), 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10 indicated on views; flag 6 near the side elevation",,True
PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,p1,0,"Description: E-size part drawing (sheet drawn rotated 90 degrees on the page) of the SAME smoke generation tube: a long machined aluminium tube with two square mounting collars, a stepped end (datum A), a side port boss with a 4-hole square flange and slot, and a slotted wall zone near the other end. Three elevation views, an end view, Section A-A and Section B-B (scale 2/1), plus an isometric view. ### Title block - Title: SMOKE GENERATION TUBE; next assembly: SMOKE GENERATION TUBE ASSEMBLY 60089MFHA125 - Drawing number: 60089MFHD126, size E, rev B - Organisation: National Aeronautics and Space Administration, John H. Glenn Research Center, Lewis Field, Cleveland, Ohio; ZIN Technologies - Project lead, quality, engineer, designer, reviewer: [name omitted], dated 02/13/06; safety: N/A - Contract number: NAS3-99154; delivery order: MRDOC-074; file location: M:\MRDOC\60089_074; CAD package: Pro/E Wildfire - Scale 1/1; initial release date 02/13/06; sheet 1 of 1; bldg ZIN; area GRC; units: inch; discipline: mechanical - ""This drawing is under configuration control: do not revise without approved ECO"". Approved: [name omitted], date 06/13/06 ### Revisions | CHG | ZONE | DESCRIPTION | APP/DATE | |---|---|---|---| | A | | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-157 | [name omitted] 5/30/06, 5/31/06 | | B | - | INCORPORATED SAME-ECO-160. | [name omitted] 06/13/06 |",,True
PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,p1,1,"### Tolerances (unless otherwise specified, dimensions in inches) .X ± 0.03; .XX ± 0.01; .XXX ± 0.005; FRACTION ± -; ANGULAR ± 0.50°; BREAK EDGES .01-.03. Dimensioning and tolerancing per ASME Y14.5M-1994.",,True
PSI-102,Engineering Documents,PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Engineering Documents/PSI-102_Engineering Documents_60089MFHD126-B Smoke Generation Tube.pdf,p1,2,"### Notes 1. MATERIAL: ALUMINUM 6061-T6 OR 6061-T651 PER AMS-QQ-A-225/8. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 2. 125 Ra ALL MACHINED SURFACES UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED PER ANSI/ASME B46.1. 3. (flag) THE 36 DEGREE TOOL ANGLE SHOWN IN SECTION B-B DESCRIBES THE ANGLE OF THE TOOLING NEEDED TO MACHINE THE .360 DIAMETER x .827 LONG SLOT. 4. (flag) GRIT BLAST INTERIOR SURFACE IN ZONE INDICATED TO UNIFORM MATTE FINISH. 5. SURFACE TREAT PER MIL-C-5541 USING IRIDITE 14-2 OR APPROVED EQUIVALENT PER MIL-DTL-81706, CLASS 3, FORM II METHOD B OR C AS APPLICABLE. SPOT TOUCH UP BY METHOD B. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 6. (flag) PRIOR TO ANODIZING, MASK ALL THREADED HOLES AND EXTERIOR SURFACES INDICATED. MASK OFF INTERIOR SURFACE OF THE TUBE EXCEPT THE ZONE AREA SHOWN IN SECTION VIEW B-B. BLACK ANDODIZE PER MIL-A-8625, TYPE II, CLASS 2. CERTIFICATE OF CONFORMANCE REQUIRED. 7. CLEAN SURFACES WITH ISOPROPYL OR ETHYL ALCOHOL AND LET AIR DRY. WIPE WITH CLEAN COTTON SWABS AND/OR LINT-FREE CLOTH. 8. HANDLE WITH CLEAN LINT FREE GLOVES. 9. BEFORE STORAGE, PROTECT WITH CONTAMINATION BARRIER. USE CLEAN, NEW, TRANSPARENT POLYETHYLENE BAG FOR SMALL ITEMS, OR 4 MIL THICK MINIMUM POLYETHYLENE SHEET AND SEAL. IDENTIFY BY TAGGING WITH PART NUMBER AND SERIAL/LOT NUMBER AS SPECIFIED IN WORK ORDER, PER SAE AS478, METHOD 35. 10. ESTIMATED WEIGHT= 1.730 Lb.",,True
