PSI-102,Science Documents,PSI-102_Science Documents_SAME_Operations Manual_007.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Science Documents/PSI-102_Science Documents_SAME_Operations Manual_007.pdf,p31,0,"SAME-DOC-007 26 Possible operations involving the P-Trak LCD: Turn on and cycle through menu choices Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 1 Off Power On 2 Countdown from 60 to 0 After 0, goes to next display 3 Real-time measurement – Sample menu item chosen Up 4 Real-time measurement – Log Mode 1 menu item chosen Right 5 Real-time measurement – Log Mode 2 menu item chosen Right 6 Real-time measurement – Log Mode 3 menu item chosen Up not shown Real-time measurement – Setup menu item chosen Enter 7 Setup menu Up or Down to change selection, Enter to enter the selection. Enter after selecting EXIT returns to 3. View single point statistics Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Enter 8 Statistics menu Enter 9 or 10 Single point statistics Enter 7 Setup menu View logged test statistics Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Enter 8 Statistics menu Down, Enter 11 or 12 Logged test statistics Enter 7 Setup menu View the log interval Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down, Enter 13,14,15,16, or 17 Current log interval Enter 7 Setup menu",,False
PSI-102,Science Documents,PSI-102_Science Documents_SAME_Operations Manual_007.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-102/Science Documents/PSI-102_Science Documents_SAME_Operations Manual_007.pdf,p32,0,"SAME-DOC-007 27 Change the log interval Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down, Enter 13,14,15,16, or 17 Current log interval Up or Down 13,14,15,16, or 17 New log interval Enter 7 Setup menu View or change the audio output options Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down (2X), Enter 18 and 19 Audio output menu Up, Down, Left, or Right. Select Exit and press Enter to return to 7. View or change the time and date Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down (3X), Enter 20 Time/Date display Up, Down, Left, or Right to change values. Press Enter to return to 7. View or change the backlight settings Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down (4X), Enter 21,22,23, or 24 Current backlight setting Up or Down. Enter to accept new setting. 7 Setup menu Clear single point memory Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down (5X), Enter 25 Clear memory menu Enter 26 Single point memory cleared message Enter 25 Clear memory menu Down (2X), Enter 7 Setup menu Clear logged test memory Display # Description Next Button Press or Reaction 7 Setup menu Down (5X), Enter 25 Clear memory menu Down, Enter 27 Logged test memory cleared message Enter 25 Clear memory menu Down, Enter 7 Setup menu",,False
