PSI-107,Reports,PSI-107_Reports_SPICE_FinalReport.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Reports/PSI-107_Reports_SPICE_FinalReport.pdf,p4,0,"iv List of Tables Table 1. Summary of smoke points observed. List of figures Figure 1. Soot path lines through buoyant and non-buoyant flames Figure 2. Schematic of SPICE experiment apparatus and its connection with SMG. The upper- right portion separated by dash lines are the SPICE apparatus. Figure 3. A photo of the SPICE apparatus. Air flows from left to right. Figure 4. This photo shows three nozzles and six igniters are stored in the storage case for being uploaded to the ISS. Figure 5. A sketch of the fuel supply system including a fuel bottle, a pressure regulator and a mass flow controller. Figure 6. The photo on the left shows six fuel bottle assemblies in the storage case and the photo on the right shows a single fuel bottle assembly including a diaphragm valve and a quick connect. The green label on the bottle describes the fuel type and pressure. Figure 7. A side view of the SPICE apparatus shows a red quick connect to the fuel bottle assemblies. Figure 8. A front view of SPICE apparatus inside of the MSG and positions of the still camera and the video camera. Note that because of limited space, the video camera views the flame through a 45 o angled mirror. Figure 9. The still camera, Nikon D100, that views the flame from the top window. Figure 10. The video camera and the mounting structure with a reflecting mirror on it. Figure 11. The control box to control air and fuel flow rates and ignition, etc.",,False
