PSI-107,Presentations,PSI-107_Presentations_IP-C Crew training 2010.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Presentations/PSI-107_Presentations_IP-C Crew training 2010.pdf,p26,0,"Major Unique Hazard Controls • After every 2 burns the MSG Work Volume must be purged for 3 minutes to promote air mixing to dilute any HF concentration byproduct produced during combustion. – MSG Glove Port open – MSG Air Cir ON • Each Gas Bottle Assembly must have a tie wrap valve restraint in place before stowing. • Prior to crew access into MSG, the Gas Bottle Assembly valve must be closed. • When the MSG Work Volume is open and a Gas Bottle Assembly is present, MSG Air Cir must be ON. • The inside of the Experiment Assembly must be permitted to cool to a temp below 49°C before crew access is permitted. – Wait time for SLICE is 1 minute (covered by 3 minute purge) – Wait time for BASS thin and candle samples is 2 minutes (covered by 3 minute purge) – Wait time for BASS sphere and thick samples is 9 minutes 26",,False
