PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p62,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 May 2008 58 ATTACHMENT 2 NASA JSC Payload Safety Review Panel Smoke Point in Co-flow Experiment Phase II Flight Safety Review Summary of Action Items January 27, 2005 AI Action Date Due 1 Assigned to: GRC/D. Truong HR: SPICE-U4 Determine if the Station-supplied fuel stowage location complies with the SPICE flammability assessment restrictions. Date: Phase III Mandatory Reviewer(s): PSRP Original Signed by: ________________________ January 27, 2005 JSC/NA3/S. Wolf Date PSRP Chairman Original Signed by: ________________________ January 27, 2005 GRC/D. Truong Date Payload Organization",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p63,0,SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 May 2008 59 Response to the agreement from the SPICE Phase II safety review Agreement: The PO agreed to provide a logic diagram depicting all of the inhibits that prevent fuel ignition at Phase III. Two diagrams are attached to SPICE unique hazard SPICE-U8 that show all of the ignition inhibits that prevent fuel ignition. Response to Action Item from the SPICE Phase II safety review Action Item: Determine if the Station-supplied fuel stowage location complies with the SPICE flammability assessment restrictions.,,False
