PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p68,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 64 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 1. Structural Failure (payloads must comply with the listed requirements for all phases of flight) Note: Locker and Soft Stowage items only. Designed to meet the standard modular locker stowage requirements of NSTS 21000-IDD-MDK or equivalent IDD _____. 1a.1 ZIN Tech Engineering will review pre-launch stowage list and re-stow procedure to confirm that SPICE experiment and associated hardware complies with NSTS 2100-IDD- MDK and ISS-MPLM-IDD-006 for launch and landing. Status – Closed to VTL. 2. Structural Failure of Sealed Containers Note 1: Only sealed containers made of conventional metal (metal alloy) can use the 1230 form. Sealed containers made of unconventional metals or non-metallic materials shall be documented on Unique Hazard Reports. Note 2: The 1230 form is not applicable for “sealed container”(s) employed in levels of containment control of hazardous fluid.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p68,1,"Sealed containers must meet the criteria of NASA- STD-5003, Para. 4.2.2.4.2.3a, contain a substance which is not a hazard if released, be made of conventional metals (e.g. Al, inconel, monel, steel or titanium), contain less than 14,240 foot-pounds (19,130 Joules) of stored energy due to pressure, and have a maximum delta pressure of 1.5 atm. N/A- SPICE Gas Bottle Assemblies and pressurized section of the Experiment Assembly contain hazardous materials and are documented under Unique Hazard Reports SPICE- U1 for Contamination Hazard and SPICE-U2 for Rupture/Leak hazard of the Pressurized Fuel Delivery System. All other containers are vented. APPROVAL PAYLOAD ORGANIZATION SSP/ISS PHASE I PHASE II PHASE III",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p69,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 65 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 3. Structural Failure of Vented Containers For intentionally vented containers, vents are sized to maintain a 1.4 factor of safety for Shuttle or a 1.5 factor of safety for Station with respect to pressure loads. Meets all of the applicable pressure rates defined for one or more of the following. a) Shuttle payload bay – ICD 2-19001, Para. 10.6.1 b) Station environment – SSP 52005, paragraph 4.3 or equivalent payload specific ICD ____. c) Station PFE discharge – SSP 57000, Para. 3.1.1.4K, or equivalent payload specific ICD _____. d) Shuttle Middeck – NSTS 21000-IDD-MDK, Section 6.1. 3b.1 Analysis. ZIN Engineering will perform an analysis to verify that the SPICE vented containers will maintain structural integrity in the event of rapid depressurization/repressurization with a factor of safety of 1.5 per SSP 52005. Status - Closed to VTL. See Vented Container Table (table B-1). 4. Sharp Edges, Corners, and/or Protrusions. Meets the intent of one or more of the following: a) NASA-STD-3000 / SSP 50005 b) SLP 2104",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p69,1,"c) NSTS 07700 Vol. XIV App. 7 (EVA hardware) d) NSTS 07700 Vol. XIV App. 9 (IVA hardware) / SSP 57000 e) SSP 41163, Para. 3.3.6.12.3 (EVA), Para. 3.3.6.12.4 (IVA). 4a.1 Analysis . ZIN Tech Engineering will conduct drawing review to ensure the requirements to remove sharp edges, corners, and protrusions have been met and prepare a report confirming design requirements. Status – Closed 12/10/03. 60054-ANA-021. Sharp Edge Analysis 4a.2 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will perform a sharp edge inspection of the SPICE hardware and record results in an inspection report. Status – Closed to VTL.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p70,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 66 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 5. Shatterable Material Release a) All materials are contained. b) Optical glass (i.e. lenses, filters, etc.) components of crew cabin experiment hardware that are non- stressed (no delta pressure) and have passed both a vibration test at flight levels and a post-test visual inspection. c) Payload bay hardware shatterable material components that weigh less than 0.25 lb and are non-stressed (no delta pressure) or non-structural. 5a.1 Analysis. ZIN Tech Engineering will ensure that SPICE design provides for containment of all shatterable materials (see list below) and prepare a report confirming design requirements have been met. Status – Closed 08/07/03. 60054-ANA-026, Containment of Shatterable Materials Analysis. 5a.2 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will verify that the as-built flight hardware conforms to the approved drawings and record results in an inspection report. Status – Closed 03/01/07. SPICE-INS-020-R1, As-Built Inspection Report",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p70,1,"5a.3 Inspection. ZIN Tech Engineering will review crew procedure inputs to ensure that checks of containment and assessment of status prior to utilizing frangible hardware are included, and prepare a report confirming inclusion in the crew procedure inputs. Status - Closed to VTL. 5b.1 Test. ZIN Tech Engineering will arrange for SPICE flight hardware to undergo acceptance vibration testing and prepare a test report confirming test was successfully completed and passed inspection for no breakage. Note even though this control is for Optics, the flow straightener has been tested, see list of all items in table B-2. Status - Closed to 02/07/07. SPICE-TST-007-R1. Stowed Vibration Test Report See shatterable materials table, table B-2. 6. Flammable Materials a) A-rated materials selected from MAPTIS, or b) Flammability assessment per NSTS 22648 6ab.1 Analysis. ZIN Tech Quality will compile a MIUL that records materials specified in approved design documents, evaluate the materials identified per NSTS 1700.7B / ISS Addendum requirements and current MAPTIS material ratings, and generate MUAs to substantiate usage of all non-A-rated materials. Any required flammability assessment per NSTS 22648 will be included in usage rationale of the MUAs. Status – Closed to VTL. 6ab.2 Analysis. NASA/GRC SMAD reviews the MIUL and MUAs and when approved provides a material certification memorandum in accordance with intercenter agreements. Status - Closed to VTL.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p70,2,"7. Materials Offgassing Offgassing tests of assembled article per NASA- STD-6001 (previously published as NHB 8060.1C). 7a.1 Test . ZIN Tech Engineering will arrange offgas testing in accordance with NASA- STD-6001, Test 7 and prepares a report. Status – Closed 2/09/07. SPICE-RPT-001. Toxic Off-gas Test Report 7a.2 Analysis. NASA/GRC SMAD reviews offgas test report and when approved provides material certification memorandum in accordance with intercenter agreements. Status – Closed to VTL.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p71,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 67 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 8. Nonionizing Radiation 8.1 Non-transmitters Meets all that apply: a) Pass ICD-2-19001, 10.7.3.2.2 / SSP 30238 EMI compatibility testing, or b) NSTS/USA approved analysis ICD Section 20, or c) ISS/EMEP approved TIA d) Meets SSP 41163, Para. 3.3.6.6 and SSP 50094, Para. 3.4. 8.1.a.1 Test. ZIN Tech Engineering performs EMI/EMC test per SSP 30238 using the requirement of MSFC-REQ-2888 and prepares a report confirming requirements have been met. Status – Closed 09/30/03. GRC-EMI-RPT-201 8.1c.1 Analysis. NASA ISS/EMEP will review and approve a TIA based on EMI test results. Waivers and deviations have been submitted and a TIA has been requested. Status – Closed to VTL. The power box and the video titler (together know as the power/video unit), the two cameras, the control box and the experiment assembly are all powered and were tested for EMI emissions. 8.2 Lasers",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p71,1,"NOTE: Lasers operating at class levels 3b and 4, meeting ANSI Z136.1, shall be documented on Unique Hazard Reports. Meet ANSI Z136.1-2000 for class 1, 2, or 3a Lasers (as measured at the source). N/A- No Lasers. 9. Battery Failure a) 9.1 Alkaline cells and batteries made of alkaline cells, connected in series or in parallel, up to 12 V and with up to 60 Watt-hours capacity, no potential charging source and cells are not in a gas-tight compartment. Cells and batteries pass acceptance tests that include loaded and open circuit voltage measurements, visual examination, and leakage check under vacuum (e.g. 6 hours at 0.1 psia). N/A Submission of EP-Form-03(including the form’s approved reference number) for EP5 approval Information to be included on the EP5 reviewed/approved Form-03: application and protective circuit schematics",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p72,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 68 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 9.2 Primary button cells such as Li-(CF)x, Li-iodine, LiV2O5, LiMnO2, Ag-Zn and rechargeable button cells such as LiV2O5, Li-ion, Ni- Cd, Ni-MH, Ag-Zn cells or batteries, which have a capacity of 300 mAh or less and no more than 3 cells per common circuit, and cells are not in a gas-tight compartment. Cells and batteries pass acceptance tests that include loaded and open circuit voltage measurements, visual examination, and leakage check under vacuum (e.g. 6 hours at 0.1 psia). Note: Above acceptance testing for button cells in Section 9.2 which are soldered to a circuit board in commercial equipment (not applicable to those button cells in a spring-loaded clip) is limited to a functional check of the equipment utilizing the subject battery. 9.2.a.1 Test. Since all batteries are soldered to the boards, ZIN Tech Engineering will conduct an acceptance functional test on each item and prepare reports confirming requirements have been met. Status – Closed to VTL.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p72,1,"NIKON D100 Digital Camera Button Cell 20mmX3.2mm, type Li-Mn-O2, 3 Volts DC 65mAh, Maxell Model No.: ML2032T6. (This battery will be removed before flight.) Dallas I-Button data device Cell, 12.5mm X 2.5mm, type Li-CFx, 3 Volt DC, 50mAh, Model No. BR1225, Manufacturer: RAYOVAC. The Horita Video Titler card contains two cells in series. The cells are 15.5 X6.3 mm Rechargeable Nickle Metal Hydride cells, 1.2 VDC each, 60mAh, Model Number GP60BNK, Manufacturer GP Batteries International LTD EP-Form-03 submitted for each battery. As submitted forms attached. Submission of EP-Form-03(including the form’s approved reference number) for EP5 approval Information to be included on the EP5 reviewed/approved Form-03: application and protective circuitry. 9.3 COTS NiMH, NiCd and Ag/Zn cells and batteries for IVA use up to 20 V and 60 Wh Cells and batteries purchased in one lot; pass acceptance tests that include loaded and open circuit voltage measurements, visual examination, leakage check under vacuum (e.g 6 hours at 0.1psia) and vibration to workmanship levels with functional checks which include charge/discharge cycles for rechargeable batteries. N/A Submission of EP5 Form-03(including the form’s approved reference number) for approval Information to be included on the EP5 reviewed/approved Form-03: manufacturer’s specification, battery protective features and charger schematics",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p72,2,"9.4 COTS Li-ion batteries up to 10 V and 60 Wh for IVA use Batteries and charger shall be from a single lot; shall show one-fault tolerance at battery level and shall pass acceptance tests that include loaded and open circuit voltage measurements, visual examination, leakage check under vacuum (e.g 6 hours at 0.1psia) and vibration to environment or double the workmanship level, whichever is higher; and functional checks which include charge/discharge cycles. .N/A",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p73,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 69 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 10. Touch Temperature a) Within IVA touch temperature range of –18 Degrees C. (0 Degrees F.) and 49 Degrees C. (120 Degrees F.) and satisfies the intentional contact constraints of letter MA2-95-048 (if applicable). b) Meets EVA touch temperature criteria of NSTS 07700 Vol. XIV App. 7. See unique HR SPICE-U6 11. Electrical Power Distribution a) Shuttle-powered payloads – Meets all circuit protection requirements of Letter TA-92-038. b) Station-powered payloads – Meets station interface circuit protection requirements of SSP 57000 and payload circuit protection requirements of Letter TA-92-038. 11b.1 Analysis . ZIN Tech Engineering will perform an analysis of the SPICE design to verify proper wire sizing for circuit protection provided by MSG and prepare a report confirming design requirements have been met. Status – Closed 6/3/03. Report 60054-ANA-017, SPICE Wire Derating Analysis demonstrates that wire size is adequate for the fusing.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p73,1,"11b.2 Analysis . ZIN Tech Engineering will perform an analysis to verify that the SPICE design incorporates proper circuit protective devices in accordance with SSP 57000 and TA-92-038 and prepare a report confirming design requirements have been met. Status – Closed 6/3/03. 60054-ANA-017, SPICE Wire Derating Analysis 11b.3 Analysis. JSC/EP5 review and approval of integrated schematic indicating bonding and grounding methodology for compliance with SSP 30245 and SSP 30240. Status – Closed 6/3/03 Schematic is provided as an attachment to the 1230 Form. 60054- ANA-015, Grounding & Cable Analysis. SPICE-TST-016-R1, As-Run Grounding Test Report. See SPICE-NCR-003 and SPICE-DEV-001. 11b.4 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will verify that the as-built electrical circuitry is in accordance with approved drawings and parts lists and record results in an inspection report. Status – Closed 3/01/07. SPICE-INS-027-R1, As-Built Electrical Circuitry Inspection Report Note: See attached figures on the electrical system: B-3, B-4 and B-5. 12. Ignition of Flammable Atmospheres in Payload Bay All ignition sources in the Payload bay, for launch and landing, are controlled as required in Letter NS2/81-MO82, and MLI grounded per ICD 2- 19001. N/A- SPICE will not be transported to ISS in Payload Bay.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p74,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 70 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 13. Rotating Equipment Rotating equipment meets criteria of NASA-STD- 5003 for obvious containment. 13.1 Analysis . ZIN Tech Engineering will review SPICE design to ensure that the rotating component which is the 3 inch, 2950 rpm Fan located in the Experiment Assembly meets the criteria of NASA-STD-5003 for containment and prepare a report confirming design requirements have been met. Status – Closed 8/1/03. 60054-ANA-028, Rotating Components Compliance Analysis. 14. Mating/demating powered connectors a) Meets the low power criteria of letter MA2-99-170 or, b) Meets the paragraph 1 criteria of letter MA2-99-170 (e.g., IVA and open circuit voltage no greater than 32 volts).",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p74,1,"14b.1 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will Inspect Crew Procedure inputs to ensure that step is in place to remove power from the MSG experiment power connector prior to mate/demate of connectors. Status – Closed to VTL. 14b.2 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will Inspect electrical connectors to comply with MSFC-RQMT-2888 connection requirements for 28 volt connections. Status – Closed 2/13/07. SPICE-INS-011-R1, Electrical Connectors and Pin Assignment Inspection Report. 14b.3 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will Inspect the SPICE hardware for design features that completely enclose or shroud the pins and sockets. Status – Closed 4/19/07. SPICE-INS-003 Connector Protection and Shape Design Inspection. 14b.4 Inspection. ZIN Tech Quality will Inspect the SPICE connectors for powered side terminating in sockets rather than pins. Status – Closed to 4/19/07. SPICE-INS-003 Connector Protection and Shape Design Inspection. 15. Contingency Return and Rapid Safing Shuttle Environment: a) If middeck payload – can be stowed within 50 min. (see paragraph 3 of letter MA2-96-190). b) If SPACEHAB transfer item – can establish a safe for return configuration within 3 min. (see paragraph 5 of letter MA2-96-190). Station Environment: c) Payload design does not impede emergency IVA egress to the remaining adjacent pressurized volumes.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p74,2,"15a.1 Analysis. ZIN Tech Engineering will perform an analysis to show that hardware can be stowed in allowed time. Status – Closed 12/10/03. 60054-ANA-030, ISS Emergency Egress Compliance Analysis 15c.1 Analysis. ZIN Tech Engineering will perform design analysis of SPICE hardware to show the design does not impede emergency IVA egress to adjacent pressurized volumes and prepare a report confirming design requirements have been met. Status – Closed 12/10/03. 60054-ANA-030, ISS Emergency Egress Compliance Analysis",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p75,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 71 A. NUMBER B. PHASE C. DATE FLIGHT PAYLOAD STANDARDIZED HAZARD CONTROL REPORT STD- SPICE-01 III May 2008 D. PAYLOAD, DTO, DSO or RME (Include Part Number(s), if applicable) HAZARD TITLE E. VEHICLE Smoke Points In Co-flow Experiment (SPICE) STANDARD HAZARDS STS/ISS F. DESCRIPTION OF HAZARD: G. HAZARD CONTROLS: (complies with) H. APP. I. VERIFICATION METHOD, REFERENCE, AND STATUS: 16. Release of Mercury from bulbs into crew habitable environment. a) Mercury vapor bulbs contain less than 30 mg of Mercury per bulb, and b) No more than one bulb could break due to a single failure. N/A-There is no mercury in any of the SPICE components.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p76,0,"SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 72 Vented Container Table B-1 (for STD SPICE-01 Description of Hazard 3) Container Housing Material Size Energy contained (ft- lbs) $ Container Volume (in3) No packing factor Vent Size (in2 ) Control Box Aluminum 4.8X2.6X1.4 inches 20 16.8 0.3 Digital Camera Plastic *8X 5X8 370 320 0.32 Video Camera Aluminum * 5.9X2.6X2.1 37 32.3 0.31 Power Control Box Aluminum 8.1X5.7X2.4 inches 128 111 0.86 Video Control Box Aluminum 8.1X5.7X 3 inches 160 139 0.86 Gas Bottle Assembly Cases Aluminum 18.2X14.5X6.2 inches 1891 1636 1.20 Component Parts Case Aluminum 18.2X14.5X6.2 inches 1891 1636 1.20 Experiment Assembly Aluminum and Lexan 13.6X10.4X6.7 1095 947 19.5 Ignitor/Burner case Aluminum 6.1X3.5X1.1 24.9 21.5 0.30 Note none of these contain any chemicals other than air except the Gas Bottle Assembly Cases which will contain the Fuel Bottles which are tox level 0 if they are all released. *The camera is not a box, these are the extreme outside dimensions and includes the lens, they are used for conservatism. @ This is based on depressurization. For the gas bottle assembly case, although any individual bottle if dumped instantly would increase the pressure in the box by 4.4 psi if the box were sealed, this occurring at the same time as a depressurization does not seem credible. $ This is based on the container being sealed and at 14.7 psi differential pressure due to depressurization.",,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p77,0,SPICE PHASE III FLIGHT SAFETY DATA PACKAGE SPICE-SDP-003 73 Shatterable Materials/Components Table B-2 (for STD SPICE-01 Description of Hazard 5) System (or Subsystem) Material name/type Location/use Protection & containment # of levels of containment Rationale for acceptance Video Camera Lens Glass lens In MSG Non stressed lens 1 The glass lens parts are small and not stressed. The camera was tested in vibration in stowage configuration. Item is contained during launch (stowed item) and is in MSG during use. Camera will be packed inside transparent bag and will be examined for glass splinters by the crew before unpacking. Verification shall be done by review and approval of inputs to crew procedures. Still Camera Lens Glass lens In MSG Non stressed lens 1 The glass lens parts are small and not stressed. The camera was tested in vibration in stowage configuration. Item is contained during launch (stowed item) and is in MSG during use. Camera will be packed inside transparent bag and will be examined for glass splinters by the crew before unpacking. Verification shall be done by review and approval of inputs to crew procedures. Flow Straightener Cordierite (ceramic),,False
PSI-107,Engineering Documents,PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-107/Engineering Documents/PSI-107_Engineering Documents_SPICE_Phase III Flight Safety Data Package.pdf,p77,1,"In MSG Non stressed, bound 4 sides, and contained 1 The part is small and not stressed. The EA was tested in vibration in stowage configuration. Item is stowed during launch. Item is contained between 100 mesh screens at all times. The item is 1 inch thick honey comb which is bound on 4 sides (3 inch sides) exposing only the ends of the square tubes formed by the ceramic.",,False
