PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,p12,0,"Evolution of maximum temperature and burning rate (do = 4.08 mm, O2/CO2/N2 0.21/0.15/0.64, 3 atm) High temperature ignition- radiative extinction Low temperature reaction-auto-thermal heating High temperature re- initiation-radiative extinction Low temperature combustion Hot Flame ??? Transient !!! Oscillatory Cool Flames – Model Predictions",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,p13,0,"Evolution of droplet diameter (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of peak temperature (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Introduction of helium increases the burning rate, at higher helium concentration a third stage quasi-steady burn is observed 1st Stage High Temperature burn 2nd Stage Moderate Temperature burn Tflame ~ 950 K 3rd Stage Low Temperature burn Tflame ~ 770 K High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,p14,0,"Evolution of droplet diameter (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of peak temperature (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). • The second stage suppresses at a higher helium concentration • The droplet diameter regression does not show any significant changes High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm 2nd Stage Moderate Temperature burn Tflame ~ 950 K 3rd Stage Low Temperature burn Tflame ~ 770 K",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,p15,0,"• A second contraction in the flame occurs as the system transitions to the third stage/low temperature burn. • Despite the decrease in the maximum temperature, it is the flame contraction that makes the droplet diameter regression insensitive to the different burn stages. High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm 3rd 1st Stage 2nd Stage 3rd Stage Evolution of flame standoff ratio (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of burning rate (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm).",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_PSI_Users_Group_Cool_Flames_in_Space_03302026.pdf,p16,0,"• A strong coupling between heat generation and losses in the system. • The radiative and diffusive heat losses are comparable in the first and second stages. • The diffusive losses become prominent in the third stage, “Cool flame” burn. High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm Evolution of radiative loss (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of diffusive loss (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm).",,False
