PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p2,0,"2 “Cool” Flames Triggered By Radiative Losses First observation of “Cool Flames” in n-heptane droplet diffusion flames International Space Station 2011, Flame Extinguishment Experiments (FLEX) Evolution of droplet diameter and burning rate (n- heptane, do = 4.00 mm, air, atmospheric pressure) V. Nayagam et al. Combustion and Flame (2012), 159, 3583 – 3588. T. Farouk and F. L. Dryer Combustion and Flame (2014), 161, 565 – 581 “Cool Flame” First Stage Second Stage Hot Flame",,False
