PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p6,0,"6 Transient Droplet Combustion Model*+ * T. Farouk and F. L. Dryer Combust. and Flame (2012) 159, 200 – 209 + T. Farouk and F. L. Dryer Combust Theory & Modelling (2011), 15, 487 – 515 Liquid Phase: • Mass conservation • Species equation • Energy conservation Gas Phase: • Multi-component molecular diffusion • Detailed chemical kinetics - high and low temperature • Mass conservation • Species equation • Energy conservation Statistical Narrowband Radiation Model mv T r ∂λ ∂ qR mpsdr dt l T r ∂λ ∂ , , li li YD r ∂ ∂ Droplet Surface: • Surface regression – Adaptive Grid • Evaporation of fuel • Condensation/Dissolution of products • Radiative heat exchange Fiber Model: One dimensional temperature distribution Energy exchange with flame and ambient fibq ambientq lossq The code numeric and data handling methodology has been revised to relax number of species constraints",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p7,0,"7 High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm Evolution of droplet diameter (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of peak temperature (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Introduction of helium increases the burning rate, at higher helium concentration a third stage quasi-steady burn is observed 1st Stage High Temperature burn 2nd Stage Moderate Temperature burn Tflame ~ 950 K 3rd Stage Low Temperature burn Tflame ~ 770 K",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p8,0,"8 High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm Evolution of droplet diameter (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of peak temperature (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). • The second stage suppresses at higher helium concentration • The droplet diameter regression do not show any significant changes 2nd Stage Moderate Temperature burn Tflame ~ 950 K 3rd Stage Low Temperature burn Tflame ~ 770 K",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p9,0,"9 High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm Evolution of burning rate (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). 3rd • A second contraction in the flame occurs as the system transitions to the third stage/low temperature burn. • Despite the decrease in the maximum temperature it is the flame contraction that makes the droplet diameter regression insensitive to the different burn stages. Evolution of flame standoff ratio (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). 1st Stage 2nd Stage 3rd Stage",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p10,0,"10 High Pressure Helium Exchange – 3 atm Evolution of radiative loss (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). Evolution of diffusive loss (n-heptane, do = 4.00 mm, XO2 = 21%, He exchange with balance N2, 3 atm). • A strong coupling between heat generation and losses in the system. • The radiative and diffusive heat losses are comparable in the first and second stage. • The diffusive losses become prominent in the third stage “Cool flame” burn.",,False
