PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p14,0,"14 Species Distribution – 3 atm, XHe = 40% • Species representative of low temperature kinetics is in prominence in the third stage • Competition between O2 addition to QOOH and decomposition of QOOH (i.e. OH, HO 2, olefin, carbonyl, QO)",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p15,0,"15 Experimental Observation of 3 Stage Behavior FLEX 1268: n-dodecane, 2.75 atm, 21.6% O2, 50.2% N2, 28.2% He. Qualitative agreement between predictions and observations",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p16,0,"16 Experimental Observation of 3 Stage Behavior FLEX 1268: n-dodecane, 2.75 atm, 21.6% O2, 50.2% N2, 28.2% He. Qualitative agreement between predictions and observations Atef et al. Combustion and Flame (2017)",,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p17,0,17 Summary • The experimental results and detailed predictions support that there exists two possible modes of quasi-steady cool flame droplet burning behaviour: “Warm” in the NTC regime and “Cold” in the low temperature regime. • The helium concentration is critical for the observed characteristics – promoting the second stage burn or completely supressing it. • A dynamic coupling between heat generation and heat loss in the system. • The low temperature kinetics is distinctive and different in the second and third stage. • Experimental observation with n-dodecane at higher pressure and helium exchange validates the “a priori” numerical predictions of a three stage behaviour inferred from n-heptane simulations.,,False
PSI-117,Presentations,PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-117/Presentations/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf,p18,0,"18 Acknowledgements • This work was supported by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration through grants NNX14AG461A (TIF), NNX09AW 19A (FLD) . • Thanks to Drs. Michael Hicks, Forman Williams and Vedha Nayagam for interest and insight throughout the course of this investigation.",,False
