PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p100,2,"which is pulled out and rotated iss066e029031 2021-11-02 Shane Kimbrough (NASA) at the CIR, where the combustion chamber is closed iss066e031702 2021-11-02 Shane Kimbrough (NASA) with the ACME insert held outside of the open CIR chamber iss066e095422 2021-12-21 Raja Chari (NASA) at the CIR to replace gas bottle(s) iss066e114301 2022-01-17 Raja Chari (NASA) with the ACME insert partially withdrawn from the open CIR chamber iss066e114415 2022-01-17 Raja Chari (NASA) with the ACME chamber insert partially withdrawn from the CIR, of which only the hatch can be seen 7. Internet Links These websites may be useful for understanding ACME’s engineering implementation and interpreting the experimental results. ACME Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments CIR Combustion Integrated Rack (ISS facility in which the ACME experiments were conducted)",,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p101,0,"ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 101 Short videos clips providing overviews of the ACME chamber insert and research can be seen and downloaded. Meanwhile, a time-lapse video clip showing astronaut Paolo Nespoli (ESA) reconfiguring the CIR’s optics bench for initial ACME testing can be seen and downloaded. As mentioned in the previous section, photographs of the hardware and more can be seen at: www.flickr.com/photos/space-flames www.facebook.com/space.flames These Space Flames websites are about space-based studies of combustion in general, but they are administered by Dennis Stocker, the ACME Project Scientist, and are an excellent source of photos of the ACME hardware and crew operations. 8.",,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p101,1,"Nomenclature ACME Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments (project conducted in the CIR) ADP Acceptance Data Package AVP avionics package BRE Burning Rate Emulator (an ACME experiment) CASIS Center for the Advancement of Science in Space CCD Charge-Coupled Device (such as a camera sensor) CIA Chamber Insert Assembly (inserted into the CIR combustion chamber) CIR Combustion Integrated Rack (ISS facility in which ACME experiments are conducted) CFI Cool Flames Investigation (an MDCA experiment preceding ACME in the CIR) CFI-G Cool Flames Investigation with Gases (an ACME experiment selected by CASIS and NSF) CLD Flame Coflow Laminar Diffusion Flame (an ACME experiments) CM Combustion Module (space shuttle precursor to the CIR) CSA Canadian Space Agency CSV comma-separated values DataCam Data Camera (developed for the ACME experiments, characterized for pyrometry, etc.) E-FIELD Flames Electric-Field Effects on Laminar Diffusion Flames (an ACME experiment) EMI electromagnetic interference EMS Experiment Mounting Structure ERD Engineering Requirements Document ESA European Space Agency Fiji Fiji Is Just ImageJ (a version of ImageJ preloaded with many plug-in features) Flame Design Flame Design (an ACME experiment) FOMA Fuel and Oxidizer Management Assembly (CIR’s gas management subsystem) FOV field of view fps frames per second GCIP Gas Chromatograph Instrumentation Package (a CIR subsystem) GIPOC Glenn ISS Payload Operations Center (also known as the TSC) GMT Greenwich",,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p101,2,Mean Time HiBMs High Bit-depth Multi-spectral camera (developed for the CIR facility) HOBJ Halcon object (binary uncompressed format; used for the DataCam) HV high voltage ImageJ Image Processing and Analysis in Java (open-source image processing software) IPSU Image Processing and Storage Unit (a CIR subsystem) IPSU-G IPSU for Gigabit ethernet cameras,,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p102,0,ACME Engineering Implementation 19 May 2022 102,,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p102,1,"ISRD Integrated Science Requirements Document (for a set of experiments) ISS International Space Station JAXA Japanese Aerospace Exploration Agency LLL-UV Low Light Level Ultraviolet camera ((developed for the CIR facility) LSP Laminar Soot Processes (a shuttle experiment conducted in the Combustion Module) MDCA Multi-user Droplet Combustion Apparatus (CIR chamber insert preceding ACME) MFC mass flow controller Mist Water-Mist Fire Suppression Experiment (a Combustion Module experiment) MIUL Materials Identification/Usage List MSG Microgravity Science Glovebox NSF National Science Foundation NTSC National Television System Committee OMA2 Optical Multi-channel Analyzer 2 (open-source software for image processing and display) ops operations PaRIS Passive Rack Isolation System PIMS Principal Investigator Microgravity Services PMT Photomultiplier Tube (where ACME is equipped with three PMT modules) PSI Physical Sciences Informatics System PT pressure transducer psia pounds per square inch QD quick disconnect qty quantity RSA Russian Space Agency (i.e., Roscosmos) s-Flame Structure and Response of Spherical Diffusion Flames (an ACME experiment) SAMS Space Acceleration Measurement System SDP Safety Data Package slpm standard liters per minute (a measure of the mass or molar flow rate of a gas) SOFBALL Structure Of Flame Balls At Low Lewis-number (a Combustion Module experiment) SoFIE Solid Fuel Ignition and Extinction (project to be conducted in the CIR after ACME) SRD Science",,False
PSI-159,Engineering Documents,PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Engineering Documents/PSI-159_Engineering Documents_ACME Engineering Implementation Rpt..pdf,p102,2,"Requirements Document TFP Thin-Filament Pyrometry (a technique for making gas-phase temperature measurements) TIFF or TIF Tagged Image File Format (used for the CFI intensified, HiBMs, and LLL-UV cameras) TM thermistor TS Transport Stream (a video format) TSC Telescience Support Center (also known as the GIPOC)",,False
