PSI-159,Raw Data,PSI-159_Raw Data_21242 test sheets.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Raw Data/PSI-159_Raw Data_21242 test sheets.pdf,p1,0,"ACME / CFI-G (inverse flame) - Science Test Sheet Test date: Aug. 30, 2021 Local time: 11:32 GMT: 21 242 15:32 ACME test #: 21242A1 Test of day #: 1 Hot flame of day #: 1 sustained Rack Officer (RO): [name omitted] DMO (CIR): [name omitted] PD (ACME): [name omitted] Researcher: [name omitted] TEST CONDITIONS Control?: fully automated Test type?: standard Fuel: C3H8 Fuel conc. % (vol, nominal): ~43 Fuel conc. % (vol, per calc): 42.87 Chamber pressure: 7.3 psia (CIR avg) — note: ""per FCU"" Vent before?: yes, to 0.2 psia Also just before?: not marked O2 bottle: 85% (volume) [printed] Burner O2 conc. % (volume): 85 O2 flow rate: 0.299 slpm (N2 basis) N2 flow rate: 0 slpm [printed ""N2 flow rate"" struck through by hand] — note: ""no N2"" INSTRUMENTATION TFP?: no Gain: 33 DataCam, 31 ops camera DataCam: marked; filter? clear; ROI? full; fps: Intensified: marked; filter? CH2O; ROI? full; fps: 23 HiBMs: [printed ""HiBMs"" underlined/struck by hand]; backlight filter? yes; CIR backlight? no; fps? [printed ""fps? 15"" struck through] — note: ""no HiBMs"" FLAME BEHAVIOR Flame (hot/cool): hot Flame (hole/opening / partially detached): not marked Flame (oscillating / unsteady / quasi-steady): quasi-steady Out: temp. limit [underlined] [time out also marked but its mark and the words ""time out"" are scribbled out] Ignited?: not marked Soot@ignition: lots [mark also in the unlabeled box printed after ""lots""] Soot@middle: lots [mark also in the unlabeled box printed after ""lots""] Soot@end:",,True
PSI-159,Raw Data,PSI-159_Raw Data_21242 test sheets.pdf,data/raw/files/PSI-159/Raw Data/PSI-159_Raw Data_21242 test sheets.pdf,p1,1,"lots [mark also in the unlabeled box printed after ""lots""] POST-TEST CONDITIONS Fuel conc. % (vol, per calc): 42.75 Valve safety timer: 962 [first digit overwritten] sec Chamber pressure: 7.4 psia (CIR avg) — note: ""per FCU"" Oxidizer bottle pressure: 82 psia GENERAL COMMENTS - burner was glowing when the flame extinguished because the burner had exceeded the temperature limit leading to shut-down of the oxidizer flow Form date: 12 July 2021",,True
